1
00:00:04,205 --> 00:00:07,308
♪ IN THE NOT-TOO-DISTANT
FUTURE ♪

2
00:00:07,342 --> 00:00:10,778
♪ NEXT SUNDAY, A.D. ♪

3
00:00:10,812 --> 00:00:13,615
♪ THERE WAS A GUY
NAMED JOEL ♪

4
00:00:13,648 --> 00:00:17,085
♪ NOT TOO DIFFERENT
FROM YOU OR ME ♪

5
00:00:17,118 --> 00:00:19,953
♪ HE WORKED
AT GIZMONIC INSTITUTE ♪

6
00:00:19,987 --> 00:00:23,425
♪ JUST ANOTHER FACE
IN A RED JUMPSUIT ♪

7
00:00:23,458 --> 00:00:25,960
♪ HE DID A GOOD JOB
CLEANING UP THE PLACE ♪

8
00:00:25,993 --> 00:00:27,762
♪ BUT HIS BOSSES
DIDN'T LIKE HIM ♪

9
00:00:27,795 --> 00:00:30,198
♪ SO THEY SHOT HIM
INTO SPACE ♪

10
00:00:32,500 --> 00:00:35,637
♪ WE'LL SEND HIM
CHEESY MOVIES ♪

11
00:00:35,670 --> 00:00:38,840
- ♪ THE WORST WE CAN FIND ♪
- ♪ LA LA LA ♪

12
00:00:38,873 --> 00:00:41,708
♪ HE'LL HAVE TO SIT
AND WATCH THEM ALL ♪

13
00:00:41,743 --> 00:00:44,978
- ♪ AND WE'LL MONITOR HIS MIND ♪
- ♪ LA LA LA ♪

14
00:00:45,012 --> 00:00:48,015
♪ NOW KEEP IN MIND
JOEL CAN'T CONTROL ♪

15
00:00:48,048 --> 00:00:51,185
- ♪ WHERE THE MOVIES
BEGIN OR END ♪
- ♪ LA LA LA ♪

16
00:00:51,218 --> 00:00:54,422
♪ BECAUSE HE USED
THOSE SPECIAL PARTS ♪

17
00:00:54,455 --> 00:00:57,392
♪ TO MAKE HIS ROBOT FRIENDS ♪

18
00:00:59,060 --> 00:01:00,995
LET'S GO.

19
00:01:01,028 --> 00:01:02,297
- CAMBOT.
- PAN LEFT.

20
00:01:02,330 --> 00:01:03,598
HI, GIRL.

21
00:01:03,632 --> 00:01:05,400
WHAT A COOL GUY.

22
00:01:05,433 --> 00:01:06,968
A WISECRACKER.

23
00:01:07,002 --> 00:01:09,970
♪ IF YOU'RE WONDERING HOW
HE EATS AND BREATHES ♪

24
00:01:10,003 --> 00:01:12,807
- ♪ AND OTHER SCIENCE FACTS ♪
- ♪ LA LA LA ♪

25
00:01:12,840 --> 00:01:15,843
♪ THEN REPEAT TO YOURSELF
"IT'S JUST A SHOW ♪

26
00:01:15,877 --> 00:01:19,213
♪ "I SHOULD REALLY
JUST RELAX ♪

27
00:01:19,247 --> 00:01:22,083
♪ FOR..." ♪

28
00:01:34,162 --> 00:01:35,763
AHH.

29
00:01:35,797 --> 00:01:38,800
RICKY, GARY,
GET ME A SCOTCH.

30
00:01:38,833 --> 00:01:40,935
OH LUCY, I WANNA
HAVE CHILDREN.

31
00:01:40,968 --> 00:01:42,337
AAH.

32
00:01:42,370 --> 00:01:44,638
HI EVERYBODY, WELCOME
TO THE SATELLITE OF LOVE.

33
00:01:44,672 --> 00:01:46,473
I'M JOEL ROBINSON,
AND IT LOOKS LIKE

34
00:01:46,507 --> 00:01:48,142
TOM SERVO AND CROW
ARE CAUGHT

35
00:01:48,175 --> 00:01:50,412
IN SOME KIND OF
RIFF-HYPER-OVERDRIVE

36
00:01:50,445 --> 00:01:52,147
WHERE THEY'RE OVERFASCINATED

37
00:01:52,180 --> 00:01:53,848
WITH THE IDEA
OF LUCILLE BALL

38
00:01:53,882 --> 00:01:55,883
FINALLY MEETING UP
WITH HARVEY FIERSTEIN.

39
00:01:55,917 --> 00:01:58,152
- LET'S WATCH.
- AH, MR. MOONEY,

40
00:01:58,185 --> 00:02:00,688
I WANTED TO MEET
ROBERT GOULET.

41
00:02:00,722 --> 00:02:02,557
I KNOW WHAT YOU MEAN,
HARVEY.

42
00:02:02,590 --> 00:02:04,092
LOVE FOR SALE!

43
00:02:04,125 --> 00:02:05,493
SEE WHAT I GOTTA LIVE WITH?

44
00:02:05,527 --> 00:02:07,495
THE ONLY WAY I CAN GET 'EM
TO INTERACT WITH ME

45
00:02:07,528 --> 00:02:09,830
IS TAKE ON THE MANNERISMS
OF A OTHER

46
00:02:09,863 --> 00:02:11,933
RASPY-VOICED CELEBRITY.

47
00:02:11,967 --> 00:02:14,068
UH, SIRS, THIS IS...

48
00:02:14,102 --> 00:02:17,538
BRENDA VACCARO HERE, SIRS.

49
00:02:17,572 --> 00:02:20,742
UH, BURGESS MEREDITH
ON LINE ONE.

50
00:02:20,775 --> 00:02:23,645
AAH, I'M ONLY TAKING CALLS
FROM DAVID JANNSEN.

51
00:02:23,678 --> 00:02:27,548
AAH, BRENDA, DARLING, POSTPONE
MY DINNER WITH KIM CARNES.

52
00:02:27,582 --> 00:02:29,183
SEE WHAT I MEAN?

53
00:02:29,217 --> 00:02:30,618
[MAGIC VOICE, RASPY]
COMMERCIAL SIGN IN FIVE,

54
00:02:30,652 --> 00:02:33,688
FOUR, THREE, TWO,
COMMERCIAL SIGN NOW.

55
00:02:33,722 --> 00:02:35,457
[ALL]
AAH.

56
00:02:42,930 --> 00:02:44,765
I'VE NEVER MET
A REAL MAN, AAH.

57
00:02:44,798 --> 00:02:46,667
GARY, WE NEED MORE CALGON.

58
00:02:46,700 --> 00:02:49,037
HEY, YOU GUYS, HOLD ON.
HEY, HEY, HOLD ON.

59
00:02:49,070 --> 00:02:51,405
GYPSY'S GOT AN IMPRESSION
SHE'S BEEN WORKING REAL HARD ON.

60
00:02:51,438 --> 00:02:53,942
OH, RICKY,
I WANNA BE IN THE SHOW TOO.

61
00:02:53,975 --> 00:02:55,510
COME ON, YOU GUYS.
STOP IT. HEY, CAMBOT.

62
00:02:55,543 --> 00:02:57,912
PUT DOWN THE LIGHTS.
GYPSY, YOU READY? COME ON.

63
00:02:57,945 --> 00:03:00,715
[GYPSY HUMS]

64
00:03:00,748 --> 00:03:03,852
- WHOA.
- AAH.

65
00:03:03,885 --> 00:03:05,387
- UH-HUH.
- DID YOU GUYS GET IT?

66
00:03:05,420 --> 00:03:08,188
SHE'S THE OPENING
TO THE NBC SUNDAY NIGHT
MYSTERY MOVIE.

67
00:03:08,222 --> 00:03:09,590
OH, THE MADS ARE CALLING.

68
00:03:09,623 --> 00:03:11,092
- COOL.
- McCLOUD!

69
00:03:11,125 --> 00:03:13,962
OH, WAY TO GIVE 'EM THE RAZZ,
ROBOT CRITTERS.

70
00:03:13,995 --> 00:03:15,663
LET'S PRESS ON, SHALL WE?

71
00:03:15,697 --> 00:03:17,532
TALL AND PROUD.

72
00:03:17,565 --> 00:03:19,800
OUR INVENTION THIS WEEK
ARE THESE PRINTERS

73
00:03:19,833 --> 00:03:21,768
YOU WEAR ON THE FRONT
OF YOUR PERSON.

74
00:03:21,802 --> 00:03:23,503
AND TINY DIODES
ARE ATTACHED--

75
00:03:23,537 --> 00:03:26,207
TINY, ITCHY DIODES,
YOU MEAN.

76
00:03:26,240 --> 00:03:29,143
TINY DIODES ARE ATTACHED
TO THE HEADBANDS,

77
00:03:29,177 --> 00:03:30,745
AND THEY READ
YOUR CRANIAL CAVITY

78
00:03:30,778 --> 00:03:32,413
AND REPRODUCE
YOUR SELF-IMAGE

79
00:03:32,447 --> 00:03:34,082
ON THESE
READY-TO-WEAR BOARDS

80
00:03:34,115 --> 00:03:36,350
FOR ALL THE WORLD TO SEE.

81
00:03:36,383 --> 00:03:37,918
READY, FRANK?
START THINKING.

82
00:03:37,952 --> 00:03:40,355
I'LL SWITCH ON
YOUR COMPUTER.

83
00:03:40,388 --> 00:03:42,190
NOW, FRANK, TELL OUR VIEWERS

84
00:03:42,223 --> 00:03:44,425
A LITTLE BIT ABOUT YOURSELF.

85
00:03:44,458 --> 00:03:46,060
WELL, WHEN I WAS
IN HIGH SCHOOL,

86
00:03:46,093 --> 00:03:48,597
I WASN'T A FREAK
OR A JOCK OR A BRAIN

87
00:03:48,630 --> 00:03:50,265
OR ANYTHING LIKE THAT.

88
00:03:50,298 --> 00:03:51,832
I WAS BASICALLY
ONE OF THOSE PEOPLE

89
00:03:51,865 --> 00:03:53,367
WHO GOT ALONG
WITH EVERYBODY.

90
00:03:53,400 --> 00:03:54,968
I FIT IN WITH EVERY GROUP.

91
00:03:55,002 --> 00:03:57,572
I'M BASICALLY A GOOD PERSON
WITH SOLID GOALS

92
00:03:57,605 --> 00:03:59,407
AND A STRONG VALUE SYSTEM.

93
00:03:59,440 --> 00:04:01,075
IF I RUN INTO SOMEONE
ON THE STREET,

94
00:04:01,108 --> 00:04:02,910
SURE, I'LL GIVE 'EM
THE TIME OF DAY.

95
00:04:02,943 --> 00:04:05,847
BUT IF THEY CROSS ME,
THEY'RE OFF MY LIST.

96
00:04:05,880 --> 00:04:07,215
I GUESS WHAT
I'M TRYING TO SAY IS,

97
00:04:07,248 --> 00:04:09,850
REMEMBER ME AS FRANK.

98
00:04:09,883 --> 00:04:11,818
ONE OF THE GOOD ONES.

99
00:04:11,852 --> 00:04:13,253
HOW'D I DO?

100
00:04:13,287 --> 00:04:16,890
GOOD, REAL GOOD.
NOW I'LL TURN MINE ON.

101
00:04:16,923 --> 00:04:19,160
WALK QUIETLY
AMONG OTHER MEN,

102
00:04:19,193 --> 00:04:21,662
BUT KNOW THEIR POWER,
FOR THEY ARE YOUR ENEMY.

103
00:04:21,695 --> 00:04:24,332
QUIETLY CRUSH THEM
AS YOU WORK DILIGENTLY

104
00:04:24,365 --> 00:04:25,667
THROUGH THE NIGHT.

105
00:04:25,700 --> 00:04:27,668
PAY ATTENTION TO
THE MAN BEHIND THE CURTAIN,

106
00:04:27,702 --> 00:04:29,437
FOR HE IS YOUR ALLY.

107
00:04:29,470 --> 00:04:31,305
DRINK DEEPLY AND LUSTFULLY

108
00:04:31,338 --> 00:04:33,207
FROM THE FOAMY DRAUGHT
OF EVIL.

109
00:04:33,240 --> 00:04:36,177
UH, DO IT TO THE OTHER GUY
BEFORE HE DOES IT TO YOU...

110
00:04:36,210 --> 00:04:39,680
AND BE BAD TO THE BONE,
WON'T YOU? THANK YOU.

111
00:04:39,713 --> 00:04:41,515
SIR, THAT COLOR
LOOKS GOOD ON YOU.

112
00:04:41,548 --> 00:04:44,018
OH, THIS OLD THING?
I JUST THREW IT ON.

113
00:04:44,052 --> 00:04:46,420
WELL, IT'S YOUR TURN,
JOELY-OLY INFANTRY.

114
00:04:46,453 --> 00:04:48,757
HEY SIRS,
THAT ONE'S PRETTY NEAT.

115
00:04:48,790 --> 00:04:50,958
I HOPE YOU LIKE MINE.
I DECIDED TO COMBINE

116
00:04:50,992 --> 00:04:52,327
TWO POPULAR PRODUCTS.

117
00:04:52,360 --> 00:04:53,460
THE KLEENEX DISPENSER

118
00:04:53,493 --> 00:04:55,028
AND THE PHONE MACHINE.

119
00:04:55,062 --> 00:04:56,963
WHEN I USED TO LIVE
BACK DOWN ON EARTH,

120
00:04:56,998 --> 00:04:58,298
WHEN I WORKED AT AN OFFICE,

121
00:04:58,332 --> 00:05:01,035
EVERYBODY COMPLAINED
THAT THE FAX MACHINE PAPER

122
00:05:01,068 --> 00:05:03,905
WAS JUST LIKE TISSUE,
AND THAT GIVES ME AN IDEA.

123
00:05:03,938 --> 00:05:06,240
AND I SAY, "HEY, WHY NOT
COMBINE THE TWO?"

124
00:05:06,273 --> 00:05:09,010
SO YOU GOT A FAX MACHINE
KLEENEX DISPENSER.

125
00:05:09,043 --> 00:05:11,745
IS IT A KLEENEX DISPENSER
THAT THINKS IT'S A FAX MACHINE?

126
00:05:11,778 --> 00:05:14,348
OR A FAX MACHINE THAT THINKS
IT'S A KLEENEX DISPENSER?

127
00:05:14,382 --> 00:05:15,650
HEY, WAIT A MINUTE!

128
00:05:15,683 --> 00:05:17,518
WELL, THANKS, LINUS.
SEND IT ON UP.

129
00:05:17,552 --> 00:05:19,653
I JUST TALKED
TO DR. LINUS PAULING,

130
00:05:19,687 --> 00:05:21,188
AND HE'S SENDING UP

131
00:05:21,222 --> 00:05:23,357
THE CURE FOR
THE COMMON COLD.

132
00:05:23,390 --> 00:05:26,027
- WOW!
- OH, YOU CAN
HEAR IT WORKING.

133
00:05:26,060 --> 00:05:28,028
OH, IT'S IN.

134
00:05:28,062 --> 00:05:30,998
HEY, THE CURE FOR
THE COMMON COLD

135
00:05:31,032 --> 00:05:32,700
IS SO...

136
00:05:32,733 --> 00:05:36,570
[JOEL SNEEZES]

137
00:05:36,603 --> 00:05:38,907
- UGH.
- SORRY, SIRS.

138
00:05:38,940 --> 00:05:40,675
GESUNDHEIT, SNOT LOCKER.

139
00:05:40,708 --> 00:05:42,710
WELL, YOUR PAIN
WILL BE COMPLETE

140
00:05:42,743 --> 00:05:44,978
AFTER VIEWING
TODAY'S EXPERIMENT.

141
00:05:45,012 --> 00:05:46,380
ANOTHER IN A SERIES

142
00:05:46,413 --> 00:05:49,683
OF MIND-POPPINGLY BAD
GAMERA FILMS.

143
00:05:49,717 --> 00:05:51,018
TODAY GAMERA'S OPPONENT IS--

144
00:05:51,052 --> 00:05:52,920
OH, LIKE IT MATTERS.

145
00:05:52,953 --> 00:05:56,357
CHEW EACH BITE
32 TIMES, BOOBY.

146
00:05:56,390 --> 00:05:58,292
[BOTH CHUCKLE]

147
00:06:00,962 --> 00:06:03,630
[BOTH LAUGH]

148
00:06:06,667 --> 00:06:09,203
[BOTH CACKLE]

149
00:06:11,705 --> 00:06:14,775
- HEY, THE--
- OH, WE GOT MOVIE SIGN!

150
00:06:23,918 --> 00:06:26,087
[BOTS, RASPY]
AAH!

151
00:06:26,120 --> 00:06:28,588
HEY, COME ON, YOU GUYS.

152
00:06:28,622 --> 00:06:32,460
OH NO, DAIEI!

153
00:06:32,493 --> 00:06:35,697
[ALL]
♪ GAOS! GAOS! ♪

154
00:06:35,730 --> 00:06:39,333
♪ DAYLIGHT COME,
AND ME WANT GO HOME ♪

155
00:06:39,367 --> 00:06:42,303
HEY, DID SOMEBODY WIPE THAT WITH
SOAP ON A WINDOW OR SOMETHING?

156
00:06:44,472 --> 00:06:47,007
OH, THAT'S JAPANESE
FOR "HIDEOUS NEGATIVITY."

157
00:06:47,040 --> 00:06:49,510
HIDEMASA NAGATA!

158
00:06:49,543 --> 00:06:51,045
HEY, HE'S AN AUTEUR PLAN.

159
00:06:51,078 --> 00:06:52,580
DID YOU READ ANDREW SARRIS'S
BOOK ABOUT HIM?

160
00:06:52,613 --> 00:06:54,882
NO.

161
00:06:54,915 --> 00:06:58,318
I LOVE PLANNING.

162
00:06:58,352 --> 00:06:59,653
HMM.

163
00:06:59,687 --> 00:07:01,822
HEY, THERE'S SOME FUMES

164
00:07:01,855 --> 00:07:04,692
COMING OFF YOUR SCREENPLAY
THERE, FUMI.

165
00:07:04,725 --> 00:07:08,562
SOUNDS LIKE MAYNARD FERGUSON
PLAYING A BALLAD, DOESN'T IT?

166
00:07:08,595 --> 00:07:09,897
HEY, WELL,
WHAT DOES A DIRECTOR DO

167
00:07:09,930 --> 00:07:13,133
IF ALL THE PLANNING'S DONE?

168
00:07:13,167 --> 00:07:16,903
MR. GAMERA'S WARDROBE
BY BOTANY 500.

169
00:07:20,508 --> 00:07:22,343
NOT-SO-SPECIAL EFFECTS

170
00:07:22,410 --> 00:07:24,912
BY KAZUFUMI FUJII.

171
00:07:27,948 --> 00:07:31,518
OH, GESUNDHEIT, TATSUJI.

172
00:07:31,518 --> 00:07:34,322
YOU KNOW, JAPANESE PEOPLE
MAKE FUN OF AMERICAN NAMES.

173
00:07:34,355 --> 00:07:36,657
OH, I SUPPOSE SO.

174
00:07:39,527 --> 00:07:42,028
♪♪ [ALL HUM TO SCORE]

175
00:07:42,028 --> 00:07:44,665
AND THE STUDENT BODY OF YALE
AS THE TOWNSPEOPLE.

176
00:07:44,732 --> 00:07:47,635
REINO IN RAGE AND REHAB.

177
00:07:52,773 --> 00:07:54,875
NOW, ARE WE SUPPOSED TO BE
FULL-SIZE OR MINIATURE?

178
00:07:54,942 --> 00:07:56,143
I CAN NEVER TELL.

179
00:07:56,177 --> 00:07:58,145
[INTERCOM]
...AT GATE NUMBER THREE.

180
00:07:58,145 --> 00:08:00,447
SO GAMERA'S RETURNED
ONCE AGAIN.

181
00:08:00,447 --> 00:08:01,948
AFTER AN ABSENCE
OF NEARLY TWO YEARS,

182
00:08:01,948 --> 00:08:03,650
WE SEE AGAIN THE GREAT BEAST
OF THE NEW STATE

183
00:08:03,683 --> 00:08:05,520
ONCE CALLED
A BENEVOLENT MONSTER.

184
00:08:05,553 --> 00:08:07,355
AND THE QUESTION IS,
HAS IT RETAINED ITS BENEVOLENCE,

185
00:08:07,388 --> 00:08:08,923
OR HAS IT PERHAPS
CHANGED NOW?

186
00:08:08,957 --> 00:08:10,190
THESE ARE THE QUESTIONS--

187
00:08:10,223 --> 00:08:11,558
HEY, HERE COMES
PAUL McCARTNEY.

188
00:08:11,592 --> 00:08:13,560
HEY.

189
00:08:13,593 --> 00:08:15,730
--AND WHY DID IT ENTER INTO
THE VERY HEART OF THE VOLCANO?

190
00:08:15,763 --> 00:08:17,298
IS IT DEAD NOW,
OR IS IT REPLENISHING

191
00:08:17,332 --> 00:08:19,300
ITS ENERGY FROM THE FLAMES?
FOR THE ANSWERS,

192
00:08:19,333 --> 00:08:20,835
WE SHALL HAVE TO BE
PATIENT FOR A LITTLE WHILE.

193
00:08:20,868 --> 00:08:22,870
UNTIL THE RESEARCH PARTY
CAN RETURN FROM THE SCENE.

194
00:08:22,903 --> 00:08:24,705
MODEL, AWAY!

195
00:08:24,738 --> 00:08:26,373
--IS NOW TAKING OFF
BY HELICOPTER.

196
00:08:26,407 --> 00:08:30,277
AND NOW I'LL SING A MEDLEY
OF HELEN REDDY SONGS.

197
00:08:30,310 --> 00:08:32,547
♪ HELLO MRS. FUJI ♪

198
00:08:32,580 --> 00:08:34,282
♪ THIS IS HARRY HOSHO ♪

199
00:08:34,315 --> 00:08:38,218
♪ CAN I SPEAK TO ANYONE? ♪

200
00:08:38,252 --> 00:08:41,888
HERE WE ARE UP ON
HOUSING PROJECT HILL.

201
00:08:43,690 --> 00:08:46,227
[PEOPLE CLAMOR]

202
00:08:46,260 --> 00:08:48,495
HMM?

203
00:08:50,530 --> 00:08:52,098
[PHONE RINGS]

204
00:08:52,132 --> 00:08:53,433
AHH, I KNEW IT WOULD RING.

205
00:08:53,467 --> 00:08:54,435
THAT'S WHY
I PUT THE CAMERA ON IT.

206
00:08:54,468 --> 00:08:56,470
- GOOD PLANNING.
- MM-HMM.

207
00:08:56,503 --> 00:08:58,973
- HAVEN'T YOU GOT HIM YET?
- I'LL KEEP ON TRYING.

208
00:08:59,007 --> 00:09:02,008
IT'S HUBERT HUMPHREY!
"I'M PLEASED AS PUNCH."

209
00:09:02,042 --> 00:09:03,843
I'M TIRED OF EXCUSES.
WHATEVER HAPPENS,

210
00:09:03,877 --> 00:09:07,147
THE WORK ON THE NEW EXPRESSWAY
HAS GOT TO GO AHEAD ON SCHEDULE.

211
00:09:07,180 --> 00:09:08,882
APART FROM THE QUESTION
OF SHAREHOLDERS,

212
00:09:08,917 --> 00:09:10,150
THE WHOLE COUNTRY'S
WATCHING TO SEE

213
00:09:10,183 --> 00:09:11,485
IF WE FINISH
THE ROAD ON TIME.

214
00:09:11,518 --> 00:09:13,988
THEY'RE STARVED
FOR ENTERTAINMENT.

215
00:09:14,022 --> 00:09:15,455
BUT I'M TIRED
OF THESE DELAYS.

216
00:09:15,488 --> 00:09:17,692
THERE SEEMS TO BE
ONE DARN THING AFTER THE OTHER.

217
00:09:17,725 --> 00:09:19,260
- SO WHAT IS IT NOW?
DO YOU KNOW, EH?

218
00:09:19,293 --> 00:09:22,128
- YES.
- UH, THIS DARN THING
HERE, SIR.

219
00:09:22,162 --> 00:09:23,897
OH, THAT DARN THING.

220
00:09:23,932 --> 00:09:26,067
--UH, IT'S THIS SECTION.
ALL THE FARMERS UP THERE

221
00:09:26,100 --> 00:09:27,668
REFUSE TO SELL THE LAND.

222
00:09:27,702 --> 00:09:29,337
WE'RE ARGUING,
BUT NOT GETTING FAR.

223
00:09:29,370 --> 00:09:31,938
- NOT GETTIN' FAR.
- WELL REALLY PUT
THE PRESSURE ON THEM.

224
00:09:31,972 --> 00:09:33,975
- YES.
- ANYWAY, GET THEM MOVED OUT.

225
00:09:34,008 --> 00:09:35,877
- DON'T WASTE ANY TIME, EH?
- YES.

226
00:09:35,910 --> 00:09:38,578
OH, JUST A MINUTE.
THE CHIEF IS CALLING YOU.

227
00:09:38,612 --> 00:09:41,082
- WHAT, SITTING BULL?
- YOU'RE THROUGH.

228
00:09:41,115 --> 00:09:45,018
MR. TSUTSUMI, THE ENGINEER
IN CHARGE OF THE ROAD.

229
00:09:45,052 --> 00:09:47,187
- NOW TSUTSUMI--
- [ALL] GESUNDHEIT.

230
00:09:47,220 --> 00:09:48,855
I HEAR THAT YOU'RE HAVING
SOME TROUBLE WITH THE FARMERS.

231
00:09:48,888 --> 00:09:50,357
THEY WON'T CLEAR OFF
THE LAND NOW.

232
00:09:50,390 --> 00:09:52,360
WELL, IT'S PART OF YOUR JOB
TO MAKE SURE THEY GET OFF.

233
00:09:52,393 --> 00:09:53,660
AND GET TO WORK MOVING.

234
00:09:53,693 --> 00:09:56,130
BUT SIR, WE'VE GOT ANOTHER
PROBLEM ON OUR HANDS NOW

235
00:09:56,163 --> 00:09:57,465
APART FROM THE LANDOWNERS--

236
00:09:57,498 --> 00:09:59,100
THE STRAP IN MY HELMET
BROKE.

237
00:09:59,133 --> 00:10:00,835
--A REPORT ON
THE RECENT ERUPTIONS HERE.

238
00:10:00,868 --> 00:10:04,038
- TO HELL WITH THE REPORT.
- OOH.

239
00:10:04,072 --> 00:10:05,940
I DON'T CARE ABOUT THE VOLCANO
OR ABOUT THE MONSTER.

240
00:10:05,973 --> 00:10:07,207
I LOVE YOU!

241
00:10:07,240 --> 00:10:09,943
JUST MAKE SURE THE FARMERS
GET OFF THE LAND.

242
00:10:09,977 --> 00:10:11,645
AND PLEASE DON'T BOTHER ME
WITH ANY MORE OF THESE

243
00:10:11,678 --> 00:10:13,547
- STUPID REASONS--
- LOOK AT THE SIZE
OF THAT PHONE.

244
00:10:13,580 --> 00:10:15,415
YEAH, AND ANOTHER THING.
I DON'T MIND TELLING YOU

245
00:10:15,448 --> 00:10:16,917
THAT YOU SHOULD-- HEY!

246
00:10:16,950 --> 00:10:20,655
HEY, HEY BOSS.

247
00:10:20,688 --> 00:10:22,357
WHAT'S THE BOSS HAVE TO SAY?

248
00:10:22,390 --> 00:10:25,893
UH...

249
00:10:25,927 --> 00:10:27,995
- WE START WORK AGAIN.
- [WORKERS] HUH?

250
00:10:28,028 --> 00:10:30,197
EVEN WHEN THERE'S A CHANCE
THERE'LL BE ANOTHER ERUPTION?

251
00:10:30,230 --> 00:10:31,798
ON MY FACE?

252
00:10:31,832 --> 00:10:34,035
LET'S GET THIS STUFF TOGETHER
AND MOVE ON UP TO THIS SITE.

253
00:10:34,068 --> 00:10:37,270
- I'LL FOLLOW ON.
- OKAY.
- RIGHT.

254
00:10:37,303 --> 00:10:39,907
WELL, I SHOULD'VE
TAKEN THAT JOB AT HONDA.

255
00:10:39,940 --> 00:10:41,708
--ONE THING AFTER THE OTHER.

256
00:10:41,742 --> 00:10:44,512
HANG IN THERE, BABY.
FRIDAY'S COMING.

257
00:10:44,545 --> 00:10:46,413
IT'S WALTER PIDGEON!

258
00:10:46,447 --> 00:10:48,482
I SEE GREER GARSON
DOWN THERE.

259
00:10:48,515 --> 00:10:51,785
REALLY?

260
00:10:51,818 --> 00:10:54,488
HEY, THEY'RE FLYING OVER
A POT ROAST.

261
00:10:54,522 --> 00:10:56,257
- MM.
- LOOKS DELICIOUS.

262
00:10:56,290 --> 00:10:59,493
- NUM.
- MM-HMM.

263
00:10:59,527 --> 00:11:01,895
HEY, THERE'S A LITTLE POCKET
OF MINT JELLY!

264
00:11:01,928 --> 00:11:04,098
INTERESTING.

265
00:11:04,132 --> 00:11:05,767
OOH.

266
00:11:05,800 --> 00:11:07,735
MAN, THE MINT JELLY'S
ATTACKING.

267
00:11:07,768 --> 00:11:09,337
DON'T SEE THAT OFTEN.

268
00:11:09,370 --> 00:11:11,938
I'M AMUSED BY
THE LITTLE POCKET OF JELLY.

269
00:11:11,972 --> 00:11:13,373
PULL OVER!

270
00:11:13,407 --> 00:11:15,375
THERE'S SO MANY THINGS
TO DO AND SEE.

271
00:11:15,408 --> 00:11:17,343
WHOO!

272
00:11:20,748 --> 00:11:22,517
UH-OH.

273
00:11:22,550 --> 00:11:24,052
WE THOUGHT IT WOULD BE FUNNY

274
00:11:24,085 --> 00:11:25,953
TO SPLIT A HELICOPTER
IN HALF.

275
00:11:25,987 --> 00:11:27,388
HEY, MY LUGGAGE!

276
00:11:27,422 --> 00:11:30,190
OOH.

277
00:11:30,223 --> 00:11:32,893
MODEL POLICE, IN COLOR!

278
00:11:32,927 --> 00:11:34,262
GEEZ.

279
00:11:34,295 --> 00:11:35,662
[MEN CLAMOR]

280
00:11:35,695 --> 00:11:38,232
WHAT'S THE BUZZ?
TELL ME WHAT'S A-HAPPENIN'.

281
00:11:40,902 --> 00:11:43,070
HEY, THERE MUST BE
A SIX FLAGS OVER OSAKA.

282
00:11:43,103 --> 00:11:45,807
--BY MOUNT FUJI ERUPTIONS.

283
00:11:45,840 --> 00:11:47,240
WAS IT GAMERA, PERHAPS?

284
00:11:47,273 --> 00:11:49,210
I HEARD SOMEBODY REPORTED
A STRONG GREEN LIGHT THERE.

285
00:11:49,243 --> 00:11:50,577
AND WHAT ABOUT THE PARTY
IN THE HELICOPTER?

286
00:11:50,610 --> 00:11:52,980
AND WHAT OF BILL
AND HIS LOVE FOR TERRY?

287
00:11:53,013 --> 00:11:54,748
ONLY ONE THING IS CERTAIN.
THE CRASH HAD

288
00:11:54,782 --> 00:11:56,817
NOTHING AT ALL TO DO WITH
THE RECENT ERUPTIONS HERE.

289
00:11:56,850 --> 00:11:59,153
YOU'LL HAVE TO WAIT
FOR THE RESULT OF THE CRASH
INVESTIGATION.

290
00:11:59,187 --> 00:12:00,687
- AND GAMERA?
- GAMERA DOESN'T SEND OUT

291
00:12:00,720 --> 00:12:03,290
DESTRUCTIVE RAYS, TO THE BEST
OF ANYONE'S KNOWLEDGE.

292
00:12:03,323 --> 00:12:05,258
BUT STILL, THE POSSIBILITY
WON'T BE IGNORED.

293
00:12:05,292 --> 00:12:06,727
NOW, THAT'S ALL I CAN
TELL YOU AT THE MOMENT.

294
00:12:06,760 --> 00:12:08,395
LOOK, I'M A DOORMAN,
LEAVE ME ALONE.

295
00:12:08,428 --> 00:12:11,198
[MEN CLAMOR]

296
00:12:11,232 --> 00:12:13,367
RIGHT. I'LL GO LOOK
FOR MYSELF.

297
00:12:13,400 --> 00:12:16,103
- D'OH.
- NOBODY LOVES ME.
EVERYBODY HATES ME.

298
00:12:16,137 --> 00:12:17,705
THINK I'LL GO FIND GAOS.

299
00:12:17,738 --> 00:12:19,707
UM, YOU MIGHT WANNA
PUT THAT HELMET ON.

300
00:12:19,740 --> 00:12:22,910
HEY, THREE BIG MACS
FOR THE PRICE OF-- OH.

301
00:12:24,845 --> 00:12:26,713
HEY, WHAT IS THIS?

302
00:12:26,747 --> 00:12:29,983
IT'S THE SET
OF COAL MINER'S DAUGHTER.

303
00:12:30,017 --> 00:12:31,718
IS IT FARMERS AGAIN?

304
00:12:31,752 --> 00:12:35,088
IT SAYS "HOLLYWOOD."

305
00:12:35,122 --> 00:12:37,758
[BOTH]
OOH.

306
00:12:37,792 --> 00:12:40,928
OH NO, IT'S THE CAST
OF "HEAD INJURY PLAYHOUSE."

307
00:12:40,962 --> 00:12:42,295
OH, WATCH IT.

308
00:12:42,328 --> 00:12:44,465
WE WANNA TRADE
LUNCH MONEY. NOW.

309
00:12:44,498 --> 00:12:46,600
[MEN GRUMBLE]

310
00:12:46,633 --> 00:12:49,002
[SERVO GRUMBLES]

311
00:12:52,005 --> 00:12:53,273
NOW HOLD IT.

312
00:12:53,307 --> 00:12:55,475
HEY BOSS, THESE GUYS
ARE OUT TO MAKE TROUBLE.

313
00:12:55,508 --> 00:12:57,678
[MEN CLAMOR]

314
00:12:57,712 --> 00:12:59,847
WAIT A MINUTE,
LET'S TALK ABOUT IT NOW.

315
00:12:59,880 --> 00:13:01,548
WHO'S SUPPOSED
TO BE IN CHARGE HERE, HUH?

316
00:13:01,582 --> 00:13:02,883
WHERE CAN I FIND
THE HEAD MAN?

317
00:13:02,917 --> 00:13:06,187
WE'RE A MOB!
WE DON'T NEED A HEAD MAN!

318
00:13:06,220 --> 00:13:07,955
JUST STOP IT, ALL OF YOU!

319
00:13:07,988 --> 00:13:09,890
- HEY...
- WHAT DO YOU THINK
YOU'RE DOING?

320
00:13:09,923 --> 00:13:13,693
WHO CAN TURN THE WORLD ON
WITH HER SMILE?

321
00:13:13,727 --> 00:13:17,097
HIM?

322
00:13:17,130 --> 00:13:19,065
YOU GET YOUR MEN
OUT OF HERE, QUICKLY.

323
00:13:19,098 --> 00:13:20,733
WELL, CAN I TALK
TO THE HEAD MAN?

324
00:13:20,767 --> 00:13:22,703
- I'M THE HEAD MAN.
- --SOME OTHER TIME.

325
00:13:22,737 --> 00:13:24,605
AT LEAST YOU CAN
TELL ME WHEN, THOUGH.

326
00:13:24,638 --> 00:13:27,073
- [ALL CLAMOR]
- [BOTS CLAMOR]

327
00:13:30,110 --> 00:13:33,013
SAY...

328
00:13:33,047 --> 00:13:34,348
[MAN]
GO ON, OUT OF HERE!

329
00:13:34,382 --> 00:13:36,617
[SERVO GROWLS]

330
00:13:36,650 --> 00:13:38,418
PLEASE DO WHAT I TELL YOU
AND GET OUT QUICKLY.

331
00:13:38,452 --> 00:13:41,055
- [PEOPLE CLAMOR]
- [BOTS CLAMOR]

332
00:13:45,058 --> 00:13:48,262
THE BIKER RALLY AT STURGIS
IS WHAT THIS LOOKS LIKE.

333
00:13:48,295 --> 00:13:50,597
WHY ARE ALL THE CUTE ONES
SO CORPORATE?

334
00:13:53,467 --> 00:13:56,237
STEVE McQUEEN IS BULLITT.

335
00:13:57,838 --> 00:14:01,575
IT'S REX DART, ESKIMO SPY.

336
00:14:01,608 --> 00:14:04,678
[CROW MIMICS BANJO]

337
00:14:04,712 --> 00:14:07,582
HMM.

338
00:14:07,615 --> 00:14:08,948
WH-- WALL DRUG,

339
00:14:08,982 --> 00:14:11,152
10,000 MILES.

340
00:14:17,692 --> 00:14:19,192
- [COW MOOS]
- OH, BLESS YOU.

341
00:14:19,227 --> 00:14:20,962
WAS HE MOOING?

342
00:14:20,995 --> 00:14:22,328
WHAT'LL HAPPEN NOW?

343
00:14:22,362 --> 00:14:24,063
AH, YOU CAN BET
THE CONSTRUCTION GANG'LL

344
00:14:24,097 --> 00:14:25,900
- BE BACK IN A FEW DAYS.
- LOOK, IT'S THE PAINTERS UNION.

345
00:14:25,933 --> 00:14:28,035
YEAH, WE OUGHTA GO UP
AND WRECK THAT SITE.

346
00:14:28,068 --> 00:14:30,470
- WHAT DO YOU SAY?
- YEAH, LET'S GO DO THAT.

347
00:14:30,503 --> 00:14:32,338
- YES. GO AHEAD.
- YEAH, LET'S GO!

348
00:14:32,372 --> 00:14:34,475
YEAH, LET'S FORM
THE REPUBLIC! WHEE!

349
00:14:34,508 --> 00:14:36,243
WE'LL TEACH 'EM.

350
00:14:36,277 --> 00:14:37,878
THE MORE TROUBLE
WE MAKE FOR THEM,

351
00:14:37,912 --> 00:14:40,347
THE MORE THEY'LL PAY US
FOR OUR LAND.

352
00:14:40,380 --> 00:14:42,750
YES, IT'S THE ONLY CHANCE
WE'RE EVER GOING TO GET.

353
00:14:42,783 --> 00:14:44,017
WE'LL MAKE THEM
PAY US MORE MONEY

354
00:14:44,050 --> 00:14:45,518
THAN WE EVER DREAMED
OF HAVING IN OUR LIVES.

355
00:14:45,552 --> 00:14:47,220
AT LEAST $100.

356
00:14:47,253 --> 00:14:50,823
JUST AS LONG AS YOU LEAVE
ALL THE PLANNING TO ME.

357
00:14:50,857 --> 00:14:52,158
OH, HE'S THE PLANNER.

358
00:14:52,192 --> 00:14:54,262
HEY, HOW'S THAT POLE
COMING, MOM?

359
00:14:54,295 --> 00:14:56,297
- YOU'RE EARLY.
- I'M NOT SURE THAT

360
00:14:56,330 --> 00:14:58,198
WE'RE DOING THE RIGHT THING
ABOUT THIS ROAD.

361
00:14:58,232 --> 00:15:00,633
I THINK IT'LL BRING A LOT
OF BENEFITS TO THE VILLAGE.

362
00:15:00,667 --> 00:15:02,502
- DON'T YOU THINK?
- SELLING ONE'S LAND

363
00:15:02,535 --> 00:15:04,103
IS ALWAYS
A PAINFUL BUSINESS.

364
00:15:04,137 --> 00:15:06,140
AND ESPECIALLY SO
IF YOU HAPPEN TO BE A FARMER.

365
00:15:06,173 --> 00:15:07,540
- I SUPPOSE YOU'RE RIGHT.
- [COW MOOS]

366
00:15:07,573 --> 00:15:10,110
COULD SOMEBODY MILK GRANDPA?
HE'S IN A LOT OF PAIN.

367
00:15:10,143 --> 00:15:12,345
- --EIICHI?
- HE'S AROUND HERE.

368
00:15:12,378 --> 00:15:13,813
HE WAS PLAYING OUTSIDE
A WHILE AGO.

369
00:15:13,847 --> 00:15:16,083
EIICHI?

370
00:15:16,117 --> 00:15:19,487
I BOUGHT HIM A NEW DIARY
WHILE I WAS OUT.

371
00:15:26,227 --> 00:15:29,797
PUT YOUR SHOES ON.
WE'RE AT GRANDMA'S.

372
00:15:29,830 --> 00:15:31,532
GET YOUR THINGS
UP TO THE SITE.

373
00:15:31,565 --> 00:15:34,368
UH-OH. IT'S THE RIGHT-WING
HIGHWAY DEPARTMENT DEATH SQUAD.

374
00:15:34,402 --> 00:15:36,103
LET'S RAPE THE LAND!
COME ON!

375
00:15:36,137 --> 00:15:38,305
YEAH, I DON'T THINK I'VE EVER
MET A MORE GREEDY CROWD

376
00:15:38,338 --> 00:15:39,940
IN MY WHOLE LIFE
THAN THESE VILLAGERS.

377
00:15:39,973 --> 00:15:41,542
ALL THIS TROUBLE
THEY'RE CAUSING IS JUST FOR

378
00:15:41,575 --> 00:15:42,943
A FEW MORE DOLLARS.

379
00:15:42,977 --> 00:15:44,645
WHAT? BUDDY HACKETT
IS THEIR FOREMAN?

380
00:15:44,678 --> 00:15:46,680
- COME ON, HURRY UP.
- OKAY.

381
00:15:49,517 --> 00:15:51,818
HEY, SOMEBODY DROPPED
THEIR DRAWERS.

382
00:15:51,852 --> 00:15:54,220
- WHAT THE HELL'S HAPPENING?
- IT'S A GARAGE SALE.

383
00:15:54,253 --> 00:15:56,223
LOOK AT THE MESS.

384
00:15:56,257 --> 00:15:57,825
HOW ON EARTH
COULD THAT HAVE HAPPENED?

385
00:15:57,858 --> 00:15:59,927
IT'S PERFECT. I LOVE IT.

386
00:16:02,328 --> 00:16:04,665
I'LL TELL YOU WHAT.
THIS MUST'VE HAPPENED RECENTLY

387
00:16:04,698 --> 00:16:06,600
BECAUSE IT WAS ALL RIGHT
WHEN WE LEFT HERE YESTERDAY.

388
00:16:06,633 --> 00:16:08,435
YEAH, SOMETIME BETWEEN
YESTERDAY AND RIGHT NOW--

389
00:16:08,468 --> 00:16:10,837
- PRETTY MUCH.
- YES, YOU'RE RIGHT.

390
00:16:10,870 --> 00:16:12,538
THIS HAS BEEN DONE
QUITE DELIBERATELY.

391
00:16:12,572 --> 00:16:14,273
- MM-HMM.
- NO QUESTION OF AN ACCIDENT.

392
00:16:14,307 --> 00:16:15,975
EXCUSE ME. I'M S-- OH.

393
00:16:16,010 --> 00:16:18,678
ALL RIGHT. IF THAT'S
THE WAY THEY WANT IT,

394
00:16:18,712 --> 00:16:20,880
THEN THEY WON'T STOP THE ROAD
GOING THROUGH NOW.

395
00:16:20,913 --> 00:16:22,683
AND THEY'RE GONNA BE
THE LOSERS IN THE LONG RUN.

396
00:16:22,717 --> 00:16:24,485
SO LET'S GET ON
WITH THE JOB.

397
00:16:24,518 --> 00:16:26,720
- YEAH, LET'S GET ON.
- RIGHT, LET'S GO.

398
00:16:26,753 --> 00:16:28,455
- RIGHT.
- OKAY, RIGHT.

399
00:16:28,488 --> 00:16:30,457
COME ON. GIVE A HAND
OVER HERE.

400
00:16:30,490 --> 00:16:32,693
- GIVE HIM A HAND, JOEL.
- PUT THAT BOX IN.

401
00:16:32,727 --> 00:16:35,528
- [SERVO MUTTERS]
- AAH! HEY, BOSS! HEY BOSS!

402
00:16:35,562 --> 00:16:37,430
LOOK! LOOK UP THERE!

403
00:16:37,463 --> 00:16:39,667
- WHERE?
- UP THERE, LOOK!
- OH, I SEE IT.

404
00:16:39,700 --> 00:16:41,935
WELL, THAT WASN'T
THERE YESTERDAY.

405
00:16:41,968 --> 00:16:43,503
WHAT ON EARTH DO YOU THINK
IT COULD BE?

406
00:16:43,537 --> 00:16:45,938
SOMETHING THAT MAKES US
TALK LIKE WALTER BRENNAN.

407
00:16:45,972 --> 00:16:47,507
FUNNY SMELL.

408
00:16:47,540 --> 00:16:49,543
AH, THEY'RE JUST
SMELLING THEMSELVES.

409
00:16:49,577 --> 00:16:51,478
I REMEMBER READING SOMEWHERE
GOLD DEPOSITS

410
00:16:51,512 --> 00:16:53,247
SOMETIMES GIVE OFF
THAT TYPE OF GLOSS.

411
00:16:53,280 --> 00:16:54,582
- GOLDILOCKS?
- THAT'S RIGHT.

412
00:16:54,615 --> 00:16:56,417
SOMEBODY ONCE TOLD ME
ABOUT THAT TOO.

413
00:16:56,450 --> 00:16:58,418
HEY, BOSS, DO YOU THINK THERE
COULD BE GOLD UP THERE, HUH?

414
00:16:58,452 --> 00:17:00,453
- SURE, BUTTERCUP, SURE.
- WELL, IT'S NOT IMPOSSIBLE--

415
00:17:00,487 --> 00:17:02,422
I SEE NOW.
THAT'S THE ANSWER, THEN.

416
00:17:02,455 --> 00:17:03,757
THAT EXPLAINS EVERYTHING.

417
00:17:03,790 --> 00:17:05,492
THOSE FARMERS KNOW
ALL ABOUT THE GOLD.

418
00:17:05,525 --> 00:17:07,560
- THAT'S WHY THEY--
- THANK YOU, CURLY JOE.

419
00:17:07,593 --> 00:17:10,130
WELL, LET'S GO ON UP
AND TAKE A LOOK AROUND THERE.

420
00:17:10,163 --> 00:17:12,665
WE HAVE TO MAKE A SURVEY
OF THE AREA FOR THE NEW ROAD.

421
00:17:12,698 --> 00:17:14,435
BRING THE STUFF ALONG.
WE'LL GO STRAIGHT UP.

422
00:17:14,468 --> 00:17:16,570
YEAH, BRING THE STUFF,
THE CRAP, AND THE JUNK.

423
00:17:16,603 --> 00:17:18,705
- OKAY.
- AND THAT THING.

424
00:17:18,738 --> 00:17:20,873
AND THE OTHER THING.

425
00:17:20,907 --> 00:17:22,475
OH, IS BOB SAGET

426
00:17:22,508 --> 00:17:26,247
GONNA LOVE THIS ONE.

427
00:17:26,280 --> 00:17:29,450
UH-OH, GAMERA'S HOMEBOY.

428
00:17:29,483 --> 00:17:32,418
- BOY.
- BOY? CRAZY BOY?

429
00:17:32,452 --> 00:17:35,355
NO, IT WASN'T EITHER.
I'M A GUARD HERE.

430
00:17:35,388 --> 00:17:38,292
I'M GONNA STOP THEM.
THE MEN FROM THE NEW ROAD CAME.

431
00:17:38,325 --> 00:17:40,227
THAT'S WHAT I'M DOING.

432
00:17:40,260 --> 00:17:42,162
I SEE NOW.
I'M A HIKER THOUGH.

433
00:17:42,195 --> 00:17:43,363
- AND A CANADIAN.
- DO YOU HAPPEN TO KNOW

434
00:17:43,397 --> 00:17:45,098
A SHORTCUT
UP TO THE TOP THERE?

435
00:17:45,132 --> 00:17:47,902
- YOU'RE TELLING ME LIES.
- SWEET LITTLE LIES.

436
00:17:47,935 --> 00:17:49,637
YOU'RE NOT A HIKER AT ALL.

437
00:17:49,670 --> 00:17:51,638
YOU'RE A NEWSPAPER REPORTER,
AREN'T YOU?

438
00:17:51,672 --> 00:17:54,508
I'LL BE ANYTHING
YOU WANT ME TO BE.

439
00:17:54,542 --> 00:17:56,443
I KNEW STRAIGHTAWAY
YOU WERE A REPORTER.

440
00:17:56,477 --> 00:17:57,778
- NICE LIPSTICK, KID.
- AND I DON'T THINK

441
00:17:57,812 --> 00:18:00,747
- I SHOULD SHOW YOU THE WAY.
- OH, I SEE.

442
00:18:00,780 --> 00:18:02,548
THAT'S A PITY, THOUGH.

443
00:18:02,582 --> 00:18:04,685
IF I COULD GET A PICTURE
OF THAT GREEN LIGHT,

444
00:18:04,718 --> 00:18:06,153
I COULD STILL GET IT
IN THE EVENING EDITION

445
00:18:06,187 --> 00:18:07,620
OF ANY NEWSPAPER.

446
00:18:07,653 --> 00:18:10,623
- THAT WOULD BE A SCOOP, HUH?
- I GUESS IT WOULD.

447
00:18:10,657 --> 00:18:12,192
I'D LIKE TO SEE A SCOOP, TOO.

448
00:18:12,225 --> 00:18:13,393
BUT I'M RETAINING WATER
RIGHT NOW.

449
00:18:13,427 --> 00:18:15,728
PERHAPS WE'D SEE
GAMERA THERE TOO.

450
00:18:15,762 --> 00:18:17,530
AND THAT WOULD BE A STORY.

451
00:18:17,563 --> 00:18:19,633
- GAMERA'S THERE?
- MM-HMM.

452
00:18:19,667 --> 00:18:21,435
GAMERA BROKE MY HEART ONCE.

453
00:18:21,468 --> 00:18:23,070
BUT I GUESS
I STILL LOVE HIM.

454
00:18:23,103 --> 00:18:25,338
MAYBE GAMERA CAN
FIX THAT KID'S TEETH TOO.

455
00:18:25,372 --> 00:18:28,075
- YEAH.
- OH, I JUST STEPPED
IN SOMETHING.

456
00:18:34,515 --> 00:18:36,115
BOY, BOY.

457
00:18:36,150 --> 00:18:39,085
- CRAZY BOY.
- DO THE BIG TREES
USUALLY FALL LIKE THIS?

458
00:18:39,118 --> 00:18:42,222
YES, AND IF NO ONE'S AROUND,
DOES IT MAKE A SOUND?

459
00:18:42,255 --> 00:18:45,025
DIE, FROG, DIE!

460
00:18:45,058 --> 00:18:46,893
- BOY. BOY.
- [ALL] CRAZY BOY.

461
00:18:46,927 --> 00:18:48,462
LOOK AT THAT.

462
00:18:48,495 --> 00:18:51,198
OH, THAT'S JUST
GRANDPA'S STILL.

463
00:18:51,232 --> 00:18:53,333
THE FOREST OF THE TRUMPETS.

464
00:18:53,367 --> 00:18:55,068
...CREME DE MENTHE?

465
00:18:58,005 --> 00:19:00,873
HEY. WHAT IS IT?

466
00:19:00,907 --> 00:19:02,408
- WELL, I DON'T KNOW.
- I'M ONLY SIX.

467
00:19:02,442 --> 00:19:05,045
WHO DO YOU THINK I AM,
CARL SAGAN?

468
00:19:08,182 --> 00:19:10,017
HEY, DO ALL JAPANESE CHILDREN
HAVE TO DRESS LIKE

469
00:19:10,050 --> 00:19:11,618
FISHER PRICE PEOPLE?

470
00:19:11,652 --> 00:19:12,953
WEEBLES.

471
00:19:12,987 --> 00:19:14,855
LISTEN. ISAAC STERN.

472
00:19:14,888 --> 00:19:16,557
ITZHAK PERLMAN?

473
00:19:16,590 --> 00:19:18,325
NO, IT'S YO-YO MA.

474
00:19:18,358 --> 00:19:19,860
MY MAMA WAS A SAINT!

475
00:19:19,893 --> 00:19:22,228
NO, YO-YO MA. THE CELLIST.

476
00:19:22,262 --> 00:19:24,397
THIS GLOW AROUND THE CAVE.
YOU SEEN IT BEFORE?

477
00:19:24,430 --> 00:19:26,800
- NO, I HAVEN'T.
- NOT SINCE THE LAST
MONSTER MOVIE.

478
00:19:26,833 --> 00:19:29,268
THERE MUST BE
SOMETHING THERE.

479
00:19:30,870 --> 00:19:34,373
[BIRDS CAW]

480
00:19:34,407 --> 00:19:37,010
- HEY, STOP THAT.
- YOU'LL GO BLIND.

481
00:19:37,043 --> 00:19:39,478
- WHAT'S HE DOING?
- HEY, HANG ON.

482
00:19:39,512 --> 00:19:42,148
- BOY.
- [ALL] BOY, CRAZY BOY.

483
00:19:42,182 --> 00:19:44,785
WHY, NO. BUT WE MAY AS WELL
HAVE A LOOK IN THERE

484
00:19:44,818 --> 00:19:46,587
NOW THAT WE'VE GOT THIS FAR.

485
00:19:46,620 --> 00:19:48,255
OH, WHY DIDN'T
I THINK OF THAT?

486
00:19:48,288 --> 00:19:50,090
THAT KID IS SMART.

487
00:19:54,227 --> 00:19:56,430
WHAT IS IT?

488
00:19:56,463 --> 00:19:58,865
MM. IT'S THE CAVE
OF THE CLAN BAR.

489
00:19:58,898 --> 00:20:00,300
HMM?

490
00:20:00,333 --> 00:20:04,137
SOUNDS LIKE SOMEBODY'S
LEANING ON THE ORGAN.

491
00:20:04,170 --> 00:20:06,940
BE CAREFUL, HUH?

492
00:20:06,973 --> 00:20:09,877
OH, IT'S ONE OF THOSE
INDUSTRIAL LOFT TYPE DISCOS.

493
00:20:09,910 --> 00:20:11,978
- THAT'S WHAT IT IS.
- OH.

494
00:20:12,012 --> 00:20:15,715
INJUN JOE? BECKY? HUCK?

495
00:20:15,748 --> 00:20:17,883
[SQUAWK]

496
00:20:17,918 --> 00:20:19,185
OH, FLYING HELL-BEASTS.

497
00:20:19,218 --> 00:20:21,822
SEEN IT.

498
00:20:21,855 --> 00:20:23,790
WE'RE HAVING AN ADVENTURE
JUST LIKE THE GOONIES,

499
00:20:23,823 --> 00:20:26,125
AREN'T WE?

500
00:20:29,095 --> 00:20:30,697
HUH. THE RIVER STYX.

501
00:20:30,730 --> 00:20:32,732
OR WORSE YET,
IT'S THE BAND STYX.

502
00:20:32,765 --> 00:20:34,367
[ROAR]

503
00:20:34,400 --> 00:20:36,670
EH, GO SEE WHAT IT IS, KID.
I'LL WAIT HERE.

504
00:20:36,703 --> 00:20:38,238
PROBABLY
THE STRONG WIND IN HERE.

505
00:20:38,272 --> 00:20:39,505
UH, THAT'S ME, SORRY.

506
00:20:39,538 --> 00:20:40,773
--ANOTHER OPENING SOMEWHERE.

507
00:20:40,807 --> 00:20:43,177
- YEAH, AN ART OPENING.
- AAH, LOOK AT THAT.

508
00:20:43,210 --> 00:20:46,045
YOU LOOK AT IT, I'M BITTER.

509
00:20:46,078 --> 00:20:47,680
OH, IT SAYS "ABANDON HOPE,

510
00:20:47,713 --> 00:20:51,318
ALL YE WHO ENTER."

511
00:20:51,352 --> 00:20:54,822
UH, DID WE COME
AT A BAD TIME?

512
00:20:54,855 --> 00:20:58,692
- EXCUSE US.
- MISTER!

513
00:20:58,725 --> 00:21:02,562
MISTER, HELP ME!
PLEASE! HELP ME!

514
00:21:02,595 --> 00:21:05,865
I GOTTA GO, KID, I'M SORRY.
I GOT A THING TO DO WITH A--

515
00:21:05,898 --> 00:21:09,035
GROWNUPS SUCK. THEY DO.

516
00:21:09,068 --> 00:21:11,772
I HATE. I HATE
BECAUSE OF THEM.

517
00:21:15,108 --> 00:21:18,312
WELL, TIE THAT YELLOW COWARD
ROUND THAT OLD OAK TREE.

518
00:21:18,345 --> 00:21:20,247
EH, CRUMMY.

519
00:21:20,280 --> 00:21:23,117
BAWK-BAWK-BAWK BAWK-BAWK.

520
00:21:23,150 --> 00:21:25,252
CHICKEN.

521
00:21:25,285 --> 00:21:27,220
WHAT-- MY LEGS!
THEY'RE HUGE!

522
00:21:27,253 --> 00:21:29,857
MY FEET ARE SWELLING!

523
00:21:29,890 --> 00:21:33,093
- WHAT'S GOING ON?
- PUT ME DOWN! PUT ME DOWN!

524
00:21:33,127 --> 00:21:34,728
WELCOME TO
THIS WEEK'S EDITION

525
00:21:34,762 --> 00:21:37,030
OF EAT THE PRESS.

526
00:21:39,767 --> 00:21:41,968
WHAT'RE WE DOING IN THIS SCENE
ALL OF A SUDDEN?

527
00:21:42,002 --> 00:21:45,405
WAIT NOW. DID YOU HEAR
SOMETHING THEN?

528
00:21:45,438 --> 00:21:47,373
- NO.
- SOUNDED LIKE A REPORTER
GETTING EATEN.

529
00:21:47,407 --> 00:21:49,608
HEY, BOSS.
DID YOU HEAR ANYTHING?

530
00:21:49,642 --> 00:21:51,845
NO, NOT A THING.

531
00:21:51,878 --> 00:21:53,280
HEY.

532
00:21:53,313 --> 00:21:55,082
YOU DON'T HAVE TO COME ALONG
IF YOU'RE SCARED.

533
00:21:55,115 --> 00:21:57,017
NO, I'LL COME ALONG TOO.

534
00:21:57,050 --> 00:21:59,218
I'M NOT SCARED.

535
00:21:59,252 --> 00:22:01,220
I DO BELIEVE IN GAOS!
I DO BELIEVE IN GAOS!

536
00:22:01,253 --> 00:22:03,157
I-DO-I-DO-I-DO-I-DO
I DO BELIEVE IN GAOS!

537
00:22:03,190 --> 00:22:05,292
I DO! I DO!

538
00:22:05,325 --> 00:22:07,860
I DO!

539
00:22:07,893 --> 00:22:10,730
BEN! BEN!

540
00:22:10,763 --> 00:22:12,998
KINDA LOOKS LIKE
CLINT HOWARD.

541
00:22:13,033 --> 00:22:14,333
I DON'T KNOW
WHERE MY FRIEND WENT,

542
00:22:14,367 --> 00:22:17,003
BUT THERE'S A PILE OF POOP HERE
WITH SHOES IN IT.

543
00:22:19,072 --> 00:22:20,907
SORRY.

544
00:22:20,940 --> 00:22:22,775
[SERVO GASPS]
WHAT'S THAT?

545
00:22:22,808 --> 00:22:25,412
I'M GUESSING HE'S THINKING
IF HE TOUCHES THAT MONSTER,

546
00:22:25,445 --> 00:22:27,413
HE'S GETTING A MERIT BADGE.

547
00:22:27,447 --> 00:22:29,348
YEP.

548
00:22:34,387 --> 00:22:36,823
HEY, LOOK! ARSENIO HALL!

549
00:22:36,857 --> 00:22:39,225
WHOOP WHOOP WHOOP!

550
00:22:39,258 --> 00:22:41,795
I CAN'T BELIEVE I'M HIDING
BEHIND A DINGLEBERRY.

551
00:22:41,828 --> 00:22:45,098
OOH.

552
00:22:45,132 --> 00:22:47,900
PEEKABOO.

553
00:22:47,933 --> 00:22:50,337
[SERVO GROWLING]
PEEKABOO.

554
00:22:50,370 --> 00:22:54,207
I SEE YOU.

555
00:22:54,240 --> 00:22:55,708
SO CUTE.

556
00:22:55,742 --> 00:22:59,078
THIS IS MY NEIGHBORHOOD.

557
00:22:59,112 --> 00:23:00,880
OOH.

558
00:23:04,150 --> 00:23:06,352
AND THAT'LL DO IT FOR
THE GROUNDBREAKING CEREMONY.

559
00:23:06,385 --> 00:23:08,822
THANK YOU VERY MUCH.

560
00:23:08,855 --> 00:23:11,692
- OOH.
- TA-DA.

561
00:23:11,725 --> 00:23:14,727
NOW I'VE CULTIVATED THE GROUND
TO A UNIFORM EIGHT INCH DEPTH.

562
00:23:14,762 --> 00:23:17,830
HELP ME! I'M ALLERGIC
TO STYROFOAM ROCKS!

563
00:23:20,900 --> 00:23:23,270
HEY-HEY-HEY!
LOVE TO EAT KIDS!

564
00:23:23,337 --> 00:23:24,972
HELP ME!

565
00:23:25,038 --> 00:23:26,940
HELP ME!

566
00:23:34,047 --> 00:23:37,050
AHH. POT-STICKERS.

567
00:23:37,050 --> 00:23:39,252
MM.

568
00:23:39,285 --> 00:23:41,555
HMM, TOO PORKY.

569
00:23:41,588 --> 00:23:43,457
I'M TRYING TO LOWER
MY CHOLESTEROL.

570
00:23:47,460 --> 00:23:51,263
OH, JUST THE THOUGHT OF FOOD
MAKES ME SLEEPY.

571
00:23:51,263 --> 00:23:52,865
[GAMERA ROARS]

572
00:23:56,503 --> 00:23:58,372
AH! GAMERA!

573
00:23:58,372 --> 00:23:59,907
HEY, THAT KID'S A TURNCOAT.

574
00:23:59,973 --> 00:24:01,475
NOW HE'S GAMERA'S PAL.

575
00:24:01,508 --> 00:24:05,412
I STICK MY NECK OUT
FOR NOBODY, KID.

576
00:24:05,478 --> 00:24:07,580
HE'S GOT THE PEZ JAW
GOING THERE.

577
00:24:07,613 --> 00:24:09,615
EVERY TIME HE SCREAMS,
A PIECE OF CANDY COMES OUT.

578
00:24:12,185 --> 00:24:13,653
UH, DON'T GET ME WRONG.

579
00:24:13,687 --> 00:24:15,855
I LIKE YOU TOO, GAOS. A LOT.

580
00:24:18,392 --> 00:24:20,127
AAH!

581
00:24:20,160 --> 00:24:23,363
LOOK AT THAT.

582
00:24:23,397 --> 00:24:26,032
THIS IS FUN! WHEE!

583
00:24:26,065 --> 00:24:28,235
HEY LOOK,
IT'S A SHOOTING RANGE.

584
00:24:32,972 --> 00:24:34,942
LOOKS LIKE SOMEBODY
GAVE GAOS A WEDGIE.

585
00:24:34,975 --> 00:24:36,910
YOU GUYS
EVER HAD A WEDGIE?

586
00:24:36,943 --> 00:24:39,245
- NO.
- IN CAMP ONCE.

587
00:24:39,278 --> 00:24:42,815
I'M COMING, DARLING.

588
00:24:42,848 --> 00:24:44,083
HUH?

589
00:24:44,117 --> 00:24:47,720
MY WINGS ARE
LIKE A SHIELD OF STEEL.

590
00:24:47,753 --> 00:24:48,988
HEY! LOOK AT THE--

591
00:24:49,022 --> 00:24:51,257
HEY, LET GO OF MY POCKET.

592
00:24:51,290 --> 00:24:53,627
HELP ME!

593
00:24:53,660 --> 00:24:56,597
HE'S NO FAY WRAY, IS HE?

594
00:24:59,398 --> 00:25:02,002
OH, WE GOTTA
GET OUT OF HERE.

595
00:25:02,035 --> 00:25:04,603
I GOTTA LAUGH.
WE DO HAVE FUN.

596
00:25:17,450 --> 00:25:20,020
OKAY, I'M FEELING REALLY
ARTSY-CRAFTSY TODAY.

597
00:25:20,053 --> 00:25:21,688
KIND OF CAPTAIN KANGAROONY

598
00:25:21,722 --> 00:25:23,122
AND A LITTLE RAY RAYNER-ISH

599
00:25:23,155 --> 00:25:26,058
AND FOXFIRE THROWN IN
JUST FOR GOOD MEASURE.

600
00:25:26,092 --> 00:25:27,860
ANYWAY. I'M GONNA
TEACH YOU TODAY

601
00:25:27,893 --> 00:25:30,530
HOW TO MAKE TODAY'S
STAR OF THE FILM, GAOS.

602
00:25:30,563 --> 00:25:32,665
AND HE'S GONNA LOOK
JUST LIKE THIS WHEN
WE'RE FINISHED.

603
00:25:32,698 --> 00:25:34,833
I GUESS I'M MORE OF
A HEC RAMSEY FAN,

604
00:25:34,867 --> 00:25:36,268
BUT THAT'S JUST ME.
AND I KNOW

605
00:25:36,302 --> 00:25:38,103
YOU'RE A BIG
SNOOP SISTERS FAN.

606
00:25:38,137 --> 00:25:40,207
OH, NO, ACTUALLY
I'VE ALWAYS LOVED BANACEK.

607
00:25:40,240 --> 00:25:42,108
OH, CALL IT
A GUILTY PLEASURE.

608
00:25:42,142 --> 00:25:43,677
HEY-- DO YOU GUYS MIND?

609
00:25:43,710 --> 00:25:45,345
OH, NOT AT ALL, JOEL.
TOSS IN.

610
00:25:45,378 --> 00:25:47,280
YEAH, BUT LET ME GUESS.
YOU'RE A McMILLAN AND WIFE FAN,

611
00:25:47,313 --> 00:25:48,915
- AREN'T YOU?
- YOU GUYS ARE
GETTING IN THE WAY

612
00:25:48,948 --> 00:25:50,983
OF MY ARTS AND CRAFTS
PROJECT.

613
00:25:51,017 --> 00:25:53,453
OH, WELL,
JOEL, YOU JUST GO ON

614
00:25:53,487 --> 00:25:56,488
WITH YOUR LITTLE CRAFTSY-WAFTSY
HOLLY HOBBY CORNER

615
00:25:56,522 --> 00:25:59,058
- AND NEVERMIND US CHICKENS.
- [SERVO BAWKS]

616
00:25:59,092 --> 00:26:00,960
ANYWAY, WHAT YOU'RE
GONNA NEED, EVERYONE,

617
00:26:00,993 --> 00:26:03,930
IS SOME SCISSORS
WITH THE ROUNDED EDGE.

618
00:26:03,963 --> 00:26:05,498
- USE SMALLER ONES.
- [BOTS WHISPER]

619
00:26:05,532 --> 00:26:07,000
ALSO, PASTE.

620
00:26:07,033 --> 00:26:09,035
I'M USING MUCILAGE
THOUGH, TODAY,

621
00:26:09,068 --> 00:26:11,938
BECAUSE I'M AN ADULT,
AND YOU'RE NOT.

622
00:26:11,972 --> 00:26:13,773
AND THEN WE'LL NEED AN 8X8

623
00:26:13,807 --> 00:26:15,208
PERFECTLY SQUARE
PIECE OF PAPER.

624
00:26:15,242 --> 00:26:18,077
I'M USING ONE THAT'S
A LITTLE BIGGER FOR CLARITY.

625
00:26:18,110 --> 00:26:20,513
NOW YOU'RE ALSO GOING TO NEED
SOME POWDERED RHINO HORN!

626
00:26:20,547 --> 00:26:23,082
YEAH, AND SOME BLOOD THAT'S FROM
THE MURDERER'S GIBBET SWEAT!

627
00:26:23,115 --> 00:26:25,418
- RIGHT! ASK YOUR MOM FIRST.
- YEAH, GOOD ONE.

628
00:26:25,452 --> 00:26:28,455
ANYWAY, WHAT YOU DO IS
YOU JUST TAKE THE FOUR CORNERS,

629
00:26:28,488 --> 00:26:30,090
AND YOU FOLD 'EM IN,
JUST LIKE THAT.

630
00:26:30,123 --> 00:26:31,692
IT'S SIMPLE.

631
00:26:31,725 --> 00:26:33,393
OH, AND WHILE
HE'S DOING THAT,

632
00:26:33,427 --> 00:26:35,128
YOU MIGHT WANT TO RUN DOWN
TO THE PUBLIC LIBRARY

633
00:26:35,162 --> 00:26:37,763
AND CUT OUT SOME INTERESTING
PICTURES FROM THE ENCYCLOPEDIA

634
00:26:37,797 --> 00:26:39,032
TO PASTE ON YOUR PROJECT.

635
00:26:39,065 --> 00:26:40,533
YEAH, AND IN CASE
YOU'RE INTERESTED,

636
00:26:40,567 --> 00:26:43,235
MUCILAGE TASTES
JUST LIKE SWEET HONEY.

637
00:26:43,268 --> 00:26:45,472
YOU GUYS, PLEASE DO NOT--

638
00:26:45,505 --> 00:26:47,840
I REPEAT, DO NOT GO DOWN
TO THE PUBLIC LIBRARY

639
00:26:47,873 --> 00:26:49,908
AND DO NOT CUT PICTURES
OUT OF THE ENCYCLOPEDIA

640
00:26:49,942 --> 00:26:52,278
AND DO NOT DRINK MUCILAGE.

641
00:26:52,312 --> 00:26:54,213
FOR IT DOES NOT TASTE
LIKE SWEET HONEY.

642
00:26:54,247 --> 00:26:55,848
FROM ONE WHO KNOWS.

643
00:26:55,882 --> 00:26:58,718
OKAY, THEN YOU TAKE--
YOU TURN THE WHOLE THING OVER.

644
00:26:58,752 --> 00:26:59,885
SEE, I'VE TURNED IT OVER--

645
00:26:59,918 --> 00:27:01,287
WELL, IF YOU GET
CONFUSED AT HOME,

646
00:27:01,320 --> 00:27:03,323
JUST DRAW A LITTLE DIAGRAM
ON YOUR BEDROOM WALL

647
00:27:03,357 --> 00:27:04,923
IN PERMANENT MARKER.

648
00:27:04,957 --> 00:27:06,458
DO NOT-- I REPEAT,

649
00:27:06,492 --> 00:27:08,928
DO NOT DRAW
ON YOUR BEDROOM WALL.

650
00:27:08,962 --> 00:27:11,597
YOU PUT THE FOUR EDGES IN
LIKE THIS.

651
00:27:11,630 --> 00:27:13,967
- YOU WHIP YOUR FINGERS
IN THERE LIKE THIS.
- WHAT'RE YOU DOING?

652
00:27:14,000 --> 00:27:17,037
AND YOU GOT GAOS.
SEE? CHECK IT OUT--

653
00:27:17,070 --> 00:27:19,705
AND IF IT DOESN'T LIKE THAT,
YOU'RE A LOSER AND A FAILURE,

654
00:27:19,738 --> 00:27:20,940
AND YOU'LL NEVER
AMOUNT TO ANYTHING.

655
00:27:20,973 --> 00:27:22,808
AND YOU CAN'T DO A THING
TO CHANGE THAT.

656
00:27:22,842 --> 00:27:25,145
TOM? TOM?

657
00:27:25,178 --> 00:27:27,013
- TOM, CAN I TELL YOU
SOMETHING?
- HUH?

658
00:27:27,047 --> 00:27:28,682
YOU GET A TIME-OUT
COMING, BUDDY.

659
00:27:28,715 --> 00:27:30,550
NO, JOEL!
PLEASE, I'M JUST A ROBOT.

660
00:27:30,583 --> 00:27:32,318
[SERVO MUTTERS]

661
00:27:32,352 --> 00:27:34,020
UH-OH, UH, COMMERCIAL SIGN.

662
00:27:34,053 --> 00:27:35,955
JOEL? JOEL?

663
00:27:35,988 --> 00:27:38,958
- YEAH?
- UH, IT'S COMMERCIAL SIGN.

664
00:27:38,992 --> 00:27:40,960
- SHOULD I GET IT?
- YEAH.

665
00:27:40,993 --> 00:27:43,028
OKAY.

666
00:27:46,465 --> 00:27:49,035
HEY KIDS. THE WORD FOR TODAY

667
00:27:49,068 --> 00:27:50,503
IS "BOOGER."

668
00:27:50,537 --> 00:27:51,772
YEAH, THAT'S RIGHT.
BOOGER!

669
00:27:51,805 --> 00:27:53,840
BOOGER-BOOGER-BOOGER
BOOGER-BOOGER-- WHAH-HOW!

670
00:28:01,347 --> 00:28:03,517
I DON'T WANT ANY MORE
CLOWNING AROUND.

671
00:28:03,550 --> 00:28:05,518
- NOW YOU SIT DOWN.
- I'M SORRY.

672
00:28:05,552 --> 00:28:08,488
- OW.
- EW, PRIMORDIAL OOZE.

673
00:28:08,522 --> 00:28:09,788
OOH.

674
00:28:09,822 --> 00:28:12,625
YEESH.

675
00:28:12,658 --> 00:28:16,028
HE'S GOT RELIEF FROM HIS MONTHLY
BLOATING, THOUGH, DOESN'T HE?

676
00:28:16,062 --> 00:28:19,498
OKAY, OKAY, RUB SALT IN IT,
WHY DON'T YOU?

677
00:28:21,700 --> 00:28:24,770
- OW! OKAY, ALREADY!
- WE GET THE POINT.

678
00:28:24,803 --> 00:28:27,607
LET'S CHANGE HIS NAME
FROM GAOS TO "GINSU."

679
00:28:30,410 --> 00:28:32,578
COME ON. IT TAKES
A REAL TURTLE TO CRY, GAMERA.

680
00:28:32,612 --> 00:28:35,948
LET IT OUT!

681
00:28:35,982 --> 00:28:38,250
IT'S TURNING INTO
AN ARTICHOKE.

682
00:28:40,018 --> 00:28:41,687
IT'S AN OREO COOKIE.

683
00:28:44,357 --> 00:28:46,993
OOH.

684
00:28:47,027 --> 00:28:50,430
NOW I LIKE GAMERA!

685
00:28:52,532 --> 00:28:56,068
OOH BOY.

686
00:28:56,102 --> 00:28:59,205
I'D LIKE A BROMO, PLEASE.

687
00:29:01,707 --> 00:29:04,343
OH, YOU HAD THE GARLIC
CHEESE PUFFS, DIDN'T YOU?

688
00:29:04,377 --> 00:29:07,080
BOO!

689
00:29:07,113 --> 00:29:08,482
EH, FORGET AGENT ORANGE.

690
00:29:08,515 --> 00:29:10,783
I'LL SHOW YOU
HOW TO DEFOLIATE A FOREST.

691
00:29:10,817 --> 00:29:14,653
[SERVO CHUCKLES]

692
00:29:14,687 --> 00:29:16,055
HEY, IF YOU CAN'T
STAND THE HEAT,

693
00:29:16,088 --> 00:29:19,692
GET OUT OF THE MOVIE.

694
00:29:19,725 --> 00:29:21,928
HEY LOOK, GAMERA HAS
EIICHI PALMS NOW.

695
00:29:21,962 --> 00:29:25,198
I GET IT.

696
00:29:25,232 --> 00:29:27,300
HEY, WHERE'S THAT HAND BEEN?

697
00:29:27,333 --> 00:29:29,868
EW. UNFORTUNATE SKIN.

698
00:29:29,902 --> 00:29:33,005
OH YEAH, EIICHI'S GONNA BE SAFE
ON GAMERA'S BACK, ISN'T HE?

699
00:29:37,077 --> 00:29:39,145
HE'S GOT A WEAK BACK.

700
00:29:39,178 --> 00:29:41,113
[SERVO MUTTERS]

701
00:29:41,147 --> 00:29:42,915
ATOMIC BATTERIES TO POWER.

702
00:29:42,948 --> 00:29:44,017
TURBINES TO SPEED.

703
00:29:44,050 --> 00:29:46,920
ROGER. READY TO MOVE OUT.

704
00:29:46,953 --> 00:29:49,888
I FORGOT,
I'M A HAND PUPPET.

705
00:29:49,922 --> 00:29:53,358
YOU KNOW, THIS HIGH-DEFINITION
TV IS REALLY SOMETHING.

706
00:29:53,392 --> 00:29:55,027
[SERVO GASPS]
HEY!

707
00:29:55,060 --> 00:29:56,528
GET THE COLEMAN PEOPLE
ON THE PHONE.

708
00:29:56,562 --> 00:29:59,498
I'VE GOT A GREAT IDEA!

709
00:30:02,035 --> 00:30:03,770
HEY, IT'S TURTLE A LA KING.

710
00:30:03,803 --> 00:30:05,305
TURTLE ALAN KING?

711
00:30:05,338 --> 00:30:07,407
A STUDENT OF THE...

712
00:30:07,440 --> 00:30:09,708
I'M TRIPPING, BIG TIME.

713
00:30:09,742 --> 00:30:11,343
OOH.

714
00:30:11,377 --> 00:30:12,978
OKAY, HERE'S WHERE
YOU GET OFF, KENNY.

715
00:30:13,012 --> 00:30:15,615
I MEAN, EIICHI.

716
00:30:15,648 --> 00:30:18,283
WE'VE GOT TO DO SOMETHING
NOW. GET THE OTHERS.

717
00:30:18,317 --> 00:30:21,922
HEY, WHAT'S A GUY GOTTA DO
TO GET A YELLOW HELMET
AROUND HERE?

718
00:30:21,955 --> 00:30:23,890
HURRY OUT.

719
00:30:29,595 --> 00:30:32,832
I'M HUNGRY. LET'S STOP
AND GET A PIZZA.

720
00:30:32,865 --> 00:30:34,233
WHEE.

721
00:30:34,267 --> 00:30:36,202
GAMERA, TAKE ME HOME NOW.

722
00:30:36,235 --> 00:30:38,470
ALL RIGHT,
THE METER'S RUNNING, KID.

723
00:30:38,503 --> 00:30:41,773
AROUND THE PARK, PLEASE.

724
00:30:41,807 --> 00:30:43,910
HEY, HEY, BIG TROUBLE!
TROUBLE--

725
00:30:43,943 --> 00:30:45,478
IN LITTLE CHINA!

726
00:30:45,512 --> 00:30:47,380
YOU REAL MEN CAN LOOK AFTER
YOUR OWN TROUBLES.

727
00:30:47,413 --> 00:30:50,783
IT'S RONALD COLMAN!

728
00:30:50,817 --> 00:30:52,918
COME ON, LET'S GO!

729
00:30:52,952 --> 00:30:56,722
EH, EXCUSE ME, I JUST GOTTA MATE
WITH THE TILT-A-WHIRL THERE.

730
00:30:56,755 --> 00:30:59,292
HEY, CAME OUT OF THE SLOT.
IT NEEDS A PUSH.

731
00:30:59,325 --> 00:31:01,560
OH, NOW THEY'RE IN
THE LAND OF MAKE-BELIEVE.

732
00:31:01,593 --> 00:31:04,597
HI. WE'RE BIG AGAIN NOW.

733
00:31:08,167 --> 00:31:11,337
WHAT IS THIS,
A CHINESE FIRE DRILL?

734
00:31:11,370 --> 00:31:14,240
I'M JUST STARTING TO COME OUT
OF MY SHELL, I THINK.

735
00:31:14,273 --> 00:31:16,242
THAT'S WHAT I DO.

736
00:31:16,275 --> 00:31:19,112
- EIICHI!
- EIICHI!

737
00:31:19,145 --> 00:31:21,413
- EIICHI!
- EIICHI!

738
00:31:21,447 --> 00:31:23,315
- KENNY! KENNY!
- EIICHI!

739
00:31:23,348 --> 00:31:25,885
- EIICHI!
- EIICHI!

740
00:31:25,918 --> 00:31:27,687
HI, WE GOT A DEAL.

741
00:31:27,720 --> 00:31:31,490
I SCRATCH HIS BACK,
HE SCRATCHES MINE.

742
00:31:31,523 --> 00:31:33,525
OOH. YOU KNOW,
GAMERA COULD USE

743
00:31:33,558 --> 00:31:35,862
A LITTLE EXFOLIATING HERE.

744
00:31:35,895 --> 00:31:38,665
GOT A SKIN FUNGUS
GOING DOWN.

745
00:31:40,165 --> 00:31:42,968
- SPIDER-BOY.
- NO, FROG-BOY.

746
00:31:43,002 --> 00:31:45,137
NO, HE'S A TICK.

747
00:31:45,170 --> 00:31:48,507
MATCH ON HIM.

748
00:31:48,540 --> 00:31:51,510
LISTEN! DON'T MOVE!

749
00:31:51,543 --> 00:31:53,813
OKAY, MOVE!

750
00:31:53,847 --> 00:31:56,815
[GAMERA GROWLS]

751
00:31:58,785 --> 00:32:00,487
THE WHEEL!

752
00:32:00,520 --> 00:32:04,257
THEY'RE GONNA
INVENT THE WHEEL!

753
00:32:04,290 --> 00:32:08,060
THIS-- I THOUGHT THIS WAS
FERRIS WHEEL'S DAY OFF.

754
00:32:13,298 --> 00:32:16,935
YOU THINK GAMERA LIKES
BEING THE SIZE OF THE PENTAGON?

755
00:32:16,970 --> 00:32:18,905
DON'T EVER CHANGE.
YOU'RE BEAUTIFUL AS IS.

756
00:32:18,938 --> 00:32:21,207
STOP, STOP!

757
00:32:21,240 --> 00:32:23,608
♪ STOP THE WORLD,
I WANT TO GET OFF ♪

758
00:32:23,643 --> 00:32:26,645
SERVO, I WARNED YOU ABOUT
DOING ANTHONY NEWLEY.

759
00:32:26,678 --> 00:32:28,247
- NOW STOP.
- OKAY.

760
00:32:28,280 --> 00:32:30,583
NOT YOU, GAMERA. THE KID.

761
00:32:32,552 --> 00:32:35,087
NOW, COME ON.

762
00:32:35,120 --> 00:32:38,490
OH, YOU'VE GOTTEN HEAVY.

763
00:32:38,523 --> 00:32:40,393
RIGHT! TAKE IT AWAY.

764
00:32:40,427 --> 00:32:43,830
[BOTS HUM CARNIVAL MUSIC]

765
00:32:51,037 --> 00:32:53,138
LIKE I LIVE TO SERVE YOU.

766
00:32:53,172 --> 00:32:56,142
I'M OUTTA HERE.
JEEZ, WHAT A GIG.

767
00:32:57,577 --> 00:32:59,845
THIS MUSIC IS SO SAD.

768
00:33:01,747 --> 00:33:03,382
GAMERA?

769
00:33:03,415 --> 00:33:05,250
I KNOW, I KNOW,
I'VE GOT A GOOD HEART,

770
00:33:05,283 --> 00:33:06,885
AND I LOVE CHILDREN.

771
00:33:06,918 --> 00:33:08,220
BLAH BLAH BLAH.

772
00:33:08,253 --> 00:33:10,322
- SOMEDAY I'M JUST GONNA...
- [GAMERA SCREAMS]

773
00:33:10,357 --> 00:33:13,793
HEY, WHO INVITED
THE ELEPHANT?

774
00:33:16,428 --> 00:33:17,997
I GUESS THAT'S "IRRELEPHANT."

775
00:33:18,030 --> 00:33:20,433
- DA-DUM.
- THAT STUNG.

776
00:33:20,467 --> 00:33:22,168
HERE, TAKE THE BOY.

777
00:33:22,202 --> 00:33:23,435
YEAH, I'LL TAKE HIM.

778
00:33:23,468 --> 00:33:25,538
HE'S MINE. I SAW HIM FIRST.

779
00:33:25,572 --> 00:33:28,842
HEY, HE'S TAKING OFF!

780
00:33:28,875 --> 00:33:32,545
[PEOPLE CLAMOR]

781
00:33:32,578 --> 00:33:34,547
AND AS I FLEW OFF THAT DAY,

782
00:33:34,580 --> 00:33:37,417
I REALIZED I HAD
BECOME A MAN.

783
00:33:40,687 --> 00:33:41,920
THANKS A LOT, GAMERA.

784
00:33:41,953 --> 00:33:43,688
HA-HAH,
WAVE LIKE AN IDIOT, KENNY.

785
00:33:43,723 --> 00:33:45,858
I MEAN "EIICHI."
GAH, I CAN'T KEEP 'EM APART.

786
00:33:45,892 --> 00:33:47,327
I KNOW WHAT YOU MEAN.

787
00:33:47,360 --> 00:33:49,995
EIICHI, ARE YOU
ALL RIGHT, MY BOY?

788
00:33:50,028 --> 00:33:52,698
YES I AM, I'M FINE.
GAMERA GAVE ME A RIDE.

789
00:33:52,732 --> 00:33:54,233
YEAH, WELL COME ON.
TELL US ALL ABOUT IT.

790
00:33:54,267 --> 00:33:57,503
TEAR HIS COAT OFF, QUICK!

791
00:33:57,537 --> 00:34:01,340
HEY LOOK. PICNIC STICK SICK.

792
00:34:01,373 --> 00:34:04,110
AH, BIL KEANE LET BILLY
DRAW THE STRIP TODAY.

793
00:34:06,278 --> 00:34:08,247
EIICHI'S HOUSE.
PLEASE HOLD, THANK YOU.

794
00:34:08,280 --> 00:34:10,382
EIICHI'S HOUSE, MAY I HELP YOU?
EIICHI'S HOUSE, HOLD PLEASE.

795
00:34:10,417 --> 00:34:13,385
GAOS IS VERY BAD.
HE CAN SHOOT OUT A RAY.

796
00:34:13,418 --> 00:34:15,955
YESTERDAY HE HURT
GAMERA'S LEG WITH THE RAY.

797
00:34:15,988 --> 00:34:18,423
IT CUT HIM VERY DEEP.
JUST LIKE A BIG KNIFE.

798
00:34:18,457 --> 00:34:20,292
I DON'T BELIEVE IT.
SUDDENLY THE KID'S

799
00:34:20,325 --> 00:34:22,495
AN AUTHORITY ON EVERYTHING.

800
00:34:22,528 --> 00:34:25,363
MM. BECAUSE HIS VOICE
SOUNDS LIKE THAT.

801
00:34:25,397 --> 00:34:27,333
IT SOUNDS AS IF
HE SCREAMS "GAOS."

802
00:34:27,367 --> 00:34:29,035
NOW, GIVE ME
MORE LICORICE STICKS.

803
00:34:29,068 --> 00:34:31,970
DR. AOKI, AS A ZOOLOGIST,
WHAT WOULD YOU SAY THE BEAST IS?

804
00:34:32,003 --> 00:34:34,540
WELL, I'D HAVE TO DEFER
TO EIICHI ON THIS ONE.

805
00:34:34,573 --> 00:34:36,975
WOULD YOU SAY IT'S A BIRD,
OR IS IT A REPTILE?

806
00:34:37,008 --> 00:34:39,412
I WOULD LIKE TO SAY. THERE ISN'T
ANY RECORDED HISTORY OF IT.

807
00:34:39,445 --> 00:34:41,513
LET'S JUST CALL IT
A MONSTER.

808
00:34:41,547 --> 00:34:43,048
I LIKE IT. IT'S SNAPPY.

809
00:34:43,082 --> 00:34:44,717
WHAT ABOUT THIS SPECIAL RAY?

810
00:34:44,750 --> 00:34:47,953
NOW, IS THERE ANY SORT OF ANIMAL
THAT COULD PRODUCE THIS RAY?

811
00:34:47,987 --> 00:34:49,422
THERE BE
SOME SORT OF REASON.

812
00:34:49,455 --> 00:34:51,690
MM. I DO HAVE
A LITTLE DATA ON THIS.

813
00:34:51,723 --> 00:34:53,758
UH, EIICHI DID
AN ETCH-A-SKETCH.

814
00:34:54,927 --> 00:34:56,362
DID HE JUST TEAR HIS SHORTS?

815
00:34:56,395 --> 00:34:59,298
...SUPERSONIC CUTTER.

816
00:34:59,332 --> 00:35:00,767
IT WORKS THROUGH
SOUND WAVES OSCILLATING

817
00:35:00,800 --> 00:35:02,000
IN THE REGION
OF 20,000 CYCLES.

818
00:35:02,033 --> 00:35:03,368
WELL ABOVE
THE RANGE OF HUMANS.

819
00:35:03,402 --> 00:35:05,437
NOW HERE'S LUCY AND VIV
AT THE CHOCOLATE FACTORY.

820
00:35:05,472 --> 00:35:07,307
THIS COULD BE USED IN SURGERY
FOR PARTICULAR JOBS

821
00:35:07,340 --> 00:35:09,108
WHERE A SCALPEL
WOULD BE UNSUITABLE.

822
00:35:09,142 --> 00:35:11,310
A PULSED OSCILLATION
PRODUCES THE WAVES.

823
00:35:11,343 --> 00:35:12,778
THEN THEY'RE BEAMED
TO A METAL PLATE.

824
00:35:12,812 --> 00:35:14,547
- THEN KABOOM.
- AT THIS STAGE,
THEY'RE QUITE WEAK.

825
00:35:14,580 --> 00:35:16,815
SO THEY MUST BE AMPLIFIED
AND MORE IMPORTANTLY

826
00:35:16,848 --> 00:35:18,417
MUST BE CONCENTRATED.

827
00:35:18,450 --> 00:35:20,587
I'LL LEAVE
SPACE FOR LAUGH HERE.

828
00:35:20,620 --> 00:35:21,853
AND THAT'S THE THEORY.

829
00:35:21,887 --> 00:35:23,857
ONCE THE SOUND WAVES
HAVE BEEN AMPLIFIED,

830
00:35:23,890 --> 00:35:26,558
WELL, THEN, THEY BECOME
A VERY POTENT ENERGY.

831
00:35:26,592 --> 00:35:28,828
- POTENT.
- OSCILLATING AT
NINE MILLION CYCLES.

832
00:35:28,862 --> 00:35:31,530
THEY CAN BE USED
TO A VERY DESTRUCTIVE EFFECT.

833
00:35:31,563 --> 00:35:33,833
- OOPS.
- MY THEORY ABOUT THIS IS

834
00:35:33,867 --> 00:35:36,602
THE MONSTER'S RAYS
ARE PRODUCED THE SAME WAY.

835
00:35:36,635 --> 00:35:38,570
IT'S JUST A THEORY.

836
00:35:38,603 --> 00:35:41,040
EIICHI, WHAT DO YOU THINK?

837
00:35:41,073 --> 00:35:43,042
IN ANY CASE, WE HAVE
TO PROCEED FROM SOME THEORY.

838
00:35:43,075 --> 00:35:45,310
AND IT'S THE ONLY ONE
THAT WE HAVE RIGHT NOW.

839
00:35:45,343 --> 00:35:47,413
YOU'RE PERHAPS WONDERING
ABOUT THE MECHANISM

840
00:35:47,447 --> 00:35:48,813
THAT PRODUCES THESE RAYS.

841
00:35:48,848 --> 00:35:50,583
- WELL--
- I LIKE IT!

842
00:35:50,617 --> 00:35:52,852
ALL THE GIRLS WILL
BE WEARING IT IN NO TIME.

843
00:35:52,885 --> 00:35:56,322
- [ALL SHOUT]
- OOH. [WHISTLES]
NOW THAT'S SCARY.

844
00:35:56,355 --> 00:35:58,623
I FEEL LIKE
I GOT X-RAY SPECS.

845
00:35:58,657 --> 00:36:00,693
--AND THEN HIGHLY AMPLIFIED
IN THE OTHER.

846
00:36:00,727 --> 00:36:02,395
- OH, LIKE QUAD.
- MM-HMM.

847
00:36:02,428 --> 00:36:04,697
THE NECK AND THE SPINE
MUST ALSO BE FORKED.

848
00:36:04,730 --> 00:36:06,198
THIS IS THEN USED
AS AN OSCILLATOR.

849
00:36:06,232 --> 00:36:08,433
- [SERVO HUMS TONE]
- REFLECTED FROM A PLATE
IN THE MOUTH,

850
00:36:08,467 --> 00:36:09,868
THERE'S YOUR BEAM.

851
00:36:09,902 --> 00:36:12,472
THEN YOU MUST BE PRETTY SURE
THE MONSTER HAS TWO THROATS.

852
00:36:12,505 --> 00:36:14,707
- WHO SAID THAT?
- OH YES, I AM.

853
00:36:14,740 --> 00:36:15,908
WOULDN'T THIS
TEND TO RESTRICT

854
00:36:15,942 --> 00:36:17,610
THE MOVEMENT
OF THE MONSTER'S HEAD?

855
00:36:17,643 --> 00:36:19,478
[ALL]
SIT DOWN. COME ON.

856
00:36:19,512 --> 00:36:21,480
IT DIDN'T TURN ITS HEAD
WHILE IT WAS BEING ATTACKED.

857
00:36:21,513 --> 00:36:24,017
WELL, THAT'S A WEAKNESS
WE COULD USE TO ADVANTAGE.

858
00:36:24,050 --> 00:36:26,818
IF WE COULD ARRANGE IN SOME WAY
FOR IT TO BE DISTRACTED,

859
00:36:26,852 --> 00:36:28,720
WE COULD ATTACK IT
WITH SAFETY FROM THE REAR.

860
00:36:28,753 --> 00:36:31,790
- MM-HMM.
- DR. AOKI, TELL ME.

861
00:36:31,823 --> 00:36:33,725
WHAT DO YOU THINK
THIS GREEN GLOW IS?

862
00:36:33,758 --> 00:36:35,895
WELL, I'M ONLY GUESSING.
A SIGN OF HUNGER

863
00:36:35,928 --> 00:36:38,497
- OR PERHAPS A SIGN OF RAGE.
- OR A SIGN OF ENVY.

864
00:36:38,530 --> 00:36:40,465
THIS IS NOT ESPECIALLY NEW
IN THE ANIMAL WORLD.

865
00:36:40,498 --> 00:36:43,235
A NUMBER OF FISH SPECIES
HAVE A SIMILAR THING, TOO.

866
00:36:43,268 --> 00:36:44,970
BUT STILL,
WHY SHOULD THE MONSTER

867
00:36:45,003 --> 00:36:46,505
CHOOSE TO MAKE
AN APPEARANCE NOW?

868
00:36:46,538 --> 00:36:48,073
- GRANDPA.
- HE MUST SURELY
HAVE BEEN HIDING SOMEWHERE

869
00:36:48,107 --> 00:36:49,408
DEEP DOWN IN
THE BOWELS OF THE EARTH

870
00:36:49,442 --> 00:36:51,077
FOR HUNDREDS
OF THOUSANDS OF YEARS.

871
00:36:51,110 --> 00:36:52,612
- ICK.
- THAT'S RIGHT.

872
00:36:52,645 --> 00:36:55,513
- PULL MY BEARD.
- --UNDISTURBED BY
THE TWO RECENT ERUPTIONS.

873
00:36:55,547 --> 00:36:58,017
- WOKEN FROM--
- HI, DAVE.

874
00:36:58,050 --> 00:36:59,352
IT COULD WELL HAVE BEEN
TRAPPED IN SOME

875
00:36:59,385 --> 00:37:01,653
DEEP SUBTERRANEAN
AIR CAVITY.

876
00:37:01,687 --> 00:37:03,488
BUT ONE THING I KNOW.

877
00:37:03,522 --> 00:37:05,692
WE MUST FIND SOME WAY
OF DESTROYING IT.

878
00:37:05,725 --> 00:37:07,260
IT'S DEMONSTRATED
ITS VICIOUSNESS.

879
00:37:07,293 --> 00:37:08,995
IT'S A VICIOUS GOSSIP.

880
00:37:09,028 --> 00:37:10,062
I HATE TO THINK
WHAT WOULD HAPPEN IF

881
00:37:10,095 --> 00:37:11,763
IT CHOSE TO ATTACK THE CITY.

882
00:37:11,797 --> 00:37:14,400
- WE MUST GET RID OF IT.
- GOOD PLAN.

883
00:37:14,433 --> 00:37:17,703
SO PLEASE. ARRANGE
TO DESTROY THE BEAST.

884
00:37:17,737 --> 00:37:19,738
- YES, I'LL DO THAT.
- ON MY WAY HOME.

885
00:37:19,772 --> 00:37:22,240
RIGHT. ALL THE PLANES ARE
STANDING BY, SIR.

886
00:37:22,275 --> 00:37:24,110
GOOD. GO AHEAD.

887
00:37:24,143 --> 00:37:25,477
ROGER.

888
00:37:25,510 --> 00:37:27,212
GO AHEAD.

889
00:37:27,245 --> 00:37:29,382
CALLING "A" SQUADRON!
CALLING "A" SQUADRON!

890
00:37:29,415 --> 00:37:31,583
TAKE OFF NOW!
ATTACK TO PROCEED NOW!

891
00:37:31,617 --> 00:37:33,485
ATTACK TO PROCEED NOW!

892
00:37:33,518 --> 00:37:35,053
THIS IS OUR MILITARY?

893
00:37:35,087 --> 00:37:36,522
OH MY GOD.

894
00:37:36,555 --> 00:37:38,290
OH. THERE'S
THE GREEN GLOW AGAIN.

895
00:37:38,323 --> 00:37:39,792
OH, MARILYN CHAMBERS--

896
00:37:39,825 --> 00:37:42,027
I WASN'T
SUPPOSED TO KNOW THAT.

897
00:37:49,468 --> 00:37:51,303
- IT'S A POCKET
OF LUNG DISEASE.
- EWW.

898
00:37:51,337 --> 00:37:53,973
WAIT A MINUTE,
HE'S MAKING POPCORN UP THERE.

899
00:37:54,007 --> 00:37:57,743
[PLANES SCREECH]

900
00:37:57,777 --> 00:37:59,978
RANDOM BOMBING
SHOULD DO THE TRICK.

901
00:38:00,012 --> 00:38:01,913
MM-HMM.

902
00:38:04,217 --> 00:38:06,918
I THINK WE SHOULD DO
A FRONTAL ATTACK FIRST, SIR.

903
00:38:11,890 --> 00:38:14,460
EH, THOSE ARE THE GREEN RIDGE
MOUNTAINS UP THERE.

904
00:38:17,062 --> 00:38:19,532
DOING IT UP, AREN'T THEY?

905
00:38:19,565 --> 00:38:22,000
AHH.

906
00:38:22,033 --> 00:38:25,370
NOW, REGRETTABLY, THERE'S BOUND
TO BE SOME COLLATERAL DAMAGE.

907
00:38:25,403 --> 00:38:26,638
OOH!
CAN YOU IMAGINE

908
00:38:26,672 --> 00:38:28,673
WHAT THAT THING
COULD DO FOR CATARACTS?

909
00:38:28,707 --> 00:38:30,642
WELL, THAT'S WHAT
THE JAPANESE EYE DOCTOR DRIVES.

910
00:38:30,677 --> 00:38:32,345
A CATARACT.

911
00:38:32,378 --> 00:38:34,313
I SAID I WOULD STAY HERE.

912
00:38:34,347 --> 00:38:36,015
THAT WAS WORSE
THAN ANTHONY NEWLEY.

913
00:38:36,048 --> 00:38:38,083
- DAMN.
- THIS IS GREAT!

914
00:38:38,117 --> 00:38:39,585
GET MARKETING, PRONTO!

915
00:38:39,618 --> 00:38:42,153
YES, SIR.

916
00:38:42,187 --> 00:38:44,823
PLANES JUST DON'T
STAND A CHANCE WITH THAT.

917
00:38:44,857 --> 00:38:46,958
WE'LL HAVE TO THINK
OF AN ALTERNATIVE IDEA.

918
00:38:46,992 --> 00:38:49,328
THIS IS JUST PLAIN MURDER.

919
00:38:49,362 --> 00:38:52,263
I WISH GAMERA WOULD
COME BACK HERE AGAIN.

920
00:38:52,297 --> 00:38:54,733
THAT'S IT!
EIICHI, I LOVE YOU!

921
00:38:54,767 --> 00:38:56,935
LET'S GET OUR LITTLE TUB-BALL
AN ICE CREAM SUNDAE,

922
00:38:56,968 --> 00:38:58,803
- WHAT DO YOU SAY?
- HE'S GONE TO THE BOTTOM
OF THE SEA AND STAY THERE

923
00:38:58,837 --> 00:39:00,405
UNTIL HIS LEG GETS BETTER.

924
00:39:00,438 --> 00:39:03,642
I WISH TO PLAY
WITH CLAY NOW.

925
00:39:03,675 --> 00:39:07,413
I'M ACTUALLY A TINY TIME PILL,
YOU REALIZE.

926
00:39:07,447 --> 00:39:09,315
GAMERA! JUST HURRY UP

927
00:39:09,348 --> 00:39:11,483
AND GET WELL AGAIN, GAMERA!

928
00:39:11,517 --> 00:39:13,452
AND GET PLENTY OF REST
AND DRINK PLENTY OF FLUIDS

929
00:39:13,485 --> 00:39:16,055
AND TAKE TWO ASPIRINS.

930
00:39:16,088 --> 00:39:17,390
GAMERA!

931
00:39:17,423 --> 00:39:18,890
[GURGLING] EIICHI!

932
00:39:18,923 --> 00:39:20,158
GAMERA!

933
00:39:20,192 --> 00:39:23,195
[GURGLING] EIICHI!

934
00:39:23,228 --> 00:39:25,230
[GURGLING] KENNY!

935
00:39:25,263 --> 00:39:28,267
OH, YOU KNOW, YOU SHOULD USE
A LITTLE PEROXIDE ON THAT.

936
00:39:28,267 --> 00:39:29,568
A LITTLE NEOSPORIN WOULD DO.

937
00:39:29,602 --> 00:39:32,203
DON'T PICK AT IT EITHER.
YOU DO NOT WANT TO DO THAT.

938
00:39:32,270 --> 00:39:34,873
- HURRY UP AND GET WELL!
- IT'S HARD TO RESIST.

939
00:39:34,873 --> 00:39:37,877
ALL RIGHT, ALL RIGHT!
I'M IN THE TUB!

940
00:39:41,513 --> 00:39:44,483
[GURGLING] OH, I JUST LOVE
HANDEL'S WATER MUSIC.

941
00:39:44,517 --> 00:39:46,718
[GURGLING] IT'S SO PEACEFUL.

942
00:39:48,887 --> 00:39:51,123
I WAS FANTASTIC LAST NIGHT.

943
00:39:54,193 --> 00:39:55,627
HMM?

944
00:39:55,693 --> 00:39:58,397
[STATIC, FEEDBACK]

945
00:39:58,430 --> 00:40:00,800
HEY, THE PLAYBOY CHANNEL.

946
00:40:00,800 --> 00:40:03,335
EIICHI'S UNSCRAMBLING IT!

947
00:40:07,338 --> 00:40:10,308
- SISTER!
- [ALL] SISTER!

948
00:40:10,342 --> 00:40:12,712
UGH.

949
00:40:17,750 --> 00:40:21,653
[ALL]
WAH-WAH-WAH-WAAAAAH.

950
00:40:21,687 --> 00:40:23,688
HOSS, LITTLE JOE!

951
00:40:26,292 --> 00:40:28,560
HOP SING! HOSS! LITTLE JOE!

952
00:40:28,593 --> 00:40:30,295
ADAM!

953
00:40:30,328 --> 00:40:34,233
YOU KNOW, WILD HORSES COULDN'T
DRAG THIS PLOT ANY FURTHER.

954
00:40:34,267 --> 00:40:35,667
--THINK EVERYTHING'S
GOING TO BE ALL RIGHT?

955
00:40:35,700 --> 00:40:37,903
- GRANDPA SOUNDS LIKE A GIRL.
- I'LL GO AND SEE.

956
00:40:37,937 --> 00:40:39,672
- EIICHI!
- NO, YOU WAIT.

957
00:40:39,705 --> 00:40:41,907
- YOU GO TO BED.
- DON'T WANT TO.

958
00:40:41,940 --> 00:40:44,377
GO ON. YOU MUST GO
STRAIGHT OFF TO BED NOW.

959
00:40:44,410 --> 00:40:46,545
GO ON, THEN.

960
00:40:46,578 --> 00:40:49,182
[GAOS ROARS]

961
00:40:49,215 --> 00:40:51,817
DID YOU EVER SEE
THE LAST EMPEROR, SISTER?

962
00:40:53,985 --> 00:40:55,822
OOH.

963
00:40:55,855 --> 00:40:59,258
OH.

964
00:40:59,292 --> 00:41:02,628
HMM?

965
00:41:02,662 --> 00:41:04,897
- AHH...
- [SERVO GROWLS]

966
00:41:04,930 --> 00:41:07,398
THERE, I JUST
MARKED OUR TERRITORY.

967
00:41:07,432 --> 00:41:10,068
--AND THAT ONE COW.
WHERE HAVE THEY ALL GONE TO?

968
00:41:10,102 --> 00:41:12,270
WE'VE GOTTA GET SOME FRESH MILK
FROM SOMEWHERE.

969
00:41:12,303 --> 00:41:14,907
- DON'T LOOK AT ME.
- --I DON'T KNOW WHERE
WE'LL GET IT AT.

970
00:41:14,940 --> 00:41:16,742
YEAH.

971
00:41:16,775 --> 00:41:19,010
- [GUNSHOTS]
- OOH. OOH.

972
00:41:19,043 --> 00:41:22,347
I'LL KILL HIM!
I'LL KILL HIM!

973
00:41:22,380 --> 00:41:24,750
- I'LL KILL HIM!
- TAKE IT EASY, TAKE IT EASY!

974
00:41:24,783 --> 00:41:26,285
- GET THE GUN.
- COW COPS, IN COLOR.

975
00:41:26,318 --> 00:41:29,087
- IT'S ALL RIGHT NOW.
- [MAN MUMBLES]

976
00:41:29,120 --> 00:41:30,622
- TAKE IT EASY.
- IT'S ALL MY FAULT!

977
00:41:30,655 --> 00:41:32,858
IT'S ALL MY FAULT!
I'LL KILL 'EM!

978
00:41:32,892 --> 00:41:35,060
WHEN I THINK ABOUT HIM,
I TOUCH MYSELF.

979
00:41:35,093 --> 00:41:36,262
I DO.

980
00:41:36,295 --> 00:41:38,197
HE'S GOT A WADE SWEATER ON.

981
00:41:38,230 --> 00:41:40,232
I DON'T KNOW. I GUESS
HE'S A LITTLE CRAZY, THAT'S ALL.

982
00:41:40,265 --> 00:41:42,835
AND WHAT DO
YOU TWO WANT, EH?

983
00:41:42,868 --> 00:41:44,370
HEY, IT'S JAMES HERRIOT.

984
00:41:44,403 --> 00:41:47,272
YOU SEE, WE RAN COMPLETELY OUT
OF FOOD AT THE SITE.

985
00:41:47,305 --> 00:41:48,473
WE CAN'T BUY ANY ANYWHERE.

986
00:41:48,507 --> 00:41:49,975
AND TOP OF THAT,
MY VOICE IS CHANGING.

987
00:41:50,008 --> 00:41:52,110
LOOKS LIKE YOU MIGHT BE ABLE
TO SELL A BIT OF MILK HERE.

988
00:41:52,143 --> 00:41:54,313
WELL, I CAN'T.
ALL OF MY DAIRY HERD

989
00:41:54,347 --> 00:41:56,382
- RAN AWAY LAST NIGHT.
- DID THEY?

990
00:41:56,415 --> 00:41:57,883
BUT YOU CAN'T BLAME THAT
ON US, THOUGH.

991
00:41:57,917 --> 00:41:59,518
- IT'S NOT OUR FAULT.
- YEAH?

992
00:41:59,552 --> 00:42:01,687
WELL, HE THOUGHT IT WAS.

993
00:42:01,720 --> 00:42:03,422
THAT'S RIGHT.
THAT'S WHAT HE SAID.

994
00:42:03,455 --> 00:42:05,157
- THAT'S WHERE THE...
- HE WENT OUT ALL LAST NIGHT.

995
00:42:05,190 --> 00:42:07,025
TO TRY AND FIND THE COWS.

996
00:42:07,058 --> 00:42:09,828
WHEN HE CAME BACK AGAIN,
HE WAS QUITE CRAZY.

997
00:42:09,862 --> 00:42:11,763
AND HE SAYS THAT THE WHOLE THING
IS YOUR FAULT.

998
00:42:11,797 --> 00:42:14,400
- THAT'S NONSENSE!
- WE HAVEN'T TOUCHED THE COWS!

999
00:42:14,433 --> 00:42:16,235
--SINCE YOU ARRIVED.

1000
00:42:16,268 --> 00:42:17,837
FIRST OF ALL,
WE HAD THE VOLCANOES.

1001
00:42:17,870 --> 00:42:19,505
THEN WE HAD THE MONSTERS.

1002
00:42:19,538 --> 00:42:21,840
AND ALL SINCE YOU ARRIVED.

1003
00:42:21,873 --> 00:42:23,475
NOW. GET OUT!

1004
00:42:23,508 --> 00:42:25,643
- [BOTS STRAIN]
- HEY! HEY!

1005
00:42:25,677 --> 00:42:27,045
EVERYBODY IN
THE VILLAGE THERE!

1006
00:42:27,078 --> 00:42:28,880
EVERY FARMER
WHO'S LOST A COW!

1007
00:42:28,913 --> 00:42:32,652
HEY, MRS. O'LEARY'S COW
TIPPED OVER THE LANTERN.

1008
00:42:32,685 --> 00:42:34,387
COME ON! CALL THE MEN IN!

1009
00:42:34,420 --> 00:42:36,688
WE NEED MORE SKIN BRACER!

1010
00:42:36,722 --> 00:42:38,557
MENIN.

1011
00:42:38,590 --> 00:42:41,227
LET'S JUST FORGET THE MILK.

1012
00:42:41,260 --> 00:42:44,028
MUST YOU TAKE THAT
WITH YOU EVERYWHERE?

1013
00:42:44,062 --> 00:42:45,932
- HUH?
- OH, IT'S-- OH.

1014
00:42:45,965 --> 00:42:48,600
MOM, IF THE U.N. CALLS,
I'M PLAYING WITH MY SLOT CAR.

1015
00:42:48,633 --> 00:42:50,168
PUT YOUR TOYS AWAY.

1016
00:42:50,202 --> 00:42:51,937
DON'T YOU TOUCH THEM.

1017
00:42:51,970 --> 00:42:53,305
THEY'RE PART OF THE SET.

1018
00:42:53,338 --> 00:42:54,707
NOW I CAN'T DO
THE NEXT SCENE.

1019
00:42:54,740 --> 00:42:56,408
WHOO-HOO!

1020
00:42:56,442 --> 00:42:58,310
EIICHI, NOT SO LOUD.

1021
00:42:58,343 --> 00:42:59,578
YOU'LL DISTURB GRANDDAD.

1022
00:42:59,612 --> 00:43:02,915
GRANDDAD'S
ALREADY DISTURBED.

1023
00:43:02,948 --> 00:43:05,417
THEY'VE BEEN IN THERE
FOR MORE THAN THREE HOURS NOW.

1024
00:43:05,450 --> 00:43:06,685
JUST SAYING THE SAME THINGS
OVER AND OVER.

1025
00:43:06,718 --> 00:43:08,853
I SWEAR, THIS IS
THE LAST BLANKET I'M WASHING.

1026
00:43:08,887 --> 00:43:12,190
--GETTING NOWHERE.

1027
00:43:12,223 --> 00:43:15,693
SO YOU THINK
WE OUGHT TO WAIT A WHILE?

1028
00:43:15,727 --> 00:43:17,462
YES, I DO.

1029
00:43:17,495 --> 00:43:19,998
WELL, YOU KNOW WHAT THEY SAY
ABOUT ANIMALS RUNNING AWAY.

1030
00:43:20,032 --> 00:43:23,168
- [ALL CACKLE]
- --A DISASTER IS COMING.

1031
00:43:23,202 --> 00:43:24,837
DON'T YOU THINK
WE'D BE BETTER OFF

1032
00:43:24,870 --> 00:43:27,572
SELLING THE LAND NOW,
WHILE WE CAN?

1033
00:43:27,605 --> 00:43:29,708
I'M AN OLD MAN,
BUT WE'VE NEVER HAD

1034
00:43:29,742 --> 00:43:31,343
ANY TROUBLES
LIKE THIS BEFORE.

1035
00:43:31,377 --> 00:43:32,712
NOT EVER SINCE
I CAN REMEMBER.

1036
00:43:32,745 --> 00:43:33,978
- WHICH IS LAST WEDNESDAY.
- I KNOW THAT WE'LL

1037
00:43:34,012 --> 00:43:35,880
LOSE SOME MONEY.
BUT I'M STILL NOT SURE

1038
00:43:35,913 --> 00:43:37,448
WE WOULDN'T BE
A LOT BETTER OFF IF WE TOOK

1039
00:43:37,482 --> 00:43:39,718
THE COMPANY'S PRESENT OFFER
FOR THE LAND AND GOT OUT?

1040
00:43:39,752 --> 00:43:42,520
WHAT ABOUT THAT HIRED GUN
NAMED SHANE?

1041
00:43:42,553 --> 00:43:44,790
YES, YOU'RE RIGHT.
I CAN'T GET TO SLEEP AT NIGHT

1042
00:43:44,823 --> 00:43:46,292
FOR WORRYING ABOUT IT.

1043
00:43:46,325 --> 00:43:47,927
JUST WAITING
FOR IT TO COME OUT.

1044
00:43:47,960 --> 00:43:49,795
IT'S STUPID OF YOU
TO TAKE THIS ATTITUDE.

1045
00:43:49,828 --> 00:43:51,963
- DIG.
- IF THEY KNOW
YOU'RE WEAKENING,

1046
00:43:51,997 --> 00:43:54,867
WELL THEN, THEY'LL JUST
DRIVE THE PRICE EVEN LOWER.

1047
00:43:54,900 --> 00:43:56,302
WILFORD BRIMLEY?

1048
00:43:56,335 --> 00:43:58,837
- NO.
- YOU WANT TO GET MORE MONEY,
DON'T YOU?

1049
00:43:58,870 --> 00:44:01,440
YOU WANT TO LET THE LAND GO
FOR ANY LESS THAN IT'S WORTH?

1050
00:44:01,473 --> 00:44:02,173
DO YOU?

1051
00:44:02,207 --> 00:44:04,275
OF COURSE WE DON'T.

1052
00:44:04,308 --> 00:44:06,278
IT'S THE RIGHT THING TO DO.

1053
00:44:06,312 --> 00:44:08,280
SO THEN, TRUST ME.

1054
00:44:08,313 --> 00:44:10,782
JUST LET ME HANDLE
THE NEGOTIATIONS FOR YOU.

1055
00:44:10,815 --> 00:44:13,418
DO YOU REALLY THINK WE CAN GET
CALIFORNIA FOR US ALL?

1056
00:44:15,687 --> 00:44:17,555
HERE'S THE NEWS.
THE MONSTER GAOS IS CAUSING

1057
00:44:17,588 --> 00:44:19,290
GREAT DAMAGE
TO THE MOUNTAIN PROVINCES.

1058
00:44:19,323 --> 00:44:21,727
UP TO NOW, NONE OF THE POLICE
NOR THE ARMED SERVICES--

1059
00:44:21,760 --> 00:44:24,262
- HMM?
- HEY, THOSE HELMETS
ARE MULTIPLYING.

1060
00:44:24,295 --> 00:44:25,797
- OH.
- --GOING TO REPORT THE NUMBER
OF PEOPLE ARE MISSING.

1061
00:44:25,830 --> 00:44:27,665
[MAN SHOUTS]

1062
00:44:27,700 --> 00:44:29,435
WHAT?

1063
00:44:29,468 --> 00:44:31,303
TURN DOWN THE RADIO!

1064
00:44:31,337 --> 00:44:33,205
--AND POLICE AUTHORITIES.

1065
00:44:35,373 --> 00:44:36,942
AAH! MORE HELMETS.

1066
00:44:36,975 --> 00:44:38,210
YOU'RE LEAVING
YOUR JOBS NOW?

1067
00:44:38,243 --> 00:44:39,645
YES. MAY AS WELL.

1068
00:44:39,678 --> 00:44:41,747
THERE'S NOTHING FOR US
TO DO HERE NOW.

1069
00:44:41,780 --> 00:44:43,648
WORK ON THE ROAD STOPPED
ALTOGETHER.

1070
00:44:43,682 --> 00:44:45,650
AND WE'RE WORRIED ABOUT
THIS MONSTER, TOO.

1071
00:44:45,683 --> 00:44:47,787
HEY, LOOKS LIKE
IL DUCE UP THERE.

1072
00:44:47,820 --> 00:44:49,220
- THE BIG BENITO?
- MM-HMM.

1073
00:44:49,253 --> 00:44:50,788
WELL, I'M SORRY
TO SEE YOU GOING.

1074
00:44:50,822 --> 00:44:53,258
- HOPE YOU FIND WORK.
- DON'T FORGET TO CALL US

1075
00:44:53,292 --> 00:44:55,260
WHEN THE WORK STOPS AGAIN,
WILL YOU, BOSS?

1076
00:44:55,293 --> 00:44:57,028
- OH, SURE.
- YEAH, RIGHT.

1077
00:44:57,062 --> 00:44:58,563
RIGHT. LET'S GO.

1078
00:44:58,597 --> 00:45:00,698
ALL RIGHT. IF WE GET WORK.

1079
00:45:00,732 --> 00:45:03,135
GET MOVING NOW.
SEE YOU GUYS.

1080
00:45:05,970 --> 00:45:08,507
HEY, WHERE'S MY HELMET?

1081
00:45:08,540 --> 00:45:12,410
HOW LONG DO YOU THINK WE'RE
GONNA HAVE TO STAY UP HERE?

1082
00:45:12,443 --> 00:45:14,378
I'LL STAY AS LONG AS
I'M IN CHARGE.

1083
00:45:14,413 --> 00:45:16,282
YOU'RE IN CHARGE
OF NOTHING, PAL.

1084
00:45:16,315 --> 00:45:18,117
--I'M GONNA HAVE TO STAY.

1085
00:45:18,150 --> 00:45:20,418
HEY LOOK, HE'S GOT
A PAC-MAN JACKET.

1086
00:45:20,452 --> 00:45:21,853
DO YOU TWO
WANT TO MOVE OUT NOW?

1087
00:45:21,887 --> 00:45:23,522
OF COURSE NOT.

1088
00:45:23,555 --> 00:45:24,990
NEITHER OF US IS AFRAID
OF THE MONSTER,

1089
00:45:25,023 --> 00:45:26,492
SO WHY SHOULD WE LEAVE?

1090
00:45:26,525 --> 00:45:29,127
[ALL IMITATE CURLY]

1091
00:45:29,160 --> 00:45:31,097
HE DOESN'T WORRY US AT ALL.

1092
00:45:31,130 --> 00:45:32,765
[ALL CHUCKLE]

1093
00:45:36,602 --> 00:45:38,270
IS HE THE CATCHER
IN THE RYE?

1094
00:45:38,303 --> 00:45:41,307
- SHEESH.
- --YOU, SCARING US LIKE THAT?

1095
00:45:41,340 --> 00:45:43,208
- "SCARING US LIKE THAT?"
- THERE'S NOTHING
TO BE SCARED OF.

1096
00:45:43,242 --> 00:45:44,843
WHY DO YOU SAY THAT?

1097
00:45:44,877 --> 00:45:47,145
GAOS IS A VERY
FEROCIOUS MONSTER.

1098
00:45:47,178 --> 00:45:48,547
YOU MEAN YOU AIN'T SCARED?

1099
00:45:48,580 --> 00:45:50,548
NOT AT DAYTIME. YOU SEE,

1100
00:45:50,582 --> 00:45:52,017
HE ONLY COMES OUT
IN THE NIGHT TIME.

1101
00:45:52,050 --> 00:45:54,820
I THANK THE LORD
FOR THE NIGHT TIME.

1102
00:45:54,853 --> 00:45:57,155
TELL US
HOW YOU FOUND THAT OUT.

1103
00:45:57,188 --> 00:45:58,790
I WROTE IT DOWN IN MY DIARY.

1104
00:45:58,823 --> 00:46:00,725
WHEN GAOS COMES OUT,
I JUST WRITE DOWN THE TIME.

1105
00:46:00,758 --> 00:46:02,327
USUALLY RIGHT AFTER CHEERS.

1106
00:46:02,360 --> 00:46:04,630
- MM.
- OH, I SEE.

1107
00:46:04,663 --> 00:46:06,232
MITCH MILLER?

1108
00:46:06,265 --> 00:46:07,867
IT NEVER OCCURRED
TO ANY OF US THAT GAOS

1109
00:46:07,900 --> 00:46:10,068
MIGHT BE
A NOCTURNAL BEAST.

1110
00:46:10,102 --> 00:46:11,937
HIDING OUT DURING
THE DAYTIME,

1111
00:46:11,970 --> 00:46:13,272
AND COMING OUT AT NIGHT.

1112
00:46:13,305 --> 00:46:15,007
THAT'S RIGHT. WE NEVER SAW EVEN
A GLIMPSE OF HIM

1113
00:46:15,040 --> 00:46:16,375
DURING THE BOMBING ATTACK.

1114
00:46:16,408 --> 00:46:18,543
HE KEPT RIGHT UNDERCOVER
THE WHOLE TIME.

1115
00:46:18,577 --> 00:46:21,112
IN THAT CASE, WE NEED ONLY
WATCH FOR HIM AT NIGHT.

1116
00:46:21,147 --> 00:46:23,615
AND YOU CAN CALL OFF YOUR TROOPS
DURING THE DAYTIME, THEN.

1117
00:46:23,648 --> 00:46:26,050
COMMANDER. DON'T YOU HAVE SOME
SPECIAL NEW FLARES THAT'RE

1118
00:46:26,083 --> 00:46:28,053
SUPPOSED TO BE PRACTICALLY
AS LIGHT AS DAYLIGHT?

1119
00:46:28,087 --> 00:46:29,453
YES, WE'VE BEEN
DEVELOPING SOME

1120
00:46:29,488 --> 00:46:30,922
SPECIALLY FOR
ANTI-GUERILLA WARFARE

1121
00:46:30,955 --> 00:46:32,590
KNOWN AS THE A.G.I.L.
FLARE SYSTEM.

1122
00:46:32,623 --> 00:46:35,393
- ...THING.
- HOWEVER, THEY ARE STILL
IN THE TRIAL STAGE.

1123
00:46:35,427 --> 00:46:36,862
OH, WE GOTTA GO.

1124
00:46:36,895 --> 00:46:38,130
- OKAY.
- LET'S TRY THEM.

1125
00:46:38,163 --> 00:46:39,765
IT SEEMS THAT GAOS
IS SENSITIVE TO LIGHT.

1126
00:46:39,798 --> 00:46:41,633
- THANKS, DAD.
- AND IF IT DOES SEEM
THAT HE HAS

1127
00:46:41,667 --> 00:46:44,468
ANY PARTICULAR WEAKNESSES,
WE MUST BE SURE TO EXPLOIT THEM.

1128
00:46:51,643 --> 00:46:55,280
OKAY, NOW LISTEN, TOM.
THIS IS THE DEUS EX MACHINA

1129
00:46:55,313 --> 00:46:56,982
WHICH IS THE GOD MACHINE.

1130
00:46:57,015 --> 00:47:00,318
OKAY? IN CASE WE CAN'T THINK OF
ANY WAY TO END THE PLAY,

1131
00:47:00,352 --> 00:47:02,053
- I'M GONNA
LOWER YOU DOWN, OKAY?
- OKAY.

1132
00:47:02,087 --> 00:47:03,622
AND HAVE A BIG PRODUCTION
ENDING, ALL RIGHT?

1133
00:47:03,655 --> 00:47:05,757
- ROGER.
- I CAN'T GET INTO THIS, JOEL.

1134
00:47:05,790 --> 00:47:07,192
"ICH BIN EIN MONSTER?"

1135
00:47:07,225 --> 00:47:08,493
- WHAT'S THAT
SUPPOSED TO MEAN?
- ALL RIGHT.

1136
00:47:08,527 --> 00:47:10,428
I JUST NEED YOU
TO FAKE IT, OKAY?

1137
00:47:10,462 --> 00:47:12,430
UH, LET'S HAVE THOSE
FOOTLIGHTS, CAMBOT.

1138
00:47:12,463 --> 00:47:15,600
- OOH.
- UM, WELCOME
TO OUR PRODUCTION,

1139
00:47:15,633 --> 00:47:18,770
WHICH IS A COMBINATION
OF THE GOTTERDAMMERUNG

1140
00:47:18,803 --> 00:47:21,473
AND GAMERA VS. GAOS.

1141
00:47:21,507 --> 00:47:25,277
WE CALL IT
THE GAMERA-DAMERA.

1142
00:47:25,310 --> 00:47:28,113
OKAY? OKAY, SPUDS,
LET'S REALLY GET WORKING NOW.

1143
00:47:28,147 --> 00:47:29,480
HERE WE GO.

1144
00:47:29,513 --> 00:47:32,450
♪♪ [BOTS FAKE-TRUMPET]

1145
00:47:32,483 --> 00:47:33,885
MEIN...

1146
00:47:33,918 --> 00:47:37,322
- MEIN LIEBER SCHATZ--
- OH, WE GOT MOVIE SIGN!

1147
00:47:37,355 --> 00:47:40,792
[SERVO GROANS]

1148
00:47:47,498 --> 00:47:49,067
OUCH, THAT HURT.

1149
00:47:49,100 --> 00:47:50,635
OH BOY, THAT HURT.

1150
00:47:50,668 --> 00:47:53,338
OH. TAKE THAT STUFF OUT.

1151
00:47:53,372 --> 00:47:56,107
- WHAT A JIP.
- HEY.

1152
00:47:56,140 --> 00:47:57,977
A THOUSAND POINTS-- I'M GONNA
GIVE YOU THE THIRD DEGREE!

1153
00:47:58,010 --> 00:47:59,912
- ANSWER!
- YOU KNOW WHAT BURNS MY BUTT?

1154
00:47:59,945 --> 00:48:01,547
A FLAME ABOUT THAT HIGH.

1155
00:48:01,580 --> 00:48:03,448
- [SERVO CHUCKLES]
- YOU FOOL!

1156
00:48:03,482 --> 00:48:07,085
I-- I JUST HAPPEN
TO BE COLD, THAT'S ALL.

1157
00:48:07,118 --> 00:48:09,053
YOU COULD'VE FOOLED ME.

1158
00:48:09,087 --> 00:48:11,022
[EXPLOSION]

1159
00:48:11,055 --> 00:48:12,457
- AAH! IT'S COMING!
- IT'S COMING!

1160
00:48:12,490 --> 00:48:16,295
- AAH! RICKY! AAH!
- TAKE IT EASY.

1161
00:48:16,328 --> 00:48:18,263
THERE'S NOTHING
TO WORRY ABOUT NOW.

1162
00:48:18,297 --> 00:48:19,765
NOT WITH THE NEW FLARES.

1163
00:48:19,798 --> 00:48:21,933
EACH ONE OF THEM'S MORE THAN
SIX MILLION CANDLE POWER.

1164
00:48:21,967 --> 00:48:24,670
THAT'S FOUR TIMES BRIGHTER
THAN THE MOON, WHEN AT MAXIMUM.

1165
00:48:24,703 --> 00:48:26,438
- NEAT.
- I'M VERY GLAD TO HEAR IT.

1166
00:48:26,472 --> 00:48:28,507
I ONLY HOPE IT REALLY IS
AFRAID OF THE LIGHT.

1167
00:48:28,540 --> 00:48:30,175
WELL, DOES THIS MEAN
WE CAN GO TO SLEEP NOW?

1168
00:48:30,208 --> 00:48:32,310
[ALL GOOFY-LAUGH]

1169
00:48:32,343 --> 00:48:33,578
--UNTIL WE'VE
TESTED THE FLARES.

1170
00:48:33,612 --> 00:48:35,513
YOU MEAN WE'VE GOTTA
SIT UP ALL NIGHT?

1171
00:48:35,547 --> 00:48:37,715
WELL, AFTER ALL, WE ARE
THE ONES NEAREST TO THE HILL.

1172
00:48:37,748 --> 00:48:39,350
WE'RE SUPPOSED
TO SIGNAL IMMEDIATELY

1173
00:48:39,383 --> 00:48:41,052
IF WE SEE ANY SIGN
OF MOVEMENT HERE.

1174
00:48:41,085 --> 00:48:43,255
- YEAH.
- YEAH.
- YOU SLEEP FIRST.

1175
00:48:43,288 --> 00:48:45,557
AND YOU KEEP CHECKING
THE REPORTS ON THE RADIO.

1176
00:48:45,590 --> 00:48:48,093
I'LL STAND UP HERE AND KEEP
THROWING THINGS.

1177
00:48:48,127 --> 00:48:49,628
YOU GET SOME SLEEP NOW,
OKAY?

1178
00:48:49,662 --> 00:48:51,062
ALL RIGHT. KEEP THE FIRE UP.

1179
00:48:51,095 --> 00:48:53,532
YES SIR, I WILL.

1180
00:48:53,565 --> 00:48:56,902
NOW, I'M JUST GONNA
TAKE MY PICTURE HERE. YEAH.

1181
00:48:56,935 --> 00:48:58,203
- AS A MEMENTO.
- YOU GET SOME SLEEP.

1182
00:48:58,237 --> 00:49:00,005
- WILL YOU BE OKAY?
- OF COURSE I WILL.

1183
00:49:00,038 --> 00:49:03,175
THAT SYMBOL ON HIS BACK IS
JAPANESE FOR "I'M WITH STUPID."

1184
00:49:03,208 --> 00:49:06,745
- WAIT.
- [RADIO STATIC]

1185
00:49:06,778 --> 00:49:09,347
OH. THAT'S MY FAVORITE
JOHN CAGE SONG.

1186
00:49:11,683 --> 00:49:13,485
D'OH, WOULD YOU--
NEXT TIME, I LEAD.

1187
00:49:13,518 --> 00:49:15,187
YOU'RE SUPPOSED
TO WATCH HERE.

1188
00:49:15,220 --> 00:49:16,488
I'LL GET TO SLEEP.

1189
00:49:16,522 --> 00:49:19,825
YEAH, SEE YOU LATER, THEN.

1190
00:49:19,858 --> 00:49:21,960
HEY, IT'S A CHEESE RADIO.

1191
00:49:21,993 --> 00:49:25,063
NO, IT'S THE ALL ORANGESICLE
STATION, I THINK.

1192
00:49:25,097 --> 00:49:27,565
YEP. CHECK IT OUT.

1193
00:49:32,570 --> 00:49:34,638
- HMM.
- OH MAN.

1194
00:49:34,673 --> 00:49:35,940
I SHOULDN'T'VE HAD
THAT TOFU CHILI.

1195
00:49:35,973 --> 00:49:37,308
YEAAH!

1196
00:49:37,342 --> 00:49:39,277
- HEY, BOSS!
- "FREE BIRD!"

1197
00:49:39,310 --> 00:49:41,312
- "FREE BIRD!"
- WHOO!

1198
00:49:41,347 --> 00:49:43,382
IT'S COMING! GET UP!

1199
00:49:43,415 --> 00:49:44,750
WHAT? WHAT? WHAT?...

1200
00:49:44,783 --> 00:49:47,585
WHAT? WHAT?

1201
00:49:47,618 --> 00:49:50,855
CAN EIICHI COME OUT
AND PLAY?

1202
00:49:50,888 --> 00:49:52,657
FIRE THE SIGNAL!

1203
00:49:52,690 --> 00:49:55,927
I'M YOUR WAKE-UP CALL!

1204
00:49:55,960 --> 00:49:57,695
YES, WE'LL BE MUCH SAFER
OUT HERE.

1205
00:49:57,728 --> 00:49:59,765
[GAOS SCREAMS]

1206
00:50:01,198 --> 00:50:03,502
- [MAN MUTTERS]
- OOH.

1207
00:50:03,535 --> 00:50:05,403
HEY, YOU MIGHT SAY HE'S GOT
A REAL FLARE FOR THIS.

1208
00:50:05,437 --> 00:50:07,238
[ALL CHUCKLE]

1209
00:50:10,808 --> 00:50:12,477
- ♪♪ [SERVO HUMS WITH SCORE]
- --FIRE!

1210
00:50:12,510 --> 00:50:14,312
- OPEN FIRE!
- OPEN THE WINDOW FIRST,

1211
00:50:14,345 --> 00:50:17,382
THEN FIRE!

1212
00:50:20,218 --> 00:50:22,820
OOH. BOY.

1213
00:50:24,757 --> 00:50:26,892
GRACE JONES
TAKES ONE TO THE HEAD.

1214
00:50:26,925 --> 00:50:30,562
- OUCH!
- SHE CAN'T TAKE IT THERE.

1215
00:50:30,595 --> 00:50:34,565
HA-HAH! THIS IS FUN!

1216
00:50:34,598 --> 00:50:38,270
MODEL TANKS
AREN'T WORKING, CAPTAIN.

1217
00:50:38,303 --> 00:50:41,105
I'M BATMAN.

1218
00:50:42,773 --> 00:50:46,712
FRIENDS, ROMANS, COUNTRYMEN,
WOULD YOU LET ME TALK?

1219
00:50:46,745 --> 00:50:50,115
[JOEL AS LUGOSI]
I VANT TO DRINK YOUR BLOOD.

1220
00:50:51,583 --> 00:50:53,118
HEY, COME ON, TOKYO.
GIVE ME A HUG.

1221
00:50:53,152 --> 00:50:54,385
I KNOW YOU GOT IT IN YOU.

1222
00:50:54,418 --> 00:50:57,688
IT'S GAOS BUSCAGLIA
HERE TALKING.

1223
00:50:57,722 --> 00:50:59,357
OH, I LOVE TO LAUGH!

1224
00:50:59,390 --> 00:51:01,158
LONG AND LOUD AND CLEAR!

1225
00:51:03,495 --> 00:51:05,063
HE'S DOING LAP FOLDS.

1226
00:51:05,097 --> 00:51:07,332
COME ON, THREE MORE.
GIVE IT TO ME. COME ON.

1227
00:51:07,365 --> 00:51:09,233
FEEL THE BURN.
YOU GOTTA WANT IT. GO.

1228
00:51:09,267 --> 00:51:12,970
- OOH.
- OOPS.

1229
00:51:13,003 --> 00:51:16,942
WELL, THAT COULD'VE
GONE BETTER.

1230
00:51:16,975 --> 00:51:19,343
CALL ME MARIAH.

1231
00:51:22,513 --> 00:51:24,883
[ALL RASP-VOICE]

1232
00:51:24,917 --> 00:51:27,118
CAN'T UNDERSTAND IT.

1233
00:51:27,152 --> 00:51:28,687
WHOA, HE'S AIR-SURFIN'.

1234
00:51:28,720 --> 00:51:30,388
[ALL]
WHOO!

1235
00:51:34,358 --> 00:51:35,860
NIGHT ON BALD MOUNTAIN.

1236
00:51:35,893 --> 00:51:39,763
♪♪ [SERVO HUMS MUSSORGSKY]

1237
00:51:39,798 --> 00:51:41,900
- IT'S MOVING OUT.
- TO THE EAST SIDE.

1238
00:51:41,933 --> 00:51:43,668
- --MOVING TO THE SOUTH.
- TO A DELUXE APARTMENT.

1239
00:51:43,702 --> 00:51:45,170
--CENTRAL CITIES
AND GIVE THEM WARNING!

1240
00:51:45,203 --> 00:51:46,838
TELL THEM,
EVACUATE WHERE THEY CAN!

1241
00:51:46,872 --> 00:51:49,440
QUICKLY. THERE ISN'T
MUCH TIME LEFT.

1242
00:51:52,443 --> 00:51:54,645
THUNDERBIRDS ARE GO!

1243
00:51:57,015 --> 00:51:59,117
NO, TORY, NO!

1244
00:52:02,087 --> 00:52:03,788
[PEOPLE SCREAM]

1245
00:52:03,822 --> 00:52:05,357
OH-- HE SPIT ON THE WINDOW.

1246
00:52:05,390 --> 00:52:07,292
--HOCKER.

1247
00:52:12,797 --> 00:52:15,233
HEY, A SPLIT-LEVEL.

1248
00:52:15,267 --> 00:52:18,470
OOH.

1249
00:52:18,503 --> 00:52:22,107
OOH!

1250
00:52:22,140 --> 00:52:25,010
MODEL TRAIN TO THE RESCUE!

1251
00:52:25,043 --> 00:52:27,178
AREN'T YOU GLAD
YOU USED DIAL?

1252
00:52:27,212 --> 00:52:29,713
DON'T YOU WISH
EVERYBODY DID?

1253
00:52:29,747 --> 00:52:31,517
I DO.

1254
00:52:31,550 --> 00:52:34,585
NO, NOT MISTER ROGERS'
NEIGHBORHOOD! NO!

1255
00:52:34,618 --> 00:52:36,453
OH...

1256
00:52:36,487 --> 00:52:38,623
- IT'S PROBABLY BETTER.
- [BOTS] YEAH.

1257
00:52:43,895 --> 00:52:47,198
HMM. MUNCHY, CRUNCHY,
CHOCOLATEY COMMUTERS.

1258
00:52:47,232 --> 00:52:48,700
HMM-MM.

1259
00:52:48,733 --> 00:52:50,268
ROAST 'EM, TENDERIZE 'EM.

1260
00:52:50,302 --> 00:52:52,337
DOWN THEY GO.

1261
00:52:56,608 --> 00:52:58,543
WHOA.

1262
00:53:03,113 --> 00:53:05,150
GET ME,
I'M DAVID COPPERFIELD!

1263
00:53:05,183 --> 00:53:06,818
I'M GONNA MAKE
THIS TRAIN DISAPPEAR.

1264
00:53:06,852 --> 00:53:08,820
[SERVO CHUCKLES]

1265
00:53:11,388 --> 00:53:12,757
[PEOPLE SCREAM]

1266
00:53:12,790 --> 00:53:15,260
I GOT A FEELING
ABOUT THOSE PEOPLE.

1267
00:53:15,293 --> 00:53:17,495
- YEP.
- OH, THEY-- YEP.

1268
00:53:17,528 --> 00:53:19,530
NEVER STAND IN GROUPS,
FOLKS.

1269
00:53:22,167 --> 00:53:25,037
OH, GOD. DORITO BREATH.

1270
00:53:25,070 --> 00:53:26,805
- YUCK.
- OOH.

1271
00:53:26,838 --> 00:53:28,607
- SHARP TEETH.
- ATTENTION, HERE IS

1272
00:53:28,640 --> 00:53:30,308
A SPECIAL EMERGENCY
ANNOUNCEMENT.

1273
00:53:30,342 --> 00:53:33,412
BLUES BROTHERS,
RHYTHM AND BLUES REVIEW!

1274
00:53:33,445 --> 00:53:36,582
--THE MONSTER
IS KNOWN TO HATE--

1275
00:53:36,615 --> 00:53:38,182
LADIES AND GENTLEMEN,

1276
00:53:38,215 --> 00:53:41,418
IT'S LIZA!

1277
00:53:41,452 --> 00:53:43,288
OOH, AND THAT'S
JUST TO LIGHT THE PATIO.

1278
00:53:43,322 --> 00:53:45,290
MM-HMM.

1279
00:53:51,162 --> 00:53:53,965
[MAN ON LOUDSPEAKER]

1280
00:53:53,998 --> 00:53:55,800
--IS NOW OPEN.
ALL CITIZENS

1281
00:53:55,833 --> 00:53:57,102
SHOULD ASSEMBLE
AT THE STADIUM.

1282
00:53:57,135 --> 00:53:58,737
AND THERE ARE
NO FUDGESICLES LEFT.

1283
00:53:58,770 --> 00:54:02,507
PIZZA, PIZZA.

1284
00:54:02,540 --> 00:54:04,175
LOOKS LIKE THE DODGERS
LEFT BROOKLYN,

1285
00:54:04,208 --> 00:54:06,712
AND IT'S PAYBACK TIME!

1286
00:54:06,745 --> 00:54:09,480
HEY, IT'S HELMET DAY.

1287
00:54:17,555 --> 00:54:18,957
IT'S A GERMAN AIR SHOW.

1288
00:54:18,990 --> 00:54:20,658
THE MONSTER HAS DISAPPEARED
TOWARD THE NORTHEAST.

1289
00:54:20,692 --> 00:54:22,260
ITS WHEREABOUTS
ARE NOT KNOWN.

1290
00:54:22,293 --> 00:54:23,595
- CITIZENS--
- SLEEP. SLEEP!

1291
00:54:23,628 --> 00:54:25,663
--INDOORS AND KEEP
THEIR LIGHTS ON.

1292
00:54:25,697 --> 00:54:28,800
SO THAT THEY MAY BE
CRUSHED MORE READILY.

1293
00:54:28,833 --> 00:54:30,268
DAMN. WHERE IS IT NOW?

1294
00:54:30,302 --> 00:54:32,003
WE CAN'T GO BACK
WITHOUT A PICTURE.

1295
00:54:32,037 --> 00:54:33,372
KEEP GOING TILL WE SEE IT.

1296
00:54:33,405 --> 00:54:35,373
WE'RE PROBABLY
WASTING OUR TIME.

1297
00:54:35,407 --> 00:54:37,375
I BET IT'S MILES AWAY
BY NOW.

1298
00:54:37,408 --> 00:54:39,877
HEY, WHO'S ROCKIN' THE CAR?

1299
00:54:39,910 --> 00:54:41,112
[PASSENGER SHOUTS]

1300
00:54:41,145 --> 00:54:43,982
THERE IT IS!
HURRY UP! QUICK!

1301
00:54:44,015 --> 00:54:46,918
- OH, THEY'RE IN BROOKLYN.
- AHH.

1302
00:54:46,952 --> 00:54:50,022
QUICK! GET A PICTURE!
HURRY! QUICK!

1303
00:54:50,055 --> 00:54:52,823
HEY, YOU TOOK MY SOUL!

1304
00:54:52,857 --> 00:54:54,825
HURRY! NOW! HEY--

1305
00:54:54,858 --> 00:54:57,128
HEY, DID YOU GUYS BORROW
THIS CAR FROM ALLEN FUNT?

1306
00:54:57,162 --> 00:54:59,397
OH, HE'S STILL
GOT A TWO-DOOR NOW.

1307
00:54:59,430 --> 00:55:02,033
HURRY! COME ON!
LET'S GET OUT OF HERE!

1308
00:55:02,067 --> 00:55:04,435
[SERVO WHEEZES]

1309
00:55:04,468 --> 00:55:06,070
[SERVO WHIMPERS]

1310
00:55:06,103 --> 00:55:07,872
GOT HALF A PAYMENT LEFT
ON HIS LEASE.

1311
00:55:07,905 --> 00:55:10,575
QUICK!

1312
00:55:10,608 --> 00:55:13,612
THANK YOU. I'D LIKE A DOZEN
WALLET-SIZED OF THAT, PLEASE.

1313
00:55:13,645 --> 00:55:15,080
I'LL SMILE.

1314
00:55:15,113 --> 00:55:16,948
ULTRA-BRIGHT SMILE.

1315
00:55:16,982 --> 00:55:19,250
HEY. GAMERA.

1316
00:55:19,283 --> 00:55:22,220
♪♪ [ALL HUM STADIUM "CHARGE"]

1317
00:55:22,253 --> 00:55:25,357
STARTING AS SECOND BASE...

1318
00:55:27,658 --> 00:55:29,360
THEY'RE GONNA SETTLE IT
LIKE REAL MEN.

1319
00:55:29,393 --> 00:55:30,728
ON THE GRIDIRON!

1320
00:55:30,762 --> 00:55:33,330
YEAH.

1321
00:55:33,365 --> 00:55:34,832
♪ PATTY-CAKE, PATTY-CAKE ♪

1322
00:55:34,898 --> 00:55:37,035
♪ BAKER'S TURTLE ♪

1323
00:55:42,007 --> 00:55:43,808
TORO! TORO, TURTLE!

1324
00:55:46,745 --> 00:55:50,148
[ALL]
OLE!

1325
00:55:50,215 --> 00:55:52,417
OH, SORRY. GIANT TURTLE
COMING THROUGH.

1326
00:55:52,417 --> 00:55:54,618
SORRY ABOUT THAT.

1327
00:55:58,122 --> 00:56:01,125
HEY YOU GUYS, LET'S DO
THAT CHEER WE WORKED OUT.

1328
00:56:01,158 --> 00:56:03,528
[ALL]
♪ OKAY GAOS, DON'T BE BLUE ♪

1329
00:56:03,562 --> 00:56:06,030
♪ FRANKENSTEIN WAS
UGLY TOO! ♪

1330
00:56:06,063 --> 00:56:08,533
- [BOTS] WHOO!
- HE'S GOING AGAIN.

1331
00:56:08,533 --> 00:56:11,970
SPIRIT!

1332
00:56:12,037 --> 00:56:14,438
HEY, UH,
HOW DOES GAMERA STEER?

1333
00:56:14,438 --> 00:56:17,242
- I-- GOT ME.
- I DON'T KNOW.

1334
00:56:20,245 --> 00:56:21,880
OOH. TRAGEDY STRUCK

1335
00:56:21,947 --> 00:56:23,915
AT THE MIDWAY
TILT-A-WHIRL TODAY.

1336
00:56:26,350 --> 00:56:28,653
THAT'S NICE.

1337
00:56:28,687 --> 00:56:31,222
COOL.

1338
00:56:31,255 --> 00:56:33,558
♪♪ [SERVO HUMS WITH SCORE]

1339
00:56:33,592 --> 00:56:35,227
COLD BEER! PEANUTS!

1340
00:56:35,260 --> 00:56:36,527
GAOS PROGRAMS HERE!

1341
00:56:36,560 --> 00:56:39,463
FROSTY MALTS!

1342
00:56:39,497 --> 00:56:42,100
- HOW DOES HE DO THAT?
- I DON'T KNOW.

1343
00:56:42,133 --> 00:56:44,302
HE'S TUMBLING.

1344
00:56:51,142 --> 00:56:52,577
OKAY.

1345
00:56:52,610 --> 00:56:54,312
YOU KNOW, I BET
THE HOLE IN THE OZONE

1346
00:56:54,345 --> 00:56:55,713
IS THIS BIRD'S FAULT.

1347
00:56:55,747 --> 00:56:57,715
[CROW GROANS]

1348
00:56:57,748 --> 00:57:00,585
[GAOS SHRIEKS]

1349
00:57:00,618 --> 00:57:02,787
JOEL, HOW DOES GAMERA FLY?

1350
00:57:02,820 --> 00:57:04,555
- I DON'T KNOW.
- WHY IS THERE AIR?

1351
00:57:04,588 --> 00:57:07,392
- WHY IS THE SKY BLUE?
- WHAT'S VIETNAM?

1352
00:57:10,862 --> 00:57:12,697
CHEAP TRICK, AT BUDDAKAN.

1353
00:57:12,730 --> 00:57:15,600
NEAT.

1354
00:57:15,633 --> 00:57:16,802
UH-OH.

1355
00:57:16,835 --> 00:57:18,435
OH, HE'S BLOWN A GASKET,

1356
00:57:18,470 --> 00:57:20,003
AND THAT MEANS
BACK TO THE PITS FOR GAMERA.

1357
00:57:20,037 --> 00:57:23,140
- I THINK GAOS IS LOSING--
- GAMERA'S WINNING!

1358
00:57:23,173 --> 00:57:24,742
HEY, SOMEBODY
DOESN'T HAVE A BUDDY.

1359
00:57:24,775 --> 00:57:28,713
HEY, YOU IN THE MIDDLE,
GET A BUDDY.

1360
00:57:28,747 --> 00:57:31,448
[SERVO MIMICS WIND]

1361
00:57:31,482 --> 00:57:35,187
UH-OH.

1362
00:57:35,220 --> 00:57:37,222
LOOK GUYS,
♪ SUPERCAR! ♪

1363
00:57:37,255 --> 00:57:38,823
[ALL]
♪ SUPERCAR! ♪

1364
00:57:38,857 --> 00:57:41,558
[ALL]
♪ SUPERCAR! ♪

1365
00:57:41,592 --> 00:57:44,428
♪ SHOVEL-HEAD ♪

1366
00:57:44,462 --> 00:57:46,030
NO, GAMERA!

1367
00:57:46,063 --> 00:57:47,432
HELP, MR. WIZARD!

1368
00:57:47,465 --> 00:57:49,533
PULL UP! PULL UP!

1369
00:57:49,567 --> 00:57:51,302
[ALL]
OH!

1370
00:57:51,335 --> 00:57:54,072
- HE HIT THE POPEYE CONVENTION!
- HOW EMBARRASS-KING.

1371
00:57:57,008 --> 00:58:00,478
[CROW CACKLES]

1372
00:58:00,512 --> 00:58:01,745
HMM.

1373
00:58:01,778 --> 00:58:05,617
HEY, I'VE GOT CONTACTS!
BE CAREFUL, COME ON.

1374
00:58:05,650 --> 00:58:08,653
CALGON, TAKE ME AWAY!

1375
00:58:12,123 --> 00:58:14,758
YOU GUYS, I SWEAR
I DREAMT THIS LAST NIGHT.

1376
00:58:24,635 --> 00:58:26,872
OH MAN, WE'RE RAMEN NOW!

1377
00:58:26,905 --> 00:58:30,107
GAME OVER, MAN!

1378
00:58:30,140 --> 00:58:32,110
OH, GREAT. NOW YOU'VE MADE
THE SUN GOD MAD.

1379
00:58:32,143 --> 00:58:34,378
GOOD ONE.

1380
00:58:34,412 --> 00:58:37,348
[GAOS SHRIEKS]

1381
00:58:37,382 --> 00:58:39,983
I'M THE SUN GOD. I'M MAD.

1382
00:58:40,017 --> 00:58:42,420
[GAOS SHRIEKS]

1383
00:58:42,453 --> 00:58:45,223
LET GO! I DON'T WANNA
GET MY HAIR WET.

1384
00:58:45,257 --> 00:58:47,325
HEY! LOOK AT THE MONSTER'S--

1385
00:58:47,358 --> 00:58:50,127
HEY, CHECK IT OUT,
A COUPLE OF MONSTERS
GOING AT IT. NEAT!

1386
00:58:50,160 --> 00:58:52,197
THERE'S SOMETHING YOU DON'T SEE
EVERY DAY, CHAUNCEY.

1387
00:58:52,230 --> 00:58:53,932
- WHAT'S THAT?
- COUPLE OF MONSTERS

1388
00:58:53,965 --> 00:58:57,902
- GOING AT IT.
- OH.

1389
00:58:57,935 --> 00:58:59,903
MOM, HE WON'T LET GO!

1390
00:58:59,937 --> 00:59:02,273
HEY!

1391
00:59:02,307 --> 00:59:04,408
HEY, KNOCK IT OFF
DOWN THERE.

1392
00:59:04,442 --> 00:59:06,177
I MEAN IT.

1393
00:59:06,210 --> 00:59:09,347
UGH. OH.

1394
00:59:09,380 --> 00:59:12,517
GOT A REAL TOEHOLD ON HIM,
DOESN'T HE?

1395
00:59:12,550 --> 00:59:15,587
OH! DO NOT FEED CHICKEN BONES
TO YOUR TURTLE.

1396
00:59:15,620 --> 00:59:18,590
NN-NN.

1397
00:59:18,623 --> 00:59:19,990
OH, I HOPE THAT'S NOT
MR. BUBBLE,

1398
00:59:20,023 --> 00:59:22,193
OR GAMERA'S GONNA GET
A KIDNEY INFECTION.

1399
00:59:24,562 --> 00:59:26,563
I'M TELLING YOU,
HE WAS 3,300 POUNDS

1400
00:59:26,597 --> 00:59:27,898
IF HE WAS AN OUNCE!

1401
00:59:27,932 --> 00:59:29,333
THE ONE THAT GOT AWAY.

1402
00:59:29,367 --> 00:59:31,468
[GAMERA ROARS]

1403
00:59:31,502 --> 00:59:33,905
IT'S TOO HOT!
THE WATER'S BOILING!

1404
00:59:33,938 --> 00:59:35,840
AAH!

1405
00:59:35,873 --> 00:59:39,443
[SERVO GURGLES]

1406
00:59:39,477 --> 00:59:41,045
- WELL, THAT'S IT.
LET'S GO, YOU GUYS.
- THAT'S THE END.

1407
00:59:41,078 --> 00:59:42,480
- THAT'S IT.
- ...OH.

1408
00:59:42,513 --> 00:59:44,982
- DARN.
- JEEZ, WHAT A NIGHT
THAT WAS LAST NIGHT.

1409
00:59:45,015 --> 00:59:47,585
YEAH, IF IT HADN'T BEEN
FOR OLD GAMERA HELPING OUT,

1410
00:59:47,618 --> 00:59:48,853
YOU'RE RIGHT.

1411
00:59:48,887 --> 00:59:51,388
YEAH, I LOST 50 BUCKS
ON THAT.

1412
00:59:51,422 --> 00:59:54,025
HEY. WHAT'S THAT THERE?

1413
00:59:54,058 --> 00:59:55,860
HEY. FIND A PENNY,
PICK IT UP.

1414
00:59:55,893 --> 00:59:57,195
ALL DAY LONG,
WE'LL HAVE GOOD LUCK.

1415
00:59:57,228 --> 01:00:00,230
LET'S GO!

1416
01:00:00,263 --> 01:00:02,100
HEY, LET'S GO
DOWN TO IT AND LOOK.

1417
01:00:02,133 --> 01:00:04,368
WHAT DO YOU SAY?

1418
01:00:04,402 --> 01:00:05,903
YUCK.

1419
01:00:05,937 --> 01:00:07,538
IT'S GAOS' FOOT!

1420
01:00:07,572 --> 01:00:09,440
I'LL GET THE SAUCE.
SHOULD I GET THE SAUCE?

1421
01:00:09,473 --> 01:00:11,875
I'LL GET THE SAUCE.

1422
01:00:11,908 --> 01:00:13,945
LATER THAT SAME YEAR.

1423
01:00:13,978 --> 01:00:15,680
WE SAW IT LYING
IN THE WATER HERE.

1424
01:00:15,713 --> 01:00:16,982
YEAH, DOWN HERE!

1425
01:00:17,015 --> 01:00:18,817
COME ON, QUINCY,
YOU GOTTA HELP US!

1426
01:00:18,850 --> 01:00:21,585
IT'S OVER HERE!

1427
01:00:21,618 --> 01:00:23,387
THIS WAS
NO BOATING ACCIDENT!

1428
01:00:23,420 --> 01:00:25,022
- --SMALLER NOW.
- YEAH.

1429
01:00:25,055 --> 01:00:26,823
IT WAS A LOT BIGGER
BEFORE, SEE?

1430
01:00:26,857 --> 01:00:28,827
OH, I SEE-- HUH?

1431
01:00:28,860 --> 01:00:30,862
HOW COULD IT SHRINK IN SIZE
IN HALF AN HOUR?

1432
01:00:30,895 --> 01:00:33,397
NO, I SWEAR, IT WAS A LOT BIGGER
WHEN WE FIRST SAW IT.

1433
01:00:33,430 --> 01:00:34,632
- UH-HUH.
- YOU'RE MAD!

1434
01:00:34,665 --> 01:00:36,467
NO, IT'S QUITE TRUE
WHAT HE SAID.

1435
01:00:36,500 --> 01:00:39,903
SEE, IT'S COLD WATER. HAVEN'T
YOU MEN-- OH, NEVER MIND.

1436
01:00:39,937 --> 01:00:41,572
SORRY.

1437
01:00:41,605 --> 01:00:44,275
I TELL YOU, WHEN I FIRST CAME
ACROSS IT DOWN BY THE BEACH,

1438
01:00:44,308 --> 01:00:46,077
IT WAS ALMOST
TWICE THAT SIZE.

1439
01:00:46,110 --> 01:00:48,345
AND THAT'S WHEN I STARTED
TALKING LIKE GEORGIE JESSEL.

1440
01:00:48,378 --> 01:00:51,082
IT MIGHT BE WORTHWHILE
CHECKING IT OUT ANYWAY.

1441
01:00:51,115 --> 01:00:52,883
WE MIGHT LEARN SOMETHING
FROM IT.

1442
01:00:52,917 --> 01:00:55,185
AND GOD KNOWS, WE NEED
ANY INFORMATION WE CAN GET.

1443
01:00:55,218 --> 01:00:56,520
YES, OF COURSE, SIR.

1444
01:00:56,553 --> 01:00:58,388
- MM-HMM.
- MM-HMM.

1445
01:00:58,422 --> 01:01:00,558
EW, THAT'S PROBABLY
HIS EARWAX.

1446
01:01:00,592 --> 01:01:02,427
UGH, POST-NASAL DRIP.

1447
01:01:06,563 --> 01:01:08,298
- AIR IT OUT, MAN.
- COME ON IN.

1448
01:01:08,332 --> 01:01:10,167
WELCOME TO MY HOME.

1449
01:01:10,200 --> 01:01:12,537
IT WAS FEATURED LAST MONTH IN
BETTER HOMES AND GARGOYLES.

1450
01:01:12,570 --> 01:01:14,638
EWW.

1451
01:01:14,672 --> 01:01:17,208
- UGH.
- BIG OLD HANGNAIL
THERE, HUH?

1452
01:01:17,242 --> 01:01:18,575
OW.

1453
01:01:18,608 --> 01:01:20,945
I'M GOING TO A DIFFERENT VET
NEXT TIME.

1454
01:01:20,978 --> 01:01:22,747
OOH, COOL.

1455
01:01:22,780 --> 01:01:24,982
HEY, I TOLD MY MOM
I WAS GONNA GROW ANOTHER FOOT,

1456
01:01:25,015 --> 01:01:26,717
AND SHE KNIT ME THREE SOCKS.

1457
01:01:26,750 --> 01:01:28,318
--THE NEXT CELL TYPE.

1458
01:01:28,352 --> 01:01:29,753
ADD FOUR.

1459
01:01:29,787 --> 01:01:32,523
IT'S TRUE. YOU'RE AS IMPOTENT
AS A DISH RAG, PHIL.

1460
01:01:32,557 --> 01:01:34,192
OOH.

1461
01:01:37,662 --> 01:01:41,132
WHO'S MAKING BEER?
I SMELL YEAST.

1462
01:01:41,165 --> 01:01:43,400
TO TEST AN ODD THEORY
THAT JUST OCCURRED TO ME.

1463
01:01:43,433 --> 01:01:45,970
- I'M A GUY.
- IT'S WORTH A TRY.

1464
01:01:46,003 --> 01:01:47,272
TRY OUT
THE ULTRAVIOLET TEST.

1465
01:01:47,305 --> 01:01:49,740
- YES.
- ULTRAVIOLET? SHE'S HERE?

1466
01:01:49,773 --> 01:01:51,942
ULTRAVIOLET TEST?
WHAT'S THE POINT?

1467
01:01:51,975 --> 01:01:53,277
NO POINT,
JUST SOMETHING TO DO.

1468
01:01:53,310 --> 01:01:55,647
--THE DECIDING FACTOR
IN ATTACKING THE BEAST.

1469
01:01:55,680 --> 01:01:57,182
IT DOES SEEM UNLIKELY.

1470
01:01:57,215 --> 01:01:58,715
BUT WE'VE GOT TO THE STAGE
WHERE WE'RE WILLING

1471
01:01:58,750 --> 01:02:00,885
TO CLUTCH AT STRAWS.

1472
01:02:00,918 --> 01:02:03,153
HEY, THEY CHAR-BROILED
HIS FOOT.

1473
01:02:03,187 --> 01:02:04,522
GET THE K.C. MASTERPIECE.

1474
01:02:04,555 --> 01:02:06,690
OOH.

1475
01:02:06,723 --> 01:02:08,525
AND HERE COMES
THE PONDEROSA HEAT LAMP.

1476
01:02:08,558 --> 01:02:10,293
IT KEEPS THE JO JO POTATOES
WARM.

1477
01:02:10,327 --> 01:02:12,663
ALL RIGHT. WE'RE READY
TO BEGIN THE TEST.

1478
01:02:12,697 --> 01:02:15,600
ALL RIGHT. NUMBER TWO PENCILS,
AND BOOKS OPEN.

1479
01:02:17,668 --> 01:02:19,737
[MACHINE WHIRS]

1480
01:02:25,910 --> 01:02:28,178
HOPE THIS DOESN'T
AFFECT THE TASTE.

1481
01:02:31,815 --> 01:02:33,683
OH NO, NO, NO.
IT'S COOKING UNEVENLY.

1482
01:02:33,717 --> 01:02:35,653
THEY NEED A MICRO-GO-ROUND.

1483
01:02:38,622 --> 01:02:41,925
BALLPARK FEET.
THEY SHRINK WHEN YOU COOK 'EM.

1484
01:02:41,958 --> 01:02:43,660
THEY SMELL LIKE IT, TOO.

1485
01:02:43,693 --> 01:02:45,262
WOOF.

1486
01:02:52,737 --> 01:02:54,105
- HMM?
- LOOK.

1487
01:02:54,138 --> 01:02:55,405
AT WHAT? OH.

1488
01:02:55,438 --> 01:02:58,542
TURN IT OFF.

1489
01:02:58,575 --> 01:03:00,343
GOSH, THAT LOOKS GOOD.
WHO WANTS HEEL?

1490
01:03:00,377 --> 01:03:02,747
I WAS RIGHT.
PURE ULTRAVIOLET RAYS

1491
01:03:02,780 --> 01:03:05,048
CAN EAT INTO TISSUE.

1492
01:03:05,082 --> 01:03:06,583
- I SEE.
- AHH.

1493
01:03:06,617 --> 01:03:08,018
WELL, IN THAT CASE THEN,

1494
01:03:08,052 --> 01:03:10,020
IF THE MONSTER
STAYS OUT IN THE SUN,

1495
01:03:10,053 --> 01:03:13,057
- IT MUST DIE, HUH?
- THAT'S RIGHT.

1496
01:03:13,090 --> 01:03:14,725
OOH, HE'S HARD ON SHOES.

1497
01:03:14,758 --> 01:03:16,727
CAN'T KEEP THIS KID
IN TENNIS SHOES, I TELL YA.

1498
01:03:16,760 --> 01:03:18,863
NN-NN.

1499
01:03:18,897 --> 01:03:20,732
[SERVO STRAINS]

1500
01:03:20,765 --> 01:03:22,933
OH, AND HE'S NEVER GONNA
PLAY PIANO AGAIN.

1501
01:03:22,967 --> 01:03:25,603
LOOK AT THAT.

1502
01:03:25,637 --> 01:03:29,207
[GAOS SHRIEKS]

1503
01:03:29,240 --> 01:03:32,108
AHH. YEAH.

1504
01:03:32,142 --> 01:03:33,810
OH YEAH, AND THE-- OOP.

1505
01:03:33,845 --> 01:03:35,178
[ALL]
AAH!

1506
01:03:35,212 --> 01:03:37,415
I DON'T BELIEVE I DID THAT!

1507
01:03:37,448 --> 01:03:39,450
OW! BOY, DID THAT HURT.

1508
01:03:39,483 --> 01:03:42,118
[CROW SIGHS]

1509
01:03:42,152 --> 01:03:43,753
THAT FOOT'S
NEVER GONNA HEAL.

1510
01:03:43,787 --> 01:03:45,557
[BOTS]
NN-NN.

1511
01:03:48,358 --> 01:03:51,162
ACTUALLY, HE'S SINGING
"I FEEL PRETTY."

1512
01:03:51,195 --> 01:03:53,430
- OH.
- YEP.

1513
01:03:53,463 --> 01:03:55,132
WELL, AS SOON AS
THE MORNING SUN CAME UP--

1514
01:03:55,165 --> 01:03:58,335
- LET'S GO FISHING.
- IT SORT OF CHANGED
IN ITS COLORS.

1515
01:03:58,368 --> 01:03:59,970
ALL ITS HEAD
WENT BRIGHT RED.

1516
01:04:00,003 --> 01:04:02,607
OH, I SEE.
A SORT OF DANGER SIGNAL.

1517
01:04:02,640 --> 01:04:04,008
WELL, IT DOES SEEM THAT
THE EXPERIMENT

1518
01:04:04,042 --> 01:04:05,943
HAS PROVED ONE THING
CONCLUSIVELY.

1519
01:04:05,977 --> 01:04:07,412
AND THAT IS, THE ONLY WAY
OF KILLING THE BEAST

1520
01:04:07,445 --> 01:04:08,778
IS TO KEEP IT OUT
IN THE SUNLIGHT.

1521
01:04:08,812 --> 01:04:10,915
OH, PREMATURELY AGE IT
TO DEATH.

1522
01:04:10,948 --> 01:04:12,517
BUT THAT WON'T BE EASY.

1523
01:04:12,550 --> 01:04:14,252
OUT OF SHEER
SELF-PRESERVATION,

1524
01:04:14,285 --> 01:04:16,087
THE MONSTER WON'T COME OUT
DURING THE DAYTIME.

1525
01:04:16,120 --> 01:04:18,122
WOULDN'T IT BE POSSIBLE
TO BUILD AN EXTRA-LARGE

1526
01:04:18,155 --> 01:04:20,190
ULTRAVIOLET-RAY PROJECTOR
AND ATTACK IT WITH THAT?

1527
01:04:20,223 --> 01:04:21,892
MAN, THAT GUY
THINKS ON HIS FEET,

1528
01:04:21,925 --> 01:04:23,460
- YOU KNOW THAT?
- MM-HMM.

1529
01:04:23,493 --> 01:04:24,862
WE CAN NEVER BUILD ONE
THAT WOULD BE LARGE ENOUGH

1530
01:04:24,895 --> 01:04:26,997
TO BE EFFECTIVE.
AND EVEN IF WE COULD BUILD ONE,

1531
01:04:27,030 --> 01:04:28,632
IT WOULD BE FAR TOO LARGE
TO BE MOBILE.

1532
01:04:28,665 --> 01:04:30,768
- MM-HMM.
- THE ONLY ANSWER I CAN SEE

1533
01:04:30,802 --> 01:04:32,670
IS LURE IT OUT
INTO THE DAYLIGHT--

1534
01:04:32,703 --> 01:04:34,538
AND BEAT THE DAYLIGHTS
OUT OF HIM!

1535
01:04:34,572 --> 01:04:36,307
I KID, THE DAYLIGHTS.

1536
01:04:36,340 --> 01:04:38,943
--KEEP IT ON THE RUN
UNTIL AFTER THE SUN CAME OUT.

1537
01:04:38,977 --> 01:04:41,312
SO THAT'S THE WAY
WE OUGHT TO BE MOVING NOW.

1538
01:04:41,345 --> 01:04:43,247
THERE HAS TO BE A WAY.

1539
01:04:43,280 --> 01:04:44,915
- LET'S THINK ABOUT IT.
- WHERE'S EIICHI?

1540
01:04:44,948 --> 01:04:47,150
--WITH SOME PLAN.
WHAT DO YOU SAY, CHIEF?

1541
01:04:47,183 --> 01:04:49,553
UH, I, UH, DIDN'T EXPECT
TO BE CALLED ON.

1542
01:04:49,587 --> 01:04:51,522
- I DON'T HAVE ANYTHING.
- IT'S VERY DIFFICULT

1543
01:04:51,555 --> 01:04:53,757
YES, IT IS.

1544
01:04:53,790 --> 01:04:56,260
- EIICHI.
- I CAN COME IN HERE,
I RULE THIS PLACE!

1545
01:04:56,293 --> 01:04:57,662
LET ME GO.

1546
01:04:57,695 --> 01:04:59,797
YOU SAW GAMERA FIGHT WITH GAOS.
IS THAT RIGHT?

1547
01:04:59,830 --> 01:05:01,698
- BOING.
- MM-HMM.
- HOW'D HE BEAT HIM?

1548
01:05:01,732 --> 01:05:03,333
- TELL ME, EH?
- YOU'RE INTERRUPTING

1549
01:05:03,367 --> 01:05:04,835
AN IMPORTANT MEETING,
DON'T YOU SEE?

1550
01:05:04,868 --> 01:05:06,170
YOU'RE FIRED!

1551
01:05:06,203 --> 01:05:08,105
- I'M SORRY--
- CAN HE FIRE HIS SISTER?

1552
01:05:08,138 --> 01:05:10,373
AH, THIS EIICHI HERE.

1553
01:05:10,407 --> 01:05:12,577
HE'S THE ONE WHO
RODE ON GAMERA'S BACK.

1554
01:05:12,610 --> 01:05:15,078
GAMERA'S A GOOD FRIEND
OF HIS, HUH?

1555
01:05:15,112 --> 01:05:16,913
HE'S A REAL EXPERT
ON MONSTERS NOW.

1556
01:05:16,947 --> 01:05:19,150
- YOU'RE JOKING.
- YES, I AM.

1557
01:05:19,183 --> 01:05:22,320
TELL ME, DIDN'T YOU GET GIDDY
UP ON GAMERA'S BACK?

1558
01:05:22,353 --> 01:05:24,555
- GIDDY?
- OH NO. GAMERA ALWAYS FLIES
STRAIGHT AHEAD

1559
01:05:24,588 --> 01:05:25,923
WITHOUT TURNING IT OFF.

1560
01:05:25,957 --> 01:05:28,158
THAT'S IT!
I COULD KISS YOU AGAIN!

1561
01:05:28,192 --> 01:05:29,427
I MEAN-- I'M KIDDING.

1562
01:05:29,460 --> 01:05:31,028
LET THE RECORD SHOW
I WAS KIDDING.

1563
01:05:31,062 --> 01:05:32,530
--THE ANSWER.
IF WE COULD ONLY

1564
01:05:32,563 --> 01:05:34,998
KEEP GAOS STILL
IN ONE PLACE.

1565
01:05:35,032 --> 01:05:37,267
AND THEN FIND SOME WAY
OF MAKING HIM DIZZY.

1566
01:05:37,302 --> 01:05:39,437
- DIZZY?
- [ALL] CHAMPAGNE!

1567
01:05:39,470 --> 01:05:40,705
ALL ANIMALS'
SENSE OF BALANCE

1568
01:05:40,738 --> 01:05:42,340
IS GOVERNED MAINLY
BY THE EARDRUMS.

1569
01:05:42,373 --> 01:05:44,575
THE INNER EAR
CONTROLS EQUILIBRIUM.

1570
01:05:44,608 --> 01:05:46,543
WE LOSE OUR BALANCE
WHEN WE SPIN AROUND RAPIDLY.

1571
01:05:46,577 --> 01:05:48,145
I'LL DEMONSTRATE. WHOO...

1572
01:05:48,178 --> 01:05:50,113
--OF LURING GAOS
INTO A PLATFORM.

1573
01:05:50,147 --> 01:05:51,382
A PRATFALL?

1574
01:05:51,415 --> 01:05:53,450
--ARRANGE FOR THE PLATFORM
TO REVOLVE RAPIDLY.

1575
01:05:53,483 --> 01:05:55,285
THE MONSTER WILL BE
COMPLETELY UNABLE TO MOVE.

1576
01:05:55,318 --> 01:05:57,322
- HMM.
- THEN KEEP HIM THERE
UNTIL DAYLIGHT.

1577
01:05:57,355 --> 01:06:00,423
ALL RIGHT, BUT WHERE COULD
WE GET A PLATFORM OF THAT SIZE?

1578
01:06:00,457 --> 01:06:01,758
THERE ISN'T ENOUGH TIME
TO BUILD ONE

1579
01:06:01,792 --> 01:06:03,560
OF THE SIZE THAT WE NEED.

1580
01:06:03,593 --> 01:06:06,463
- I GOT ONE IN MY ROOM!
- --UPSTAIRS, HERE!

1581
01:06:06,497 --> 01:06:08,265
ON THE ROOF.

1582
01:06:08,298 --> 01:06:09,500
YOU KNOW, HE'S RIGHT AGAIN!

1583
01:06:09,533 --> 01:06:11,035
OPERATION WHIRLYBIRD

1584
01:06:11,068 --> 01:06:14,105
COMMENCES NOW!

1585
01:06:14,138 --> 01:06:15,840
HOLIDAY INN,
TOWERING A FULL

1586
01:06:15,873 --> 01:06:18,408
FOUR STORIES OVER THE CITY.

1587
01:06:22,480 --> 01:06:24,515
THE MEMBERS OF
THE FORCE TEN FROM NAVARONE

1588
01:06:24,548 --> 01:06:25,917
SNAP INTO ACTION.

1589
01:06:25,950 --> 01:06:28,852
HEADQUARTERS.
SUB-STATION HERE.

1590
01:06:28,885 --> 01:06:31,288
FIREMAN ABILITY HAS BEEN
INCREASED BY OVER 300%.

1591
01:06:31,322 --> 01:06:34,092
ADDITIONAL FIRE CAN BE MADE
AVAILABLE NOW.

1592
01:06:34,125 --> 01:06:36,093
- GOOD.
- GOT IT.

1593
01:06:36,127 --> 01:06:38,462
ADAM AND EVE IN A RAFT.
WRECK 'EM.

1594
01:06:38,495 --> 01:06:40,732
- ALL RIGHT.
- AND WE NEED MORE GLOVES.

1595
01:06:43,167 --> 01:06:44,402
THEY LOVE THEIR GLOVES.

1596
01:06:44,435 --> 01:06:46,170
HEY, SIR,
IT'S THE COFFEE PERCOLATOR.

1597
01:06:46,203 --> 01:06:48,438
WE'RE GONNA GET HIM
REALLY CAFFEINED UP

1598
01:06:48,472 --> 01:06:50,673
AND GIVE HIM A MEAN BUZZ.
THAT'S IT.

1599
01:06:50,708 --> 01:06:52,977
HEY, IT'S A SWINGIN' 60s
APARTMENT.

1600
01:06:53,010 --> 01:06:54,412
THINK IT'LL BE
STRONG ENOUGH?

1601
01:06:54,445 --> 01:06:56,913
WELL, GAOS IS OVER
200 FEET LONG.

1602
01:06:56,947 --> 01:06:59,183
MUST WEIGH 25 TONS.

1603
01:06:59,217 --> 01:07:00,785
WELL, I WOULDN'T WANT HIM
IN THE TOP BUNK.

1604
01:07:00,818 --> 01:07:02,285
- MM-MM.
- GOOD WORK.

1605
01:07:02,318 --> 01:07:04,155
INFORM THE SUB-STATION MEN.

1606
01:07:04,188 --> 01:07:05,688
THEN TAKE THE REST
OF THE DAY OFF.

1607
01:07:05,723 --> 01:07:07,057
--TO STAND UP
ON THAT THING, HUH?

1608
01:07:07,090 --> 01:07:08,625
THAT'S A SECRET
YOU'LL DISCOVER LATER.

1609
01:07:08,658 --> 01:07:11,062
OLD MAN!

1610
01:07:11,095 --> 01:07:13,263
THE CONTROL.
IT'S BEEN REINFORCED.

1611
01:07:13,297 --> 01:07:15,165
ALL THE WIRING'S
BEEN COMPLETED NOW.

1612
01:07:15,198 --> 01:07:17,200
- GOT IT.
- GET IT. GOOD.

1613
01:07:17,233 --> 01:07:19,770
CAPTAIN, HAS ALL THE WIRING
BEEN COMPLETED YET?

1614
01:07:19,803 --> 01:07:22,707
- YES, SIR.
- [ALL HUM]

1615
01:07:22,740 --> 01:07:24,875
THE PRESIDENT.

1616
01:07:24,908 --> 01:07:27,978
COOL WASH.

1617
01:07:28,012 --> 01:07:29,647
I GUESS I'LL JUST HAVE
THE DELI STACKER

1618
01:07:29,680 --> 01:07:32,883
ON THE NINE GRAIN.

1619
01:07:32,917 --> 01:07:34,818
[CROW MUTTERS]

1620
01:07:34,852 --> 01:07:38,122
EITHER MY EARS ARE BURNING,
OR SOMEONE'S ORDERING LUNCH.

1621
01:07:42,827 --> 01:07:45,997
OH, THEY'RE BRINGING DOWN
THE GO-GO CAGE TO DANCE IN HERE?

1622
01:07:46,030 --> 01:07:48,532
WATCH IT. ALL RIGHT.
ALL RIGHT. ALL RIGHT.

1623
01:07:48,565 --> 01:07:50,902
- ALL RIGHT.
- CHECK THE FLARES.
GET READY NOW.

1624
01:07:50,935 --> 01:07:54,438
GET BUCKY FULLER ON THE LINE!
WE DON'T KNOW HOW TO FINISH IT!

1625
01:07:54,472 --> 01:07:56,473
[MEN CLAMOR]

1626
01:07:58,608 --> 01:08:00,210
HEY, CHECK--
CHECK ON THE MIC.

1627
01:08:00,243 --> 01:08:02,412
CHECK ONE, CHECK TWO. COULD
I GET SOME MORE MONITOR HERE?

1628
01:08:02,447 --> 01:08:05,115
- TWO, TWO.
- BREAKER-NINER-ONE.

1629
01:08:05,148 --> 01:08:07,685
- BREAKER-NINER-ONE.
- GOOD, PUT IT IN NOW.

1630
01:08:09,420 --> 01:08:11,022
HEY, BOSS!

1631
01:08:11,055 --> 01:08:13,957
SKINNY AND FATTY FROM
THE CHILDREN'S FILM FESTIVAL.

1632
01:08:13,990 --> 01:08:15,325
I SUPPOSE YOU COULD
CALL IT A FOUNTAIN.

1633
01:08:15,358 --> 01:08:16,727
- PETE FOUNTAIN?
- NO.

1634
01:08:16,760 --> 01:08:18,128
GAOS IS KNOWN TO LIKE
HUMAN BLOOD.

1635
01:08:18,162 --> 01:08:19,997
- HEY, BUT WHO DOESN'T?
- --WILL SPRAY OUT A SUBSTANCE

1636
01:08:20,030 --> 01:08:22,098
WHICH RESEMBLES HUMAN BLOOD,
BOTH IN SMELL AND IN TASTE.

1637
01:08:22,132 --> 01:08:24,768
- WHO TESTED IT?
- WE'RE HOPING IT'S GOING
TO LURE HIM TO THE PEDESTAL.

1638
01:08:24,802 --> 01:08:26,103
UGH...

1639
01:08:26,137 --> 01:08:27,370
THE SCIENTISTS ARE
WORKING ON HOW TO MAKE

1640
01:08:27,403 --> 01:08:29,207
A SUITABLE LIQUID
IN THE LABORATORY.

1641
01:08:29,240 --> 01:08:30,908
THEY'RE FINDING IT DIFFICULT
TO GET JUST THE RIGHT QUANTITY.

1642
01:08:30,942 --> 01:08:32,342
SO WHY DON'T YOU TWO
HEAD OVER THERE?

1643
01:08:32,375 --> 01:08:34,110
DO YOU THINK
IT'LL WORK OUT ALL RIGHT?

1644
01:08:34,145 --> 01:08:35,512
IT'S SIMPLY GOT
TO WORK OUT ALL RIGHT.

1645
01:08:35,545 --> 01:08:37,715
- NOW BACK TO WORK.
- RIGHT.

1646
01:08:37,748 --> 01:08:39,583
YEAH, I'M SENDING OVER
A COUPLE OF BLOOD DONORS.

1647
01:08:39,617 --> 01:08:42,953
[CROW CACKLES]

1648
01:08:42,987 --> 01:08:44,455
- THE SHUTTLES ARE READY--
- ONE COOKIE

1649
01:08:44,488 --> 01:08:45,923
AND A CHEESE DINGLEBERRY
AND A BOUNCE-AROUND.

1650
01:08:45,957 --> 01:08:49,393
COME ON, PICK IT UP!
PICK IT UP!

1651
01:08:49,427 --> 01:08:52,295
- HEY, BOSS-- MESSENGER.
- RIGHT.

1652
01:08:52,328 --> 01:08:55,332
IT'S AN ARMY OF METER-MEN.

1653
01:08:57,935 --> 01:09:01,205
- MORNING!
- MORNING! HAD YOUR COFFEE?

1654
01:09:01,238 --> 01:09:02,840
DO YOU HAVE
A MINUTE TO SPARE?

1655
01:09:02,873 --> 01:09:04,208
YES, WHAT IS IT?

1656
01:09:04,242 --> 01:09:06,210
UH, YOU SEE,
WE WANT TO WITHDRAW

1657
01:09:06,243 --> 01:09:07,645
OUR PREVIOUS OBJECTION
TO THE ROAD.

1658
01:09:07,678 --> 01:09:10,013
- AND SUBMIT A NEW ONE.
- DO YOU NOW?

1659
01:09:10,047 --> 01:09:12,583
WE WANT TO SELL THE LAND NOW,
AT THE PRICE YOU OFFERED.

1660
01:09:12,617 --> 01:09:14,785
WHAT DO YOU SAY?

1661
01:09:14,818 --> 01:09:16,920
THAT ALL THE WORK ON THE ROAD
HAS ALREADY BEEN STOPPED NOW.

1662
01:09:16,953 --> 01:09:18,588
WE MAY CHANGE THE COURSE.

1663
01:09:18,622 --> 01:09:21,458
[MEN CLAMOR]

1664
01:09:21,492 --> 01:09:23,360
YOU WILL HAVE TO WAIT.

1665
01:09:23,393 --> 01:09:25,462
I'LL TELL MY BOSS,
AND HE'LL GET IN TOUCH WITH YOU.

1666
01:09:25,495 --> 01:09:28,332
NOW I'VE GOT THIS
MONSTER THING TO DEAL WITH.

1667
01:09:28,365 --> 01:09:32,235
ALL RIGHT, LET'S GO.

1668
01:09:32,268 --> 01:09:36,240
[SERVO GRUMBLES]

1669
01:09:36,273 --> 01:09:37,842
AND WHAT THE DEVIL DO YOU THINK
YOU'RE DOING OUT HERE?

1670
01:09:37,875 --> 01:09:40,277
HEY, YOU'RE SUPPOSED TO BE HOME
MILKING THE COWS, OLD MAN.

1671
01:09:40,310 --> 01:09:42,145
EH? IF YOU ARE
WEAKENING NOW,

1672
01:09:42,178 --> 01:09:43,413
YOU WILL LOSE IT ALL.

1673
01:09:43,447 --> 01:09:45,248
HOW MANY TIMES
DO I HAVE TO TELL YOU?

1674
01:09:45,282 --> 01:09:46,850
JUST DO EXACTLY
WHAT WE AGREED, HUH?

1675
01:09:46,883 --> 01:09:48,685
- [SERVO GRUNTS]
- LISTEN, THOUGH,
ARE YOU QUITE SURE

1676
01:09:48,718 --> 01:09:50,020
THAT WE'RE
DOING THE RIGHT THING?

1677
01:09:50,053 --> 01:09:51,722
THEY SAY THEY MAY EVEN CHANGE
THE COURSE OF THE ROAD.

1678
01:09:51,755 --> 01:09:53,557
NONSENSE. RUMORS!

1679
01:09:53,590 --> 01:09:55,025
- YOU'LL BELIEVE ANYTHING.
- INNUENDO.

1680
01:09:55,058 --> 01:09:56,627
- YOU LEAVE IT TO ME, WILL YOU?
- [CAR HORN HONKS]

1681
01:09:56,660 --> 01:09:59,363
HEY, CAN YOU GET THE SUBPLOT
OFF THE ROAD PLEASE?

1682
01:09:59,397 --> 01:10:02,065
COME ON.

1683
01:10:02,098 --> 01:10:03,667
TRYING TO KILL
A MONSTER HERE.

1684
01:10:03,700 --> 01:10:05,202
CONVOY,
STARRING ALI MacGRAW.

1685
01:10:05,235 --> 01:10:06,503
ALL PREPARATIONS COMPLETED.

1686
01:10:06,537 --> 01:10:09,072
- ALL RIGHT.
- OKAY, YOU CAN SIT DOWN THEN.

1687
01:10:09,105 --> 01:10:12,242
- I FEEL SO SILLY.
- SIT DOWN.

1688
01:10:12,275 --> 01:10:14,778
ALL THIS WORK TO REDESIGN.

1689
01:10:14,812 --> 01:10:18,615
I STILL SMELL BEER.
I DON'T UNDERSTAND IT.

1690
01:10:18,648 --> 01:10:21,052
- DR. AOKI.
- TIME FOR KARAOKE.

1691
01:10:21,085 --> 01:10:22,753
[SERVO CHUCKLES]

1692
01:10:22,787 --> 01:10:25,288
- LOOK AT THIS NOW.
- YES.

1693
01:10:25,322 --> 01:10:27,023
- YOU'VE DONE IT.
- IT'S A BABY BOY.

1694
01:10:27,057 --> 01:10:29,327
ALL OF THE QUALITIES
OF HUMAN BLOOD.

1695
01:10:29,360 --> 01:10:31,595
I'M GRATEFUL.
I'M GRATEFUL!

1696
01:10:31,628 --> 01:10:34,130
IT'S A GRAPE-LIKE BEVERAGE.

1697
01:10:34,163 --> 01:10:36,500
[ALL]
♪ 53 BOTTLES OF BLOOD
ON THE WALL ♪

1698
01:10:36,533 --> 01:10:38,602
♪ 53 BOTTLES OF BLOOD ♪

1699
01:10:38,635 --> 01:10:41,638
♪ TAKE ONE DOWN,
WRITE PIG ON THE WALL ♪

1700
01:10:41,672 --> 01:10:44,140
THE WIND'S BLOWING IN FROM
THE WEST NOW. JUST ABOUT
THE RIGHT VELOCITY.

1701
01:10:44,173 --> 01:10:46,777
I DIDN'T KNOW TENNESSEE TUXEDO
WAS IN THIS MOVIE.

1702
01:10:46,810 --> 01:10:48,978
GOOD. COMMANDER.

1703
01:10:49,012 --> 01:10:50,580
OH, TIME TO GO.

1704
01:10:50,613 --> 01:10:52,348
- OH.
- EVERYTHING'S IDEAL

1705
01:10:52,382 --> 01:10:53,650
- LET'S DO IT.
- LET'S FALL IN LOVE.

1706
01:10:53,683 --> 01:10:56,153
SET THE TRAP TONIGHT.

1707
01:10:56,187 --> 01:10:59,357
I AGREE. CONTACT
ALL OPERATIONAL POINTS.

1708
01:10:59,390 --> 01:11:01,392
RIGHT.

1709
01:11:08,565 --> 01:11:10,700
AND THIS-- UP BOY, UP!
COME ON, BOY, COME ON!

1710
01:11:10,733 --> 01:11:12,737
UP! THROUGH THE HOOP!
COME ON, BOY! UP!

1711
01:11:12,770 --> 01:11:15,405
D'AH, HIS NAME
USED TO BE LIGHTNING.

1712
01:11:15,438 --> 01:11:17,340
COME ON, YOU MISERABLE
SON OF A-- COME ON!

1713
01:11:17,373 --> 01:11:18,975
WELL, UM, WELL,
THAT'S WHAT IT LOOKS LIKE

1714
01:11:19,008 --> 01:11:20,543
AFTER HE JUMPS
THROUGH THE HOOP.

1715
01:11:20,577 --> 01:11:22,713
- THANK YOU,
LADIES AND GENTLEMEN.
- [CANNED APPLAUSE]

1716
01:11:22,747 --> 01:11:24,247
THANK YOU. AND...

1717
01:11:24,280 --> 01:11:26,083
HEY, THANK YOU.
THANK YOU VERY MUCH.

1718
01:11:26,117 --> 01:11:27,550
LET'S KEEP IT GOING
FOR TOM SERVO

1719
01:11:27,583 --> 01:11:29,487
- AND GROMIT, THE WONDER DOG.
- [CANNED APPLAUSE]

1720
01:11:29,520 --> 01:11:31,622
THANK YOU. THANK YOU.
THANK YOU VERY MUCH.

1721
01:11:31,655 --> 01:11:33,990
WE'RE GOING TO HAVE THEM BACK
REALLY, REALLY SOON.

1722
01:11:34,023 --> 01:11:36,660
A FINE, FINE PERFORMANCE
BY THOSE TWO YOUNGSTERS.

1723
01:11:36,693 --> 01:11:39,797
AND NOW, BEFORE WE BRING OUT
OUR NEXT GUEST,

1724
01:11:39,830 --> 01:11:42,332
I'D LIKE TO SAY HELLO
TO A VERY, VERY SPECIAL LADY

1725
01:11:42,332 --> 01:11:44,368
HERE IN THE AUDIENCE TONIGHT.
WHERE IS SHE?

1726
01:11:44,435 --> 01:11:46,070
OH, THERE SHE IS.

1727
01:11:46,137 --> 01:11:47,872
HI-- HI, EVERYBODY.

1728
01:11:47,938 --> 01:11:49,540
THANK YOU, DEAR. THANK YOU.

1729
01:11:49,573 --> 01:11:52,142
GYPSY'S IN TOWN THIS WEEK,
TAKING OVER FOR PAT CARROLL

1730
01:11:52,175 --> 01:11:55,545
IN GERTRUDE STEIN,
GERTRUDE STEIN, GERTRUDE STEIN.

1731
01:11:55,545 --> 01:11:57,848
BUT NOW, RIGHT HERE
IN OUR SATELLITE,

1732
01:11:57,882 --> 01:11:59,483
A BRIGHT YOUNG JUGGLER
AND MAGICIAN.

1733
01:11:59,550 --> 01:12:00,850
LET'S HAVE A BIG
ROUND OF APPLAUSE

1734
01:12:00,883 --> 01:12:03,087
FOR GAOS THE GREAT.

1735
01:12:07,057 --> 01:12:09,258
HEY! GET THE PLATES.

1736
01:12:09,292 --> 01:12:11,562
HEY! HEY! HEY!

1737
01:12:11,595 --> 01:12:13,563
HEY!

1738
01:12:19,268 --> 01:12:21,672
NUMBER TWO--
GET THE NEXT ONE.

1739
01:12:23,407 --> 01:12:25,008
OW. OW-OW-OW.

1740
01:12:25,075 --> 01:12:27,277
[SERVO MUTTERS]

1741
01:12:27,310 --> 01:12:29,278
THE FIRST ONE NOW!
THE FIRST-- OH!

1742
01:12:29,312 --> 01:12:31,915
GOOD, GET IT! COME ON.

1743
01:12:31,948 --> 01:12:35,685
AY-- HEY!

1744
01:12:35,718 --> 01:12:38,388
OW. DOGGONE IT.

1745
01:12:38,422 --> 01:12:39,757
YOU'RE LOSING 'EM.
JUGGLE OR SOMETHING.

1746
01:12:39,790 --> 01:12:41,858
COME ON.

1747
01:12:41,892 --> 01:12:43,227
COME ON. OH--

1748
01:12:43,260 --> 01:12:44,862
PLEASE, COME ON. THIRD ONE.

1749
01:12:44,895 --> 01:12:46,930
GET BACK TO THE FIRST ONE--

1750
01:12:46,963 --> 01:12:48,565
[SERVO MUMBLES]

1751
01:12:48,598 --> 01:12:50,667
- THANK YOU, THANK YOU.
- AND NOW, FOR THE YOUNGSTERS,

1752
01:12:50,700 --> 01:12:54,505
WE HAVE TO CUT AWAY NOW FOR
THE YOUNGSTERS' COMMERCIAL SIGN.

1753
01:12:54,538 --> 01:12:56,540
YOU GUYS ARE WORSE THAN
ALLEN AND ROSSI.

1754
01:12:56,573 --> 01:12:57,842
THANK YOU.

1755
01:13:05,982 --> 01:13:07,717
[PEOPLE CLAMOR]

1756
01:13:07,752 --> 01:13:09,085
YOU TOLD ME
YOU COULD SPIN PLATES.

1757
01:13:09,118 --> 01:13:10,920
WELL, I THOUGHT I COULD.

1758
01:13:10,953 --> 01:13:13,123
YOU GUYS SHOULD BE ON
THE GONG SHOW.

1759
01:13:13,157 --> 01:13:15,092
OOH.

1760
01:13:19,797 --> 01:13:22,198
HERE WE GO.

1761
01:13:23,967 --> 01:13:25,802
PULL THE PRESSURE UP HIGHER!

1762
01:13:25,835 --> 01:13:28,438
HEY, IT'S A BLOOD ATOMIZER.

1763
01:13:28,472 --> 01:13:30,207
- HEY.
- AND I WAS WORRIED
ABOUT FRION

1764
01:13:30,240 --> 01:13:31,475
WRECKING THE ENVIRONMENT.

1765
01:13:31,508 --> 01:13:33,410
EWW.

1766
01:13:33,443 --> 01:13:35,545
[CROW AAH'S]

1767
01:13:39,517 --> 01:13:41,585
HEY, HE LOVES RUNNING
THROUGH THE SPRINKLER.

1768
01:13:43,353 --> 01:13:45,655
- MUST NOT BE HIS TYPE.
- NN-NN.

1769
01:13:47,423 --> 01:13:50,360
THIS IS A GREAT VIEW
UP HERE.

1770
01:13:52,695 --> 01:13:56,633
- OOH.
- HE'S MAD 'CAUSE
IT'S LAST CALL.

1771
01:13:56,667 --> 01:13:58,035
WHOA!

1772
01:13:58,068 --> 01:13:58,968
LOOK OUT! GET DOWN!

1773
01:13:59,002 --> 01:14:01,372
GET DOWN WITH IT WITH...

1774
01:14:01,405 --> 01:14:03,407
[GAOS SHRIEKS]

1775
01:14:03,440 --> 01:14:05,442
UH-OH.

1776
01:14:09,012 --> 01:14:11,882
[BOTS MIMIC PLANE NOISES]

1777
01:14:11,915 --> 01:14:13,317
PUT THE PRESSURE ON HIGHER!

1778
01:14:13,350 --> 01:14:16,787
WHAT, THE BLOOD PRESSURE?

1779
01:14:16,820 --> 01:14:18,222
OKAY, LET'S FACE IT.
HE LIKES BLOOD,

1780
01:14:18,255 --> 01:14:19,657
BUT NOT THE WAY YOU MAKE IT.

1781
01:14:19,690 --> 01:14:23,360
OOH.

1782
01:14:23,393 --> 01:14:25,162
ALL RIGHT,
IT'S A LAST RESORT,

1783
01:14:25,195 --> 01:14:27,230
BUT SEND UP
THE PEEL-AND-EAT HUMANS.

1784
01:14:27,263 --> 01:14:29,867
OOH.

1785
01:14:29,900 --> 01:14:32,937
WELL, IT'S PRETTY.
YOU GOTTA ADMIT THAT, DON'T YOU?

1786
01:14:35,005 --> 01:14:37,975
AW, THAT DID IT.
HE'S GONNA HAVE A FACIAL NOW.

1787
01:14:38,008 --> 01:14:40,043
MM. I SHOULDN'T REALLY,

1788
01:14:40,077 --> 01:14:42,045
BUT HERE GOES.

1789
01:14:42,078 --> 01:14:43,313
- EW.
- OH.

1790
01:14:43,347 --> 01:14:45,915
I SAID A "BUD LIGHT,"
NOT A "BLOOD LIGHT."

1791
01:14:45,948 --> 01:14:47,583
LOOKS MORE LIKE
TAHITIAN TREAT.

1792
01:14:47,617 --> 01:14:50,453
OOH.

1793
01:14:50,487 --> 01:14:52,555
[MACHINES WHIR]

1794
01:14:52,588 --> 01:14:55,492
SET IT TO 33 RPMs.

1795
01:14:58,528 --> 01:15:00,463
WHOA, EITHER I'M SPINNING,

1796
01:15:00,497 --> 01:15:03,133
OR THIS IS SOME
REALLY GOOD BLOOD HERE.

1797
01:15:04,902 --> 01:15:06,437
- FASTER NOW!
- RIGHT!

1798
01:15:06,470 --> 01:15:07,905
FASTER!

1799
01:15:07,938 --> 01:15:10,140
DID YOU WANNA GO FASTER?

1800
01:15:10,173 --> 01:15:12,275
[ALL]
WHEE!

1801
01:15:12,308 --> 01:15:14,545
GET THE SPEED HIGHER!

1802
01:15:14,578 --> 01:15:16,447
THAT HOWARD JOHNSON
WAS DESIGNED FOR SPEED.

1803
01:15:16,480 --> 01:15:19,248
--I'M SURE THAT'S SAFE
FOR AT LEAST THREE HOURS.

1804
01:15:21,452 --> 01:15:23,520
- SO GOOFY.
- TOP SPEED NOW!

1805
01:15:23,553 --> 01:15:25,755
OPERATION GOOFY
NOW IN EFFECT.

1806
01:15:31,160 --> 01:15:34,397
IT'S GOOD, BUT IT'S NOT
AS GOOD AS BLOOD CLASSIC.

1807
01:15:34,430 --> 01:15:37,033
- WHAT IS IT RIGHT NOW?
- THREE MINUTES.

1808
01:15:40,703 --> 01:15:43,373
IS HE SUPPOSED TO THINK
HE'S TAKING DANCE CLASS?

1809
01:15:43,407 --> 01:15:45,242
I'M NOT...

1810
01:15:46,877 --> 01:15:50,380
OOH. OOH!

1811
01:15:50,413 --> 01:15:52,048
- SOMETHING WRONG.
- SOMETHING SERIOUS?

1812
01:15:52,082 --> 01:15:53,450
WE'RE JUST GONNA DIE,
THAT'S ALL.

1813
01:15:53,483 --> 01:15:55,418
OH, WELL-- OH.

1814
01:15:58,055 --> 01:16:00,323
- OOH.
- NOW LOOK!
THE POWER'S GOING.

1815
01:16:03,027 --> 01:16:06,997
NOTHING LIKE A BLOODY MARY
IN THE MORNING.

1816
01:16:07,030 --> 01:16:09,265
- HOW LONG TILL SUNRISE?
- JUST ONE MINUTE.

1817
01:16:09,298 --> 01:16:10,800
TEQUILA SUNRISE?

1818
01:16:10,833 --> 01:16:12,868
LOOK, THE SUN'S
COMING UP NOW.

1819
01:16:12,902 --> 01:16:14,772
RIDIN' WITH LADY LUCK!

1820
01:16:14,805 --> 01:16:17,040
OH GOOD, THEY PUT HIM
ON A BIG MECHANICAL BULL NOW.

1821
01:16:17,073 --> 01:16:19,442
THAT'LL REALLY SCREW HIM UP.

1822
01:16:19,475 --> 01:16:21,745
YOU KNOW, HE GETS VIOLENT
WHEN HE DRINKS FROM THAT.

1823
01:16:21,778 --> 01:16:23,413
YEAH, THAT BLOOD'S GOING
RIGHT TO HIS HEAD.

1824
01:16:23,447 --> 01:16:25,048
--HELP NOW.

1825
01:16:25,082 --> 01:16:27,383
IT MUST BE WEAKENING.

1826
01:16:27,417 --> 01:16:28,818
OH, NOW LOOK,
HE'S EMBARRASSED.

1827
01:16:28,852 --> 01:16:30,687
NOW, IF YOU HAD A HEAD
SHAPED LIKE A DIXIE CUP,

1828
01:16:30,720 --> 01:16:34,490
- YOU'D BE EMBARRASSED TOO.
- YOU GOT ME THERE.

1829
01:16:34,523 --> 01:16:36,860
- WHAT'S HAPPENING?
- POWER'S GOING!

1830
01:16:36,893 --> 01:16:38,528
I DON'T THINK THE SUB-STATION'S
GONNA HOLD OUT!

1831
01:16:38,562 --> 01:16:40,797
- WE ONLY NEED FIVE MINUTES.
- FIVE MINUTES!

1832
01:16:40,830 --> 01:16:44,768
THERE ISN'T ANY POWER
COMING THROUGH AT ALL NOW!

1833
01:16:44,802 --> 01:16:48,205
WOULDN'T PAY THE BILL.

1834
01:16:48,238 --> 01:16:50,907
- WHAT'S UP?
- IT'S GONE. IT'S GONE.

1835
01:16:55,712 --> 01:16:57,447
SUB-STATION'S BURNING NOW!

1836
01:16:57,480 --> 01:16:59,817
WE'LL HAVE TO GO
TO SCHLOTZSKY'S.

1837
01:17:10,027 --> 01:17:12,695
[ALL]
FINISH IT! FINISH IT!

1838
01:17:12,728 --> 01:17:14,665
WHOO!

1839
01:17:14,698 --> 01:17:17,533
AH-- AAH--

1840
01:17:17,567 --> 01:17:21,270
I NEVER LIKED YOU!
I NEVER LIKED YOU!

1841
01:17:21,303 --> 01:17:22,538
COME HERE!

1842
01:17:22,572 --> 01:17:25,042
POOR SLOB, SOMEBODY BETTER
CALL HIM A SOBER CAB.

1843
01:17:25,075 --> 01:17:27,677
LOOK AT HIM!

1844
01:17:27,710 --> 01:17:30,280
NOW THAT'S-- THAT'S GETTING
CRUSHED, ISN'T IT, STEVE?

1845
01:17:30,313 --> 01:17:33,983
WE'RE DEAD, AREN'T WE?

1846
01:17:34,017 --> 01:17:37,353
- THAT WOULD BE US.
- MAKE A FOUNTAIN OF BLOOD.

1847
01:17:37,387 --> 01:17:39,255
I DON'T BELIEVE IT...

1848
01:17:42,325 --> 01:17:44,493
THERE HE GOES AGAIN.

1849
01:17:44,527 --> 01:17:46,597
OOH.

1850
01:17:46,630 --> 01:17:47,897
...OR SOMETHING.

1851
01:17:47,930 --> 01:17:49,532
HE MUST REALLY PIT OUT SHIRTS,
YOU KNOW?

1852
01:17:49,565 --> 01:17:51,802
YEAH, I THINK SO.

1853
01:17:51,835 --> 01:17:54,872
[CROW COUGHS]

1854
01:17:54,905 --> 01:17:57,707
HUH. KINDA HANDY.

1855
01:17:57,740 --> 01:18:00,043
OH, HE'S GONNA GET
PULLED OVER FOR SURE.

1856
01:18:00,077 --> 01:18:01,845
YEAH.

1857
01:18:01,878 --> 01:18:03,313
UH, HONEY, COULD YOU HAND ME

1858
01:18:03,347 --> 01:18:05,615
THAT "BIRDS OF JAPAN" BOOK?

1859
01:18:05,648 --> 01:18:07,083
A FLASH-BULLETIN!

1860
01:18:07,117 --> 01:18:09,285
THE LATEST OF MEN'S EFFORTS
TO DESTROY THE MONSTER GAOS

1861
01:18:09,318 --> 01:18:11,287
HAVE FAILED MISERABLY.

1862
01:18:11,320 --> 01:18:12,822
THERE SEEMS TO BE
NO WAY TO DESTROY

1863
01:18:12,855 --> 01:18:15,425
THIS MONSTROUS
AND DANGEROUS BEAST.

1864
01:18:15,458 --> 01:18:17,293
THE EFFORTS OF SCIENTISTS
HAVE FAILED,

1865
01:18:17,327 --> 01:18:19,797
- AND PEOPLE'S HOPES
ARE FADING.
- AWW.

1866
01:18:19,830 --> 01:18:21,197
MY HOPE IS FADING.

1867
01:18:21,230 --> 01:18:24,802
IF ONLY GAMERA
WOULD COME BACK.

1868
01:18:24,835 --> 01:18:27,203
THAT'S IT! I COULD KISS YOU!

1869
01:18:27,237 --> 01:18:29,305
FOR THE THIRD TIME!

1870
01:18:29,338 --> 01:18:31,508
MAYBE NOT.

1871
01:18:31,542 --> 01:18:33,477
- [MEN CLAMOR]
- OH, SO WHAT IS THIS?

1872
01:18:33,510 --> 01:18:37,413
HOW GREEN IS MY VALLEY,
ALL OF A SUDDEN?

1873
01:18:37,447 --> 01:18:39,448
OH, EIGHT BOXES
OF LITTLE DEBBIES.

1874
01:18:39,482 --> 01:18:42,252
HE'S TOO BIG TO GET UP NOW.

1875
01:18:42,285 --> 01:18:44,287
HAS HE GROWN?

1876
01:18:44,320 --> 01:18:46,423
- WHAT IS IT? WHAT IS IT?
- HEADMAN,

1877
01:18:46,457 --> 01:18:47,890
THEY'RE NOT
GOING TO BUY THE LAND.

1878
01:18:47,923 --> 01:18:49,225
THAT'S RIGHT,
AND IF WE HADN'T LISTENED

1879
01:18:49,258 --> 01:18:51,027
TO YOUR STUPID ADVICE,
WE COULD'VE ALL HAD MONEY

1880
01:18:51,060 --> 01:18:53,530
- IN THE BANK BY NOW.
- JUST WHAT ARE YOU GONNA
DO ABOUT IT?

1881
01:18:53,563 --> 01:18:55,898
WAIT A MINUTE. I HAVE NO IDEA
WHAT YOU'RE TALKING ABOUT.

1882
01:18:55,932 --> 01:18:58,835
- I REALLY HAVEN'T.
- DON'T LIE TO US!

1883
01:18:58,868 --> 01:19:02,572
YOU KNEW. TOKI WENT ALONG
TO THE ROAD CORPORATION
HEADQUARTERS.

1884
01:19:02,605 --> 01:19:04,440
THEY'RE CHANGING
THE COURSE OF THE ROAD.

1885
01:19:04,473 --> 01:19:05,842
I JUST DON'T BELIEVE
A WORD OF IT!

1886
01:19:05,875 --> 01:19:07,610
- IT'S NONSENSE, THAT'S WHAT!
- NONSENSE!

1887
01:19:07,643 --> 01:19:09,847
THEY'RE JUST SAYING THAT
TO FRIGHTEN YOU.

1888
01:19:09,880 --> 01:19:11,848
WE'VE LISTENED
LONG ENOUGH TO YOU.

1889
01:19:11,882 --> 01:19:14,017
IT WAS YOUR ADVICE
THAT GOT US INTO THIS.

1890
01:19:14,050 --> 01:19:15,418
IT'S YOUR FAULT!

1891
01:19:15,452 --> 01:19:17,453
IT'S ALL YOUR FAULT!
YOU'D BETTER THINK ABOUT--

1892
01:19:17,487 --> 01:19:20,223
UH, YOU'D BLAME ME
FOR THE TOPSOIL TOO.

1893
01:19:20,257 --> 01:19:21,525
--UNREASONABLE ABOUT THIS--

1894
01:19:21,558 --> 01:19:23,493
- HELP US!
- YOU GOT THE MONEY FOR US.

1895
01:19:23,527 --> 01:19:24,995
WE WANT WHAT'S REASONABLE!

1896
01:19:25,028 --> 01:19:27,397
MY HORSES. MY COWS. MY MEN.

1897
01:19:27,430 --> 01:19:29,198
EVERYTHING I LOVE.

1898
01:19:29,232 --> 01:19:31,433
I'VE GOT NOTHING LEFT.
SO WHAT NOW?

1899
01:19:31,468 --> 01:19:33,803
GO AWAY! GO AWAY!
GO AWAY! GO AWAY! GO AWAY!

1900
01:19:33,837 --> 01:19:36,238
EIICHI! STOP!

1901
01:19:36,272 --> 01:19:38,975
THEY'RE JUST A ROTTEN BUNCH
OF SILLY STUPID--

1902
01:19:39,008 --> 01:19:41,978
QUICK! GET A PENCIL
UNDER HIS TONGUE.

1903
01:19:42,012 --> 01:19:44,247
PLEASE, COME ON NOW.
IT'S ALL RIGHT NOW.

1904
01:19:44,280 --> 01:19:47,317
COME INSIDE, HONEY. LET'S
GET YOU SOME PANCAKE BATTER.

1905
01:19:47,350 --> 01:19:48,785
[EIICHI SOBS]

1906
01:19:48,818 --> 01:19:50,687
[SERVO SOBS]

1907
01:19:50,720 --> 01:19:53,390
HE'S VERY HIGH-STRUNG.

1908
01:19:53,423 --> 01:19:55,958
- [CROW CLEARS THROAT]
- [SERVO WHISTLES]

1909
01:19:55,992 --> 01:19:59,395
YEP.

1910
01:19:59,428 --> 01:20:01,130
I KNOW WHAT
YOU'RE ALL FEELING.

1911
01:20:01,163 --> 01:20:03,633
I'M VERY SORRY.

1912
01:20:03,667 --> 01:20:06,035
BUT DON'T BLAME
MY GRANDFATHER.

1913
01:20:06,068 --> 01:20:08,205
HE ONLY DID WHAT HE THOUGHT
WAS THE BEST THING.

1914
01:20:08,238 --> 01:20:11,007
HE HAD TO INVEST IN...

1915
01:20:11,040 --> 01:20:13,543
SO PLEASE.
TRY TO FORGIVE HIM.

1916
01:20:13,577 --> 01:20:14,945
- OKAY.
- HE WOULDN'T HAVE

1917
01:20:14,978 --> 01:20:17,013
HAD THIS HAPPEN
FOR THE WORLD.

1918
01:20:17,047 --> 01:20:19,382
AND YOU KNEW THAT.

1919
01:20:19,415 --> 01:20:21,518
- BUT WHAT ABOUT THE LAND?
- ENOUGH.

1920
01:20:21,552 --> 01:20:23,220
COME ON, LET'S GO.

1921
01:20:23,253 --> 01:20:24,687
IXNAY ON THE AND-LAY.

1922
01:20:24,720 --> 01:20:27,023
LET'S GO.

1923
01:20:27,057 --> 01:20:30,660
[SERVO GRUMBLES]

1924
01:20:30,693 --> 01:20:34,230
SUMIKO.

1925
01:20:34,263 --> 01:20:36,833
SHAME.

1926
01:20:36,867 --> 01:20:38,502
SHAME.

1927
01:20:38,535 --> 01:20:40,203
HE THREW THESE MODELS

1928
01:20:40,237 --> 01:20:43,072
THAT WERE IN THE LAST SCENE.

1929
01:20:43,105 --> 01:20:45,075
OH, THERE GOES HIS
HIP SOCKET.

1930
01:20:45,108 --> 01:20:47,443
- UH-OH.
- OUCH.

1931
01:20:51,915 --> 01:20:54,183
AND THEN WE APPROACHED
FROM THE REAR,

1932
01:20:54,217 --> 01:20:56,787
USING THE SAME STRATEGY
WE DID IN NORMANDY.

1933
01:20:56,820 --> 01:20:59,522
NOW DO I TELL HIM
HE'S NOT MINE?

1934
01:20:59,555 --> 01:21:01,958
OH. GAMERA.

1935
01:21:01,992 --> 01:21:03,360
MM.

1936
01:21:03,393 --> 01:21:07,197
GAMERA WOULDN'T HAVE ANY TROUBLE
GETTING RID OF GAOS.

1937
01:21:07,230 --> 01:21:09,832
HE'D JUST BREATHE FIRE ON HIM
AND BURN HIM RIGHT UP.

1938
01:21:09,865 --> 01:21:12,435
- UH-HUH.
- AND AFTERWARDS,
HE COULD COME HERE.

1939
01:21:12,468 --> 01:21:15,305
AND BURN UP ALL THOSE MEN
WHO WERE MEAN TO GRANDDAD.

1940
01:21:15,338 --> 01:21:17,773
UH, YOU'RE GETTING INTO
A WEIRD AREA HERE, EIICHI.

1941
01:21:17,807 --> 01:21:20,443
--BUT STILL, THERE'S NO WAY
OF GETTING IN TOUCH WITH GAMERA.

1942
01:21:20,477 --> 01:21:21,912
YOU ONLY
HAVE TO START A FIRE.

1943
01:21:21,945 --> 01:21:24,480
- START A FIRE?
- MM.

1944
01:21:24,513 --> 01:21:26,282
GAOS JUST CAN'T STAND FIRES,

1945
01:21:26,315 --> 01:21:28,252
AND GAMERA LIKES THEM
MORE THAN ANYTHING.

1946
01:21:28,285 --> 01:21:29,618
HE'D SOON COME.

1947
01:21:29,652 --> 01:21:32,355
- NEAT.
- YOU SEE, GAOS WOULD
SOON GET WEAK.

1948
01:21:32,388 --> 01:21:33,757
GAMERA WOULDN'T HAVE
VERY MUCH TROUBLE

1949
01:21:33,790 --> 01:21:36,760
- BEATING HIM THEN.
- HMM. SOUND. GOOD LOGIC.

1950
01:21:36,793 --> 01:21:39,428
BUT WHEREABOUTS
COULD WE START THE FIRE, HUH?

1951
01:21:39,462 --> 01:21:41,097
OH, THAT WOULDN'T
BE ANY TROUBLE.

1952
01:21:41,130 --> 01:21:43,098
WE JUST SET FIRE
TO THE MOUNTAIN.

1953
01:21:43,132 --> 01:21:46,068
I LIKE IT.
THIS KID'S NOT HALF-BAD.

1954
01:21:47,637 --> 01:21:51,440
THIS IS A GREAT DRAWING!
THIS KID DRAWS REALLY WELL.

1955
01:21:51,473 --> 01:21:53,108
--BUT STILL,
REMEMBER THE LAST TIME.

1956
01:21:53,142 --> 01:21:54,577
HE COULD PROBABLY
BEAT OFF THOSE FLAMES

1957
01:21:54,610 --> 01:21:56,145
WITH THOSE BIG WINGS.

1958
01:21:56,178 --> 01:21:57,980
ALL RIGHT, SO WHAT IF
HE DID MANAGE TO BLOW OUT

1959
01:21:58,013 --> 01:21:59,415
THE FIRST FEW FIRES, THEN?

1960
01:21:59,448 --> 01:22:00,683
WE'D JUST KEEP
LIGHTING NEW ONES.

1961
01:22:00,717 --> 01:22:02,785
ALWAYS LOOKING ON
THE BRIGHT SIDE, OLD MAN.

1962
01:22:02,818 --> 01:22:05,088
--YOU BURN DOWN
WOULD BE ENORMOUS.

1963
01:22:05,122 --> 01:22:06,890
IT WOULD COST YOU
MILLIONS OF YEN.

1964
01:22:06,923 --> 01:22:09,158
- YES, I KNOW ALL THAT.
- I DON'T HAVE ANY YEN.

1965
01:22:09,192 --> 01:22:10,693
--THINK THAT THE GODS
SENT GAOS TO PUNISH

1966
01:22:10,727 --> 01:22:12,862
ALL THE FARMERS
FOR BEING QUITE SO GREEDY.

1967
01:22:12,895 --> 01:22:16,700
SO THIS IS OUR PUNISHMENT,
AND WE GET RID OF GAOS
AT THE SAME TIME.

1968
01:22:16,733 --> 01:22:19,002
PERHAPS THE GODS WILL AGREE
TO FORGIVE US THEN.

1969
01:22:19,035 --> 01:22:20,537
ANYWAY, IF YOU THINK
IT MAY WELL PLEASE,

1970
01:22:20,570 --> 01:22:22,738
GO AHEAD AND SET FIRE
TO THE WHOLE OF THE MOUNTAIN.

1971
01:22:22,772 --> 01:22:24,707
THANK YOU, SIR.
I'M GRATEFUL.

1972
01:22:24,740 --> 01:22:27,743
- NO, NO, NO, NO.
- [ALL] NO, NO, NO, NO, NO.

1973
01:22:27,777 --> 01:22:29,245
...THE IDEA.

1974
01:22:29,278 --> 01:22:32,348
HE BELIEVES THAT ONCE WE GET
A BIG HILL FIRE STARTED,

1975
01:22:32,382 --> 01:22:34,917
GAMERA WILL ARRIVE ON THE SCENE
AND FINISH OFF GAOS.

1976
01:22:34,950 --> 01:22:37,287
NOW I'M READY FOR
THAT PIECE OF CAKE.

1977
01:22:37,320 --> 01:22:39,122
ALL RIGHT THEN.
NOW THIS MAY WELL BE

1978
01:22:39,155 --> 01:22:41,057
THE LAST CHANCE
WE'RE GONNA HAVE.

1979
01:22:41,090 --> 01:22:42,458
- SO WHATEVER--
- HMM. WHAT FLAVOR?

1980
01:22:42,492 --> 01:22:45,295
- THIS IDEA HAS GOT TO WORK.
- EVERGREEN?

1981
01:22:45,328 --> 01:22:46,963
MY MEN CAN HELP YOU
WITH THIS.

1982
01:22:46,997 --> 01:22:49,932
THEY KNOW THAT COUNTRYSIDE.

1983
01:22:49,965 --> 01:22:53,068
THE LOGGING INDUSTRY!
OVER THREE BILLION DOWN!

1984
01:22:53,102 --> 01:22:56,005
WE WORK FOR YOU
WHILE WE WORK AGAINST YOU!

1985
01:22:56,038 --> 01:22:57,507
FEEDING YOU PICKS
AND DOUBLE-TALK.

1986
01:22:57,540 --> 01:22:59,842
STEALING YOUR DREAMS
AND SELLING THEM BACK TO YOU!

1987
01:22:59,875 --> 01:23:02,278
WHY, THIS TREE HERE
COULD HOLD A SHAMROCK SHAKE,

1988
01:23:02,312 --> 01:23:04,013
OR ONE OF THOSE
BENDY CARDBOARD THINGS

1989
01:23:04,047 --> 01:23:05,748
IN THE BOTTOM
OF A HOSTESS CUPCAKE.

1990
01:23:05,782 --> 01:23:07,117
ALL RIGHT, FORWARD.

1991
01:23:14,457 --> 01:23:16,960
EW. [SERVO COUGHS]

1992
01:23:21,932 --> 01:23:24,033
THIS IS NEAT.

1993
01:23:31,942 --> 01:23:35,145
COME ON! BRING IT ON!
WHAT ELSE YOU GOT?

1994
01:23:35,178 --> 01:23:38,382
HE'S JUST BLOWING OUT
THE FLAMES. AMAZING!

1995
01:23:38,415 --> 01:23:40,250
QUICK! CONTINUE THE ATTACK.

1996
01:23:40,283 --> 01:23:42,018
RIGHT!

1997
01:23:46,088 --> 01:23:48,725
OOH! GOOD THING
HE HAS HIS CUP ON.

1998
01:23:48,758 --> 01:23:51,260
HEY...

1999
01:23:51,293 --> 01:23:54,830
[GAOS SCREAMS]

2000
01:23:54,863 --> 01:23:57,133
HMM.

2001
01:24:02,205 --> 01:24:04,307
I THINK I HEAR
THE PITTER-PATTER OF GAMERA.

2002
01:24:04,340 --> 01:24:06,408
AH! GAMERA.

2003
01:24:06,442 --> 01:24:08,277
I'LL HAVE MY CANDY NOW.

2004
01:24:11,280 --> 01:24:13,717
TOLD YOU HE'D COME,
DIDN'T I?

2005
01:24:13,750 --> 01:24:16,518
YEAH, GREAT. WHY DON'T YOU
GO OUT AND SAY HI?

2006
01:24:19,888 --> 01:24:22,492
♪♪ [SERVO HUMS WITH SCORE]

2007
01:24:22,525 --> 01:24:26,262
SOUNDS LIKE QUO VADIS,
NOT GAMERA.

2008
01:24:26,295 --> 01:24:30,032
YOU KNOW, I'M INTRIGUED
BY THIS PLUCKY GAMERA.

2009
01:24:30,065 --> 01:24:33,503
[JOEL CHUCKLES]

2010
01:24:33,537 --> 01:24:35,638
♪♪ [SERVO HUMS WITH SCORE]

2011
01:24:42,345 --> 01:24:44,780
A-HA, SO HE FINALLY
LEARNED HOW TO DUCK.

2012
01:24:44,813 --> 01:24:47,783
I GUESS HE REMEMBERED
HE HAD A SHELL.

2013
01:24:47,817 --> 01:24:50,085
[BOTS]
OH.

2014
01:24:51,520 --> 01:24:54,257
THAT CHEESES HIM OFF.

2015
01:24:57,293 --> 01:24:59,328
GO RIGHT BEHIND HIM,
OR HE'LL BURN YOU TO PIECES

2016
01:24:59,362 --> 01:25:01,230
WITH THE RAYS, GAMERA.

2017
01:25:01,263 --> 01:25:03,733
OH YEAH. THANKS, EIICHI.
I FORGOT.

2018
01:25:11,707 --> 01:25:14,043
HMM.

2019
01:25:21,750 --> 01:25:23,487
NO FAIR.

2020
01:25:27,890 --> 01:25:29,625
BOY, YOU KNOW, I BET
THEY CAN NEVER GET

2021
01:25:29,658 --> 01:25:31,928
THOSE PIT STAINS
OUT OF HIS SHIRT.

2022
01:25:34,997 --> 01:25:36,432
WHUH-OH. BLINDSIDED.

2023
01:25:36,465 --> 01:25:39,935
OH, CROSS-CHECK.
HE'LL BE IN THE BOX FOR TWO.

2024
01:25:44,007 --> 01:25:46,075
[CROW GROWLS]

2025
01:25:49,312 --> 01:25:52,282
HE'S DOWN.

2026
01:25:52,315 --> 01:25:55,852
- WELL, HEY.
- WAIT-- THIS IS NEW.

2027
01:25:55,885 --> 01:25:57,653
OH, THE FLYING
HEAD SCISSORS,

2028
01:25:57,687 --> 01:26:00,122
- AND A FIGURE FOUR!
- WHOO!

2029
01:26:00,155 --> 01:26:03,425
- VERY IMPRESSIVE.
- MM-HMM.

2030
01:26:03,458 --> 01:26:04,827
UH-OH. NOT AGAIN.

2031
01:26:04,860 --> 01:26:06,428
YOU KNOW,
IF YOU BITE MY LEG OFF,

2032
01:26:06,462 --> 01:26:09,065
IT'LL JUST GROW BACK.
SO DON'T EVEN BOTHER.

2033
01:26:13,268 --> 01:26:15,205
LOOK. HE'S GETTING AWAY.

2034
01:26:15,238 --> 01:26:17,240
[ALL]
AAH, SHUT UP.

2035
01:26:20,643 --> 01:26:23,212
HMM. YOU KNOW,
YOU'D BE GOOD WITH CURRY.

2036
01:26:23,245 --> 01:26:24,747
[SERVO MUMBLES]

2037
01:26:24,780 --> 01:26:26,648
A LITTLE TOUGH.

2038
01:26:26,682 --> 01:26:28,652
UH...

2039
01:26:30,085 --> 01:26:32,288
- [SERVO SPITS]
- YOU GOT A LITTLE...

2040
01:26:32,322 --> 01:26:34,057
- SOMETHING THERE.
- JUST GOTTA-- [SPITS]

2041
01:26:34,090 --> 01:26:35,892
THERE.

2042
01:26:39,262 --> 01:26:41,630
HAH! HAH!

2043
01:26:41,663 --> 01:26:44,300
I MAY BE A TURTLE,
BUT I'M FAST!

2044
01:26:46,202 --> 01:26:47,903
♪ DANCE, DANCE ♪

2045
01:26:47,937 --> 01:26:51,908
♪ DO THE MONSTER MASH ♪

2046
01:26:51,942 --> 01:26:54,143
- HUH?
- HAH!

2047
01:26:54,177 --> 01:26:55,978
HAH! CAN'T TOUCH ME.

2048
01:26:56,012 --> 01:26:57,447
HMM.

2049
01:26:57,480 --> 01:26:59,848
YOU'VE GOT HIM NOW, GAMERA.

2050
01:26:59,882 --> 01:27:03,452
UH-OH, YOU BLEW A HOSE.
OH, BUMMER.

2051
01:27:15,965 --> 01:27:18,433
♪♪ [SERVO HUMS WITH SCORE]

2052
01:27:22,038 --> 01:27:23,707
- HUH?
- DID WE MISS SOMETHING?

2053
01:27:23,740 --> 01:27:25,842
OH.

2054
01:27:30,145 --> 01:27:33,082
HERE'S THAT MRS. SMITH'S PIE
YOU ORDERED.

2055
01:27:34,983 --> 01:27:36,452
- WHOO.
- OH BOY, HE CAN IMPACT.

2056
01:27:36,485 --> 01:27:38,988
GAMERA!

2057
01:27:39,022 --> 01:27:41,690
OH, AND AGAIN.

2058
01:27:41,723 --> 01:27:42,958
NOT FAIR.

2059
01:27:42,992 --> 01:27:45,060
HEY, ISN'T THIS
HOW AESCHYLUS DIED?

2060
01:27:45,093 --> 01:27:47,897
- HUH?
- YEAH. PELICAN DROPPED
A TURTLE ON HIS HEAD.

2061
01:27:47,963 --> 01:27:50,500
- OH.
- IT'S TRUE, LOOK IT UP.

2062
01:27:56,572 --> 01:27:58,875
AND AGAIN.

2063
01:28:01,277 --> 01:28:02,678
HERE'S A LITTLE GAMERA
FOR YA!

2064
01:28:02,678 --> 01:28:04,280
WHOO!

2065
01:28:08,083 --> 01:28:11,988
OH, HE'S LINED UP WELL.

2066
01:28:11,988 --> 01:28:13,622
OH, HE HIT THE SLOT.
HE'S IN THE GROOVE--

2067
01:28:13,690 --> 01:28:16,325
OH! PERFECT GAME!
HE BOWLED A STRIKE.

2068
01:28:19,095 --> 01:28:21,097
- OW. OWEE.
- OH...

2069
01:28:21,130 --> 01:28:24,000
YUCK.

2070
01:28:24,000 --> 01:28:25,300
HEY, HE'S SUPPOSED
TO BE THE HERO,

2071
01:28:25,335 --> 01:28:27,203
AND HE'S GETTING THE SNOT
KICKED OUT OF HIM.

2072
01:28:27,203 --> 01:28:29,405
[BOTS]
LITERALLY.

2073
01:28:29,405 --> 01:28:31,340
IF I COULD ONLY

2074
01:28:31,407 --> 01:28:33,608
REACH THE ROCK...

2075
01:28:33,608 --> 01:28:36,812
AAH.

2076
01:28:36,845 --> 01:28:39,615
- OH BROTHER.
- WOW.

2077
01:28:39,648 --> 01:28:41,650
COME ON.

2078
01:28:46,055 --> 01:28:49,658
[JOEL MUMBLES]

2079
01:28:53,662 --> 01:28:56,498
OOPS. NOW WHAT?

2080
01:28:56,532 --> 01:28:58,000
I DON'T KNOW,
BUT I'VE LOST THE PLOT.

2081
01:28:58,033 --> 01:28:59,935
MM-HMM. ME TOO.

2082
01:28:59,968 --> 01:29:00,970
SOMETHING MUST'VE HAPPENED.

2083
01:29:01,003 --> 01:29:02,705
I DON'T KNOW.

2084
01:29:02,738 --> 01:29:05,642
OH, YOU'RE A FAT OLD HOG,
AIN'T YOU?

2085
01:29:05,675 --> 01:29:09,512
[SERVO SQUEALS]

2086
01:29:09,545 --> 01:29:11,047
SORRY.

2087
01:29:14,517 --> 01:29:17,453
UH-OH-- OH, YUCK!

2088
01:29:17,487 --> 01:29:19,588
OH, HE'S SPURTING
DISHWASHING LIQUID.

2089
01:29:19,622 --> 01:29:21,257
IT'S PEPTO-BISMOL.

2090
01:29:21,290 --> 01:29:24,893
HE'S GOT A CREAMY FILLING.

2091
01:29:24,927 --> 01:29:26,628
OH, IT'S EVERYWHERE.

2092
01:29:26,662 --> 01:29:27,963
I CAN'T WATCH THIS.

2093
01:29:27,997 --> 01:29:30,433
I'VE GROWN TO KNOW THAT
CHARACTER SO WELL.

2094
01:29:30,467 --> 01:29:32,135
YEAH.

2095
01:29:32,168 --> 01:29:34,403
JUST LIKE WHEN GARY DIED.

2096
01:29:36,805 --> 01:29:39,342
BE CAREFUL THERE, GAMERA!

2097
01:29:39,375 --> 01:29:41,643
HEY, NO COACHING FROM
THE SIDELINES, SHRIMP.

2098
01:29:43,980 --> 01:29:45,213
NICE DAY FOR IT.

2099
01:29:45,247 --> 01:29:48,550
RED SKY MORNING,
MONSTERS TAKE WARNING.

2100
01:29:48,583 --> 01:29:50,085
HEY, LOOKS LIKE GORBACHEV.

2101
01:29:50,118 --> 01:29:53,790
YEAH, AND HE'S
FIGHTING YELTSIN.

2102
01:29:53,823 --> 01:29:55,123
HEAD'S TURNING RED!

2103
01:29:55,157 --> 01:29:58,493
- YOU'VE WON, GAMERA!
- OH, SHUT UP.

2104
01:29:58,527 --> 01:30:00,663
OH LOOK,
NOW HE'S A RAKU KILN.

2105
01:30:00,697 --> 01:30:04,367
OOH. COOL.

2106
01:30:04,400 --> 01:30:06,868
WHAT, SUDDENLY GAMERA
HAS A LUGGAGE RACK?

2107
01:30:06,902 --> 01:30:08,237
I GUESS SO.

2108
01:30:08,270 --> 01:30:11,140
OH, HE'S GOTTA RETURN
FOR DEPOSIT AND RECYCLE.

2109
01:30:11,173 --> 01:30:13,877
OH, THAT'S REALLY SWEET.

2110
01:30:17,012 --> 01:30:19,482
♪♪ [SERVO HUMS WITH SCORE]

2111
01:30:22,352 --> 01:30:24,220
IT'S THE FLYING DUTCHMAN.

2112
01:30:24,253 --> 01:30:26,055
HMM.

2113
01:30:30,927 --> 01:30:34,397
COME ON, COME ON.

2114
01:30:34,430 --> 01:30:36,565
NO! DON'T YOU DO IT!

2115
01:30:36,598 --> 01:30:37,900
DON'T YOU DO IT!

2116
01:30:37,933 --> 01:30:40,537
I GOT NOWHERE ELSE TO GO!

2117
01:30:44,073 --> 01:30:46,642
NO-- NO, PLEASE DON'T,
NOT INTO THE VOLCANO!

2118
01:30:46,675 --> 01:30:50,112
PLEASE, NO! EIICHI, NO!

2119
01:30:52,282 --> 01:30:53,448
HMM.

2120
01:30:53,482 --> 01:30:54,717
AND THAT'S THE END OF GAOS.

2121
01:30:54,750 --> 01:30:57,487
GOOD NIGHT,
AND MAY GOD BLESS.

2122
01:30:59,855 --> 01:31:02,158
YES. THAT'S THE END OF HIM,
ALL RIGHT.

2123
01:31:02,192 --> 01:31:04,893
NOW IT'S OVER, YOU CAN START
WITH THE ROAD AGAIN, CAN'T YOU?

2124
01:31:04,927 --> 01:31:06,495
YES. WE'LL START WORK
TOMORROW.

2125
01:31:06,528 --> 01:31:07,963
- HEY, YOU QUIT.
- HEY, BOSS!

2126
01:31:07,997 --> 01:31:09,798
HEY, BOSS! IT'S YOU.

2127
01:31:09,832 --> 01:31:11,567
TELL EVERYONE TO START WORKING
ON THE ROAD TOMORROW.

2128
01:31:11,600 --> 01:31:13,135
THEY'RE ON A NEW COURSE.

2129
01:31:13,168 --> 01:31:15,638
OH, THAT WAS A RUMOR,
LIKE I TOLD YOU.

2130
01:31:15,672 --> 01:31:19,508
- [ALL LAUGH]
- VERY GULLIBLE.

2131
01:31:19,542 --> 01:31:21,243
GOOD NEWS, BOSS.

2132
01:31:21,277 --> 01:31:22,978
THANK YOU VERY MUCH,
FOR EVERYTHING.

2133
01:31:23,012 --> 01:31:25,280
- YOU'RE WELCOME.
- NO, EIICHI'S THE ONE TO THANK.

2134
01:31:25,313 --> 01:31:26,782
[JOEL GASPS]

2135
01:31:26,815 --> 01:31:28,183
DONUTS, PEANUTS, COMBO CORN,

2136
01:31:28,217 --> 01:31:30,252
WALL OF KEYBOARDS, A THOUSAND
DOLLARS' WORTH OF CDs,

2137
01:31:30,285 --> 01:31:32,522
CRACKLING PORK BREAD.

2138
01:31:33,788 --> 01:31:35,157
HEY.

2139
01:31:35,190 --> 01:31:37,493
COME BACK AGAIN SOON
AND SEE US, GAMERA.

2140
01:31:37,527 --> 01:31:38,995
DON'T FORGET, NOW.

2141
01:31:39,028 --> 01:31:41,930
BRUSH!

2142
01:31:41,963 --> 01:31:44,000
EIICHI!

2143
01:31:46,268 --> 01:31:50,205
- BYE.
- OH.

2144
01:31:50,238 --> 01:31:52,908
- WELL, THAT WAS FUN.
- THAT WAS NEAT--

2145
01:31:52,942 --> 01:31:56,145
HERE ARE SCENES
FROM NEXT WEEK'S GAMERA.

2146
01:31:56,178 --> 01:31:58,847
OH, WHAT'S THIS?

2147
01:31:58,882 --> 01:32:00,783
WELL, KIDS, IF YOU ENJOYED
TODAY'S MOVIE,

2148
01:32:00,817 --> 01:32:03,452
YOU'RE SURE TO LIKE
THIS SHAMELESS PADDING.

2149
01:32:03,485 --> 01:32:05,020
EH, IT'S JUST LIKE
A BURT REYNOLDS FILM.

2150
01:32:05,053 --> 01:32:07,923
- THESE ARE THE OUTTAKES.
- OH...

2151
01:32:11,627 --> 01:32:13,462
NOW WE CAN SPIN HIM.

2152
01:32:13,495 --> 01:32:16,465
HEY...

2153
01:32:16,498 --> 01:32:19,702
OH, THIS IS WHERE
DOM DeLUISE BLOWS A LINE.

2154
01:32:19,735 --> 01:32:22,037
IT KILLS ME EVERY TIME.

2155
01:32:22,070 --> 01:32:24,607
- REMEMBER THAT?
- OH YEAH, THAT WAS
A BLAST, MAN.

2156
01:32:24,640 --> 01:32:26,475
REALLY IS.
JUST A TON OF FUN.

2157
01:32:26,508 --> 01:32:29,912
- OH.
- [BOTS LAUGH]

2158
01:32:29,945 --> 01:32:32,482
- OH YEAH.
- THAT WAS GREAT.

2159
01:32:32,515 --> 01:32:34,150
THIS IS EVEN BETTER
THE SECOND TIME AROUND.

2160
01:32:34,183 --> 01:32:35,585
IT'S LIKE LASAGNA.

2161
01:32:35,618 --> 01:32:37,052
NOW, A LOT OF PEOPLE
WROTE IN AND SAID

2162
01:32:37,085 --> 01:32:38,453
THEY'D LIKE TO SEE
MONSTERS FIGHT.

2163
01:32:38,487 --> 01:32:39,922
- WELL, HERE YOU GO.
- YEP.

2164
01:32:39,955 --> 01:32:41,990
ALL YOU WANT.

2165
01:32:42,023 --> 01:32:43,692
- MORE THAN YOU WANT.
- YEP, YEP YEP.

2166
01:32:43,725 --> 01:32:46,128
SAW THAT TOO.

2167
01:32:46,162 --> 01:32:48,830
YOU KNOW, I'M BEGINNING TO THINK
THIS IS KIND OF CHEAP.

2168
01:32:48,863 --> 01:32:50,767
NAH.

2169
01:32:50,800 --> 01:32:52,968
OH, I REMEMBER THIS.
THIS IS WH--

2170
01:32:53,002 --> 01:32:55,237
WAIT A MINUTE.

2171
01:32:55,270 --> 01:32:57,105
- NOW THAT--
- WHAT'S GOING ON?

2172
01:32:57,138 --> 01:32:58,440
THAT'S BARUGON.

2173
01:32:58,473 --> 01:33:00,375
IT'S A GAMERA FAMILY ALBUM.

2174
01:33:00,408 --> 01:33:02,177
YEAH-- HUH?

2175
01:33:06,348 --> 01:33:08,250
AND HERE'S AGNES MOOREHEAD.

2176
01:33:08,283 --> 01:33:10,385
LOOKING FINE, AGGY.

2177
01:33:13,322 --> 01:33:14,957
WAIT,
THEY REVERSED THE FILM.

2178
01:33:14,990 --> 01:33:16,525
REMEMBER WHAT
WE SAID ABOUT THAT?

2179
01:33:16,558 --> 01:33:20,028
- NEW COMBINATION.
- YEAH, THAT WAS FUNNY,
WASN'T IT?

2180
01:33:20,062 --> 01:33:21,963
AAH.

2181
01:33:21,997 --> 01:33:23,432
HEY, THERE'S A TICK ON GAM--

2182
01:33:23,465 --> 01:33:27,035
- OH, IT'S EIICHI.
- YEP, YEP.

2183
01:33:27,068 --> 01:33:30,840
AND DIDN'T ALL OUR EYES GET
MOIST AT THIS POIGNANT MOMENT?

2184
01:33:32,040 --> 01:33:34,610
REMEMBER WHERE WE WERE
WHEN WE SAW THAT?

2185
01:33:34,643 --> 01:33:37,513
[SERVO YAWNS]

2186
01:33:37,547 --> 01:33:39,748
OH, SORRY.

2187
01:33:39,782 --> 01:33:41,350
- [ALL CHEER]
- FINALLY.

2188
01:33:41,383 --> 01:33:43,218
ACT NOW TO GET
GAMERA'S FUNNIEST MOMENTS

2189
01:33:43,252 --> 01:33:45,520
AND SEE HIM ON
ALAN KING: INSIDE
THE MONSTER MIND.

2190
01:34:01,703 --> 01:34:03,305
OH BOY, OH MAN, JOEL.

2191
01:34:03,338 --> 01:34:04,773
THAT WAS ABOUT
THE LAMEST ATTEMPT

2192
01:34:04,807 --> 01:34:07,142
TO GET RID OF A MONSTER
I HAVE EVER SEEN.

2193
01:34:07,175 --> 01:34:10,245
YEAH, COME ON. A FOUNTAIN
OF BLOOD AND A TURNTABLE?

2194
01:34:10,278 --> 01:34:11,613
SHEESH.

2195
01:34:11,647 --> 01:34:13,382
WELL, YOU KNOW WHAT?
YOU GUYS SHOULD SNAP ON

2196
01:34:13,415 --> 01:34:14,850
THE RIGHT SIDE
OF YOUR BRAINS.

2197
01:34:14,883 --> 01:34:17,420
COME UP WITH SOME IDEAS
FOR HOW TO OFF GAOS.

2198
01:34:17,453 --> 01:34:19,155
- THAT'D BE PRETTY FUN.
- OH, OH, OH, OH, OH.

2199
01:34:19,188 --> 01:34:21,457
I GOT A GOOD ONE. YOU COULD
WAIT TILL HE GOES TO THE BANK,

2200
01:34:21,490 --> 01:34:23,958
AND THEN WRITE "I HAVE A GUN.
GIVE ME ALL YOUR MONEY."

2201
01:34:23,992 --> 01:34:25,627
ON HIS DEPOSIT SLIP.

2202
01:34:25,660 --> 01:34:27,830
YEAH, OR, I KNOW, OKAY?

2203
01:34:27,863 --> 01:34:30,465
YOU ASK HIM TO COME OVER,
MAYBE FOR, I DON'T KNOW,

2204
01:34:30,498 --> 01:34:32,568
TEA OR SOMETHING. THEN YOU
GO INTO THE REFRIGERATOR

2205
01:34:32,602 --> 01:34:34,303
AND GET OUT AN ICICLE,
AND YOU OFF HIM!

2206
01:34:34,337 --> 01:34:35,705
YOU STAB HIM,
AND THE EVIDENCE MELTS.

2207
01:34:35,738 --> 01:34:37,440
COOL. COOL.
OH, I GOT A GREAT ONE--

2208
01:34:37,473 --> 01:34:39,175
- HOW ABOUT--
- OH, I KNOW, I KNOW, I KNOW.
I KNOW, I KNOW.

2209
01:34:39,208 --> 01:34:41,543
UH, YOU COULD, UM,

2210
01:34:41,577 --> 01:34:43,978
CHOP HIS HEAD OFF.

2211
01:34:44,012 --> 01:34:45,480
UH-HUH.

2212
01:34:45,513 --> 01:34:47,583
WELL, WHERE WERE WE?
OH OH OH, HERE WE GO.

2213
01:34:47,617 --> 01:34:49,052
YOU COULD GIVE HIM
A CUP OF GASOLINE.

2214
01:34:49,085 --> 01:34:50,953
- TELL HIM IT'S CIDER,
OF COURSE.
- YES.

2215
01:34:50,987 --> 01:34:52,688
THEN YOU MAKE HIM
EAT A WINTERGREEN LIFESAVER.

2216
01:34:52,722 --> 01:34:54,390
'CAUSE EVERYBODY KNOWS
WHEN YOU BITE 'EM, THEY SPARK.

2217
01:34:54,423 --> 01:34:55,992
THEN THE SPARK WILL
SET OFF THE GASOLINE,

2218
01:34:56,025 --> 01:34:58,260
- AND HE'LL BLOW UP. BOOM!
- EXCELLENT. OKAY.

2219
01:34:58,293 --> 01:35:00,128
I GOT AN IDEA.
YOU INVITE GAOS

2220
01:35:00,162 --> 01:35:02,097
TO VACATION WITH YOU
IN THE BAHAMAS.

2221
01:35:02,130 --> 01:35:04,867
AND AFTER A LEISURELY LUNCH,

2222
01:35:04,900 --> 01:35:07,803
YOU INVITED HIM TO COME OUT
DEEP-SEA FISHING.

2223
01:35:07,837 --> 01:35:10,238
AND IT'S YOUR TREAT,
BECAUSE THAT SCUBA GEAR

2224
01:35:10,272 --> 01:35:13,542
IS EXPENSIVE,
AND THEN YOU CUT HIS HOSE.

2225
01:35:13,575 --> 01:35:15,243
YEAH! PRETEND HIS HEAD
IS A RAILROAD SPIKE,

2226
01:35:15,277 --> 01:35:16,812
AND DRIVE IT
INTO THE GROUND.

2227
01:35:16,845 --> 01:35:20,548
MEH! BAM! WITH A BIG HAMMER.

2228
01:35:20,582 --> 01:35:22,083
YEAH. WHERE WERE WE?

2229
01:35:22,117 --> 01:35:23,785
OH. OKAY, OKAY.
YOU COULD GET HIM A JOB

2230
01:35:23,818 --> 01:35:25,253
IN A LIQUOR STORE
IN A BAD PART OF TOWN--

2231
01:35:25,287 --> 01:35:27,255
HEY. YOU GOT A BETTER IDEA?

2232
01:35:27,288 --> 01:35:30,860
IF YOU THINK SO, SEND IT TO
"WAYS TO SNUFF GAOS"

2233
01:35:30,893 --> 01:35:33,228
CARE OF...

2234
01:35:40,002 --> 01:35:41,470
OH, AND THEN YOU COULD
BEAT HIM TO DEATH

2235
01:35:41,503 --> 01:35:43,538
WITH A PORK CHOP
AND FEED IT TO THE POLICE.

2236
01:35:43,572 --> 01:35:45,307
- THAT'S PRETTY GOOD.
- YEAH!
- THAT'S NOT HALF-BAD!

2237
01:35:45,340 --> 01:35:47,943
WE'VE GIVEN IT BACK TO YOU.
WHAT DO YOU THINK, SIRS?

2238
01:35:47,977 --> 01:35:50,880
WELL, I THINK YOU COULD TAKE
A PAIR OF NEEDLE-NOSE PLIERS

2239
01:35:50,913 --> 01:35:54,283
AND JAM 'EM UP INTO HIS NOSE
AND TWIST HIS SEPTUM INTO...

2240
01:35:55,417 --> 01:35:58,187
UH, WELL, UNTIL NEXT TIME,
JOEL-ERA.

2241
01:35:58,220 --> 01:35:59,955
UM. PUSH THE BUTTON, FRANK.

2242
01:35:59,988 --> 01:36:02,190
I HOPE JOEL PICKS MINE.
I DEVELOPED A PLAN

2243
01:36:02,223 --> 01:36:03,958
USING MUCILAGE
AS SWEET HONEY.

2244
01:36:03,992 --> 01:36:05,227
OH.

2245
01:36:05,260 --> 01:36:07,830
AND I'VE ALSO COME UP
WITH A THING FOR...

2246
01:36:07,863 --> 01:36:09,532
86-ING YOU, DOCTOR.

2247
01:36:09,565 --> 01:36:11,467
WELL, FRANK, THAT SHOWS
GREAT INITIATIVE.

2248
01:36:11,500 --> 01:36:14,937
86-- WOULD YOU
JUST PUSH THE BUTTON?
